{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:51:18.817054Z","id":"a3d0695a93efadfc5368992b5d4e4d1b040eff37d58ba1a6ce10d7be659a7bd0","body":{"detail":"release_owned_in (crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs) selects threads WHERE target_session_id = ?1, and Store::roster groups threads by target_session_id; crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs indexes neither. Both are full scans of threads: off the request hot paths (ends, the reaper, GET /api/agents) and cheap at today's sizes, but linear in all threads ever made.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1449},"end":{"line":1465},"content_hash":"ed1cb058eed0b38a9d4e07ae6c733539b4ca4c1c6388d6f7a4614ccf4b5c1af2"},"suggested_fix":"Add CREATE INDEX threads_by_target ON threads(target_session_id) WHERE target_session_id IS NOT NULL in the next migration.","summary":"Every session end and every roster read scans threads for target_session_id, which has no index","supersedes":"94285f387344cc5e2780991a92a1e777b279adc0774b19e43f4ed4acb5b8273e","tags":["perf","revisit:the next migration on this branch","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:51:18.817738Z","id":"f1deb673fd8027e9f0c220eabd61f66b8e9d49c60a03fb253d51c9d3cee7c468","body":{"detail":"An invite that expires unredeemed records nothing (audit spec section 6.13 lists only invite.create and invite.revoke). When release_unconnected then returns its person to a plain viewer it sets person = 0 and rights_json = NULL in the sweep or a revoke, so rights set by invite.create's rights or person.rights change with no person.rights event: the journal's last word on that person's rights is wrong.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2294},"end":{"line":2305},"content_hash":"3661554d9ec3b6ade08fbb453c62e14c05eacd1871b109bac087e43dd7492399"},"summary":"An invite's lapse is not recorded, and release_unconnected clears a person's flag and rights without an event","supersedes":"d1dcd98c6b93f08c945eb3f10844a11540fa51bfde1b0a84973137e587e7b5b1","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:51:18.821370Z","id":"cd01ae06abce3cd4bb62cf9f17e2e9f3a7db87448c07a0bc29f00beee390b6fc","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7e11f344","summary":"Fixed: Store::narrow_agent and Store::elevate_agent (crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs, set_agent_rights) call visibility_changed when they change sessions.narrow_json or elevate_json, and the routes PUT /api/agents/<handle>/narrow, PUT|DELETE /api/agents/<handle>/elevate use them. store::approvals::tests::every_visibility_change_bumps_the_generation_once now pins both (1 bump per change, 0 when unchanged or refused) and an agent's end clearing them (1 bump); it passes, as do api_people::elevation_exceeds_the_person_for_one_agent_only_until_its_session_ends and api_people::a_waiting_agent_takes_with_its_narrowed_rights.","supersedes":"d9fb0be608fcfff98d859883ebcfdddf71178581b63a4b7a356bfbf6b1237306","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:51:18.821945Z","id":"d555cc0452c3a3e491d57e1ee938b05d7578806a21bec19e4c0e3470fe61edfd","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:35cec880","summary":"Fixed: DELETE /api/agents/<handle> (crates/clax-server/src/routes/people.rs end_agent; the owner's browser ends any agent, a connected person's browser their own; the token alone is 403 browser_required) ends the session through Store::end_session_by_person, EndReason::Person, with Store::end_in's cleanup and the server's end announcements. api_people::a_person_or_the_owner_ends_one_agent_with_its_cleanup passes: ended_reason person, the question withdrawn, narrowing and elevation cleared, session.end recorded with reason person.","supersedes":"6b05cc8e718566c0bd2531739ada737d768414a3503be59600c51b6f4a1f12c1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:51:18.822546Z","id":"e1832cca50941329fb3b0293de9f90f47901ec3b30b9ea28f5b7025f7c0b2fd8","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"63cb4ceee8070bb7ca207c0e3a295f4f748b3a05d00992033aa59925b306cc98","summary":"The agent side of the suggested fix landed in 7e11f344 and 35cec880: every name of a viewer who is neither the owner nor a person reads '<name> (not connected)' in what an agent gets (feedback items and their author lines, batch senders, withheld authors, thread comments, resolved_by_name, artifact participants; crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs Connected::label, crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs mark_thread). A LAN viewer named 'Аlex' therefore reads 'Аlex (not connected)' to the owner's agents (api_people::unconnected_authors_are_marked_not_connected). The shell's flag for such a viewer is still open, for the People and thread-card UI.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/exec.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:40:09.188208Z","id":"8b4baa3000e4dfa58d592123aaf5bf0ab05d0c80dd91284842fa9b7065046d83","body":{"detail":"The pool runs a read inside a read (two reader leases) and a write inside a read (the writer is a separate connection; store::exec::tests::one_read_sees_one_snapshot relies on it). Single::hold panics on both, since the one connection is inside the outer read transaction. No store method nests today: store::tests::the_store_tests_pass_on_one_connection reran 455 store and journal tests on one connection, all passing. A future method that nests passes natively on the pool and panics on a Durable Object, caught only when a test reaches it through test_util::store. Single also has no read limit (no deadline check, since Instant panics on wasm32), and natively Store::call on one connection blocks the async caller's thread for the job.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":83},"end":{"line":188},"content_hash":"c1d80a8fcc61179cf2f1f246e489ac3e75b111001bbbc7608de14c0320e61c3e"},"summary":"One connection refuses nested jobs that the pool runs: a read or write started inside a read","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/site.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:45:13.519980Z","id":"71a2a628555762e3ed1e6fb9fc946b02b9e370fcd8c453c6cdadfbe61bf526ed","body":{"detail":"refile_threads (site.rs:1202) and snapshot_linking (live.rs:580, its content read at live.rs:600) drive content I/O with content::wait, which suits FsContent and MemContent only. create/publish/delete and the asset methods have async twins (Store::publish_version_async etc.); these paths still need theirs before a Cloudflare Artifacts backend can serve live pages.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1270},"end":{"line":1272},"content_hash":"ee880ff28152be532ea8679820403dc7943574423829f0b3f9bf3f73be3534e4"},"summary":"Re-filing and live snapshots have only synchronous entry points, so they cannot run on a ContentStore whose futures need an executor","tags":["content-store","wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:45:13.520078Z","id":"2b832d193dd7bf67f0c7c7c705baaa72e15fcdbd48c7b00cdfc70b21b7c71e8a","body":{"detail":"ArtifactLocks (content/mod.rs) serialise version writes within one process, so there the loser waits and then sees Conflict (concurrent_publishes_with_same_if_version_yield_one_winner). Across processes the loser's content write fails first; it is mapped to Conflict only when the artifact has already moved past the expected version. Nothing is corrupted (the loser removes nothing it did not write). The daemon is the only writer of versions today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1131},"end":{"line":1137},"content_hash":"6f2dbb750ce61f4294ee41c543d304be8fa47aa432433385b4d54e4435384279"},"summary":"Two processes publishing the same version at once: the loser gets the content store's AlreadyExists error, not Conflict, while the winner has not yet recorded it","tags":["content-store","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:45:13.520229Z","id":"8c05fce93257bb2ac3d7188ac15e9e386ac230a9065d20bc53288fe47cd2dbb8","body":{"detail":"feedback.rs:1266 and clax-server/src/feedback.rs snapshot_path name versions/<n>/index.html under the home; thread clips (Home::clip_path, site.rs refile) stay files; backfill.rs hashes version files and assets on disk; stray_version_dirs (artifacts.rs:498), stray_asset_temp_files (assets.rs:350), AssetRow::path and clax doctor's version_files check read the FsContent layout. All are correct only for a store whose content is the home's files (the default).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1266},"end":{"line":1271},"content_hash":"3ab35733ac7086103d6097ed3d991d1ab66a18fc698aed1a4e6932e10be6ad47"},"summary":"Several paths still use the home's files directly, outside ContentStore: snapshot paths handed to agents, clip images, the audit backfill, and doctor's stray scans","tags":["content-store","wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/site.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:04:51.606309Z","id":"898fd843fd1dce65e1e8ef7b182b871ca50ffb6057ced08b6dfa5a9e30ab18d5","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"71a2a628555762e3ed1e6fb9fc946b02b9e370fcd8c453c6cdadfbe61bf526ed","summary":"Two more sync-only content paths: Store::delete_zero_version_artifacts (store/artifacts.rs:575) and the purge of deleted artifacts' assets (store/assets.rs:374) call content::wait directly. Since 3c5715dc content::wait panics on wasm32 when a future is pending, so every such path fails loudly in a Worker instead of spinning.","tags":["content-store","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/site.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:05:25.519398Z","id":"5a05ec9054c297fee4f1c37b068416f74efc362d037f6b0a61c75684296e597f","body":{"detail":"refile_threads (site.rs:1202) and snapshot_linking (live.rs:580, its content read at live.rs:600) drive content I/O with content::wait, which suits FsContent and MemContent only. create/publish/delete and the asset methods have async twins (Store::publish_version_async etc.); these paths still need theirs before a Cloudflare Artifacts backend can serve live pages.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1270},"end":{"line":1270},"content_hash":"55c11ff69457a2067c86c8bd2c1c3b0acb55e62efe651c146eee0f15b08eb3bc"},"summary":"Re-filing and live snapshots have only synchronous entry points, so they cannot run on a ContentStore whose futures need an executor","supersedes":"71a2a628555762e3ed1e6fb9fc946b02b9e370fcd8c453c6cdadfbe61bf526ed","tags":["content-store","wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:18:31.972469Z","id":"c1b6119a426b5dd0b59d0169e3a0143d950db74d14921a8ac95dc66f53c74c43","body":{"detail":"Store::open_on's doc says the files under home are the host's, but the store reaches them only through std::fs, which on wasm32-unknown-unknown returns io::ErrorKind::Unsupported for every call. So a store opened on one connection in a Durable Object migrates, reads and records comments, but publishing a version (crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs:1073-1103, 1220), uploading an asset (store/assets.rs:172-177), writing a clip (store/threads.rs:720-723), site versions (store/site.rs:496-515, 711) and the live index read (store/live.rs:600) fail with an I/O error. No seam (as toolpath::segment::JournalFs is for the journal) lets a host supply those bytes. A fresh database's audit backfill opens no file (store/backfill.rs:834 runs per staged row), so open_on itself succeeds.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":188},"end":{"line":206},"content_hash":"e5006e5c673b9be19ae5e3b92134705f53dd44512141b81680901523efc80f7f"},"suggested_fix":"Put the home's file operations behind a trait the host implements (like JournalFs), or state in open_on's doc which operations a wasm host cannot run yet.","summary":"On wasm32 every store operation that writes or reads version, asset, clip or site bytes fails: they go through std::fs","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/exec.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:18:31.973222Z","id":"ca4e0940452b0a17e3c9de0ec97ac657e3be01cf13965d24c44896a3d0f1f87f","body":{"detail":"The target's panic strategy is abort: catch_unwind in Store::call's one-connection branch (crates/clax-core/src/store/exec.rs:878-883) returns nothing and Hold's Drop never runs, so Single::hold's refusal kills the wasm instance and every Durable Object it hosts. A static scan of clax-core's non-test code (every closure passed to with_read, with_tx, with_write, exec.read or exec.write, checked for calls to any function that transitively runs one; the scan finds the nested calls in store::exec::tests at exec.rs:1109, 1116, 1153) found no nested job, so none is reachable today. Single::hold could return an error (the jobs already return Result) so a future nesting fails one request instead.","kind":"comment","references":"8b4baa3000e4dfa58d592123aaf5bf0ab05d0c80dd91284842fa9b7065046d83","summary":"On wasm32-unknown-unknown panics abort, so a nested job's panic (or any panic in a job) traps the instance rather than failing one call","tags":["wasm","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:18:31.973455Z","id":"1dfa15273401de23d2cff6a3ede0019ed454b434dd5fb3cd8ba4470f4d3674c7","body":{"detail":"Measured on this machine (load average about 45): the clax-core lib tests take 12.4 s with --skip the_store_tests_pass_on_one_connection and 20.8 s with it, since the child runs 455 tests after the parent's. The threshold `passed > 300` passes with 455; a module dropped from the filter (or from test_util::store) loses its coverage on one connection without failing it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":637},"end":{"line":663},"content_hash":"075f0c3559d3b8aa8331c20e826e32a310d08f66e1a3cfc9a3751fcd0f651820"},"suggested_fix":"Compare `passed` against the count the same filter lists (`--list`) less the ignored ones, or pin the module set.","summary":"The one-connection rerun adds about 8 s to the clax-core unit suite, and its >300 threshold only catches an empty filter","tags":["wasm","gate-speed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:34:34.828469Z","id":"346934ac6486d35219631299974804ad12f76cc932b11ac5b49a03b3863ae6a7","body":{"detail":"ArtifactLocks (content/mod.rs) serialise version writes within one process, so there the loser waits and then sees Conflict (concurrent_publishes_with_same_if_version_yield_one_winner). Across processes the loser's content write fails first; it is mapped to Conflict only when the artifact has already moved past the expected version. Nothing is corrupted (the loser removes nothing it did not write). The daemon is the only writer of versions today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1132},"end":{"line":1138},"content_hash":"6f2dbb750ce61f4294ee41c543d304be8fa47aa432433385b4d54e4435384279"},"summary":"Two processes publishing the same version at once: the loser gets the content store's AlreadyExists error, not Conflict, while the winner has not yet recorded it","supersedes":"2b832d193dd7bf67f0c7c7c705baaa72e15fcdbd48c7b00cdfc70b21b7c71e8a","tags":["content-store","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:34:34.836865Z","id":"2b65f5930a4745777b415618c06886409eb54b36f6f6a04a97be021f4dbc0ea8","body":{"detail":"Store::version_meta resolves p.person, else the session's person, else the owner, before the content write; version_authors (artifacts.rs:817) resolves the row's person again inside the transaction. They agree today (tests a_version_write_names_its_publisher_agent_and_note), but a change to one rule that misses the other makes git's Clax-Publisher disagree with the row.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1255},"end":{"line":1300},"content_hash":"f66737ba4a9dd7d9da9cdce5fcc6307c341c28fc26dd5d18049c8140d75255da"},"suggested_fix":"Resolve the person once before the content lock and pass it to version_authors.","summary":"The publisher the content store is told and the one the version row records are resolved by separate code","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:12:31.494881Z","id":"7043fbd5259361e1f92b353a6bd44a8f46b28b1a9ce3a03f695c5d72ade8ae44","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:274f3832","summary":"Clips, re-filed clips, the live index read, site copies and the clip route go through ContentStore (put_clip/read_clip/delete_clip, async twins); the one-connection test stores keep content in MemContent and `cargo test -p clax-core --lib` passes (815 passed, including store::tests::the_store_tests_pass_on_one_connection, which reruns the store tests on open_on + MemContent). What still reads the home's files is local tooling, listed in the store module's Content section: the audit backfill of a home that predates the audit (nothing to do for a fresh database) and clax doctor's scans (empty where there is no filesystem).","supersedes":"c1b6119a426b5dd0b59d0169e3a0143d950db74d14921a8ac95dc66f53c74c43","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/exec.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:12:31.499424Z","id":"4206995cdeaf8f25e9d51e818c71f5ef700064a4aa42261b875a8885dbda09f3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5c7f2bef","summary":"Single::hold returns CoreError::NestedJob instead of panicking, so a nested job fails one call rather than aborting a wasm instance (ca4e0940); the pool still runs a read and a write inside a read. `cargo test -p clax-core --lib store::exec` passes one_connection_refuses_a_{write_inside_a_write,read_inside_a_write,write_inside_a_read,read_inside_a_read} and the_pool_runs_a_read_and_a_write_inside_a_read. The record's other points (no read limit on one connection, Store::call blocking the caller natively) are the documented design of Single and unchanged.","supersedes":"8b4baa3000e4dfa58d592123aaf5bf0ab05d0c80dd91284842fa9b7065046d83","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/site.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:12:31.504228Z","id":"f9337f039d13dfdc5df7a13a3021edca817ec2e2abea633445566306b9847cc8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:274f3832","summary":"refile_threads_async, the live snapshot path's async twins (ensure_live_page[_linking]_async, store_snapshot_async, snapshot_pending_async, create_live_thread_async, create_picked_thread_async), delete_zero_version_artifacts_async and delete_assets_of_deleted_artifacts_async (898fd843) await the content store; the synchronous methods run them through Store::block_on, which on wasm32 fails with WouldBlock instead of content::wait's panic. `cargo test -p clax-core --lib` passes (815 passed) on the pool and on open_on + MemContent.","supersedes":"5a05ec9054c297fee4f1c37b068416f74efc362d037f6b0a61c75684296e597f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:12:31.534122Z","id":"8e0636770ecf75c3b425476b78fac5f032d60e6efcf52458ede1ac6c34a271b9","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"8c05fce93257bb2ac3d7188ac15e9e386ac230a9065d20bc53288fe47cd2dbb8","summary":"Since 274f3832 clip images live in the content store and the paths handed to agents come from ContentStore::local_clip and local_file (None, so null or a 'no file on this machine' snapshot line, for a store that keeps no files). Still on the home's files, as local tooling documented in the store module's Content section: backfill.rs's hashing of old homes, stray_version_dirs, stray_asset_temp_files (both find nothing where read_dir is Unsupported), AssetRow::path and clax doctor's version_files check. Whether that is the intended end state is the owner's call.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:12:31.535722Z","id":"d7c84f95906d2377de1b3e9c02ee6fc5c9948e629dc9d2f6ccbe8ae010e9216b","body":{"detail":"Store::block_on on wasm32 runs the async twin with content::ready and returns WouldBlock when it is pending. A pending lock is the first await of every method, so that refusal changes nothing; but with a content store whose I/O needs an executor, the future can be pending after a write (a version written but not yet recorded or removed, a clip put before its thread's transaction), and dropping it skips the removal that follows: unrecorded bytes are left, never served, as after a crash. Untested natively, where block_on parks instead. Hosted callers with such a content store are meant to await the async twins (store module doc, Content).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":379},"end":{"line":389},"content_hash":"abb2bb9a6e4a16a8c5617be734cd3de766cc5dede4de30e91e452d75d69dbbc3"},"summary":"On wasm32 a synchronous method whose content I/O is pending drops its future part-way, so its cleanup does not run","tags":["content-store","wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:13:42.705615Z","id":"4f959f4e207e449f5acbd79d1eb0998f772719127b10103c939383b563d0bf3b","body":{"detail":"ArtifactLocks (content/mod.rs) serialise version writes within one process, so there the loser waits and then sees Conflict (concurrent_publishes_with_same_if_version_yield_one_winner). Across processes the loser's content write fails first; it is mapped to Conflict only when the artifact has already moved past the expected version. Nothing is corrupted (the loser removes nothing it did not write). The daemon is the only writer of versions today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1145},"end":{"line":1151},"content_hash":"6f2dbb750ce61f4294ee41c543d304be8fa47aa432433385b4d54e4435384279"},"summary":"Two processes publishing the same version at once: the loser gets the content store's AlreadyExists error, not Conflict, while the winner has not yet recorded it","supersedes":"2b832d193dd7bf67f0c7c7c705baaa72e15fcdbd48c7b00cdfc70b21b7c71e8a","tags":["content-store","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:13:42.709816Z","id":"e702794718214f13ceb5356d26bf88c31e042b04fef96665e1ad32b6288fa0a1","body":{"detail":"Measured on this machine (load average about 45): the clax-core lib tests take 12.4 s with --skip the_store_tests_pass_on_one_connection and 20.8 s with it, since the child runs 455 tests after the parent's. The threshold `passed > 300` passes with 455; a module dropped from the filter (or from test_util::store) loses its coverage on one connection without failing it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":750},"end":{"line":776},"content_hash":"b3bfd31319c95da4542d5ac7bd7f9fa165b3082f4e9534f5f055a9a24bdcbbee"},"suggested_fix":"Compare `passed` against the count the same filter lists (`--list`) less the ignored ones, or pin the module set.","summary":"The one-connection rerun adds about 8 s to the clax-core unit suite, and its >300 threshold only catches an empty filter","supersedes":"1dfa15273401de23d2cff6a3ede0019ed454b434dd5fb3cd8ba4470f4d3674c7","tags":["wasm","gate-speed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:58:52.343076Z","id":"261a17c29ec590370be21b92ab1287ebaba7155eb131f5466c6959b10b640205","body":{"detail":"Measured on this machine (load average about 45): the clax-core lib tests take 12.4 s with --skip the_store_tests_pass_on_one_connection and 20.8 s with it, since the child runs 455 tests after the parent's. The threshold `passed > 300` passes with 455; a module dropped from the filter (or from test_util::store) loses its coverage on one connection without failing it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":737},"end":{"line":763},"content_hash":"b3bfd31319c95da4542d5ac7bd7f9fa165b3082f4e9534f5f055a9a24bdcbbee"},"suggested_fix":"Compare `passed` against the count the same filter lists (`--list`) less the ignored ones, or pin the module set.","summary":"The one-connection rerun adds about 8 s to the clax-core unit suite, and its >300 threshold only catches an empty filter","supersedes":"e702794718214f13ceb5356d26bf88c31e042b04fef96665e1ad32b6288fa0a1","tags":["wasm","gate-speed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/exec.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:58:52.362517Z","id":"53321d53c63416d674f21c59c46cdadadeb8105aca2fbd3ecaca55cbb8f6b402","body":{"detail":"On the pool a started job runs to completion on its worker (call_on_worker), but inline the request future owns the job: a client gone or a timeout layer dropping the handler between ContentStore::write_version and the version transaction (store/artifacts.rs:1145) skips both the record and the remove_version that a failed transaction runs. FsContent and a create-only git backend then refuse version n as already present (artifacts.rs a_stray_version_directory_refuses_the_publish_and_records_nothing), so the artifact cannot be published again until the stray is removed (clax doctor natively; nothing on a Durable Object). A dropped clipped thread creation leaves an unreferenced clip; a dropped create_artifact a zero-version row. Removing an unrecorded n before writing it is safe only where one process writes the content (a Durable Object), not natively with several daemons (record 4f959f4e).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":910},"end":{"line":940},"content_hash":"68f7616e26a49e70da13008ab0b933c12adca6dea763e30fb402f4ea0f4602dd"},"suggested_fix":"On one connection, make an unrecorded version n replaceable: when write_version reports n present and the row still says n - 1, remove_version(n) under the content lock and write again; or run the job to completion detached from the request (ctx.waitUntil on a Worker).","summary":"A call_async job awaited inline (one connection, wasm32) stops wherever its future is dropped, so a cancelled publish can leave version n written but unrecorded, which refuses every later publish of n","tags":["content-store","wasm","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:58:52.363587Z","id":"41096f57f311a889782d90ef468545c5d7eedf754cdd0cfe84ea00fdb57758a1","body":{"detail":"Before 274f3832 the clip was written inside the thread transaction after the liveness, version and anchor checks. create_thread_inner now takes the content lock, checks liveness and puts the clip first; invalid_anchor, unknown_version and route checks fail later in the transaction and the clip is removed at threads.rs:926. A failed removal is only logged, leaving an unreferenced clip under clips/ (FsContent) or the clip-<thread> asset key. The content lock also makes a clipped thread wait for a publish of the same artifact in progress. Checking the version and anchor in a read before the put would keep refusals free of content I/O.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":814},"end":{"line":826},"content_hash":"da9c324b36bc56145b156ff2a9e326de501b4210777bf1a14697ddd9bfe8b870"},"summary":"A clipped thread now writes its clip before the version and anchor are checked, so every refused clipped request writes and deletes a clip","tags":["content-store","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:59:01.902437Z","id":"a7eadafc8b0d38c39cfbf317674211c0c678988758749fcf43a435d0935bf761","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e5f50927","summary":"A content store whose I/O needs an executor says so (ContentStore::needs_executor) and Store::block_on then fails with WouldBlock before running any of the twin, so no synchronous method starts content I/O it cannot finish; the server awaits the twins instead (Store::call_async, 5d7572d1). Evidence: store::tests::a_sync_method_on_a_content_store_that_needs_an_executor_writes_nothing (no row, no version left by a refused create_artifact) and api_hosted_content::content_routes_await_a_content_store_that_needs_an_executor pass; cargo test -p clax-core -p clax-server -p clax-mcp -p clax-cli -p clax-hooks: all ok (clax-core 816, clax-server integration 665). A store that needs an executor but does not declare it is still dropped part-way on wasm32.","supersedes":"d7c84f95906d2377de1b3e9c02ee6fc5c9948e629dc9d2f6ccbe8ae010e9216b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:19:06.766662Z","id":"b3c8598da46ce8a6053247f9a88f6e3aa31eefd37e034d7da75e9811bf3aa14c","body":{"detail":"The prototype names a guest 'Name (guest)' wherever Clax shows a name to an agent or an approver. Here a guest is a plain viewer row with viewers.guest = 1; feedback, comments_read and approval views show the bare name. Names cannot collide with members' or other guests' (check_guest_name), which limits impersonation.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":204},"end":{"line":220},"content_hash":"9d9c16dbf5d11129a5e54c8324a2a05213b0f474bfec7c320bcb50cb8610eb12"},"suggested_fix":"Mark guest authors in the agent-facing views and approval cards.","summary":"Guests are not labelled as guests to agents or approvers","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:19:06.766707Z","id":"bbb5cb2dc70ecca74d83af47147f17b80fa830bcdea094effac4a0cddad38c00","body":{"detail":"An agent token is a bearer grant (grants.bearer = 1, its cxa_ token in grant_tokens, kept out of credential_index so it never passes the signed Clax-Grant path). The endpoint resolves Authorization: Bearer cxa_... with bearer_grant, then Store::grant_caller for its person and rights, and builds Caller::PersonAgent; no route accepts the token yet.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":600},"end":{"line":604},"content_hash":"6118ad026448bf7342835eef06f09082a183699f7c1c18391bc4c90fa653e306"},"summary":"Store::bearer_grant is how the remote MCP endpoint should authenticate an agent token","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:19:06.766804Z","id":"1a769143fc51679984b3c9067cfcc62b06effe0f6a6fd8db39a16a82fb2eb1ee","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":741},"end":{"line":743},"content_hash":"7b8c2cfc4b3987a8e331333cde1cdfbfbebd527f736765bcd9ae5f2176add692"},"summary":"Migration 27 (hosted sign-in) takes the next number after multi-person's 26; it renumbers if another branch lands first","tags":["hosted","merge","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:55:24.322753Z","id":"2fbe03ca51dae73f9efbef87abc8425be7aee20f6f6d0f41dfec647a432f3bc6","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"1a769143fc51679984b3c9067cfcc62b06effe0f6a6fd8db39a16a82fb2eb1ee","summary":"Checked on 2026-10-13: every rust-* branch and multi-person end at 26, so 27 is the next free number on akesling/clax-artifacts; branch flutter-app (from main at 23) also writes a migration 27 (model use by apps) after its own 24 to 26, so whichever lands second renumbers.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:34:48.034299Z","id":"90c7d3726e0de58f0aaf99ca3998bfa1c3e317d15855b4c741a563d2e5e725df","body":{"detail":"Measured on this machine (load average about 45): the clax-core lib tests take 12.4 s with --skip the_store_tests_pass_on_one_connection and 20.8 s with it, since the child runs 455 tests after the parent's. The threshold `passed > 300` passes with 455; a module dropped from the filter (or from test_util::store) loses its coverage on one connection without failing it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":738},"end":{"line":764},"content_hash":"b3bfd31319c95da4542d5ac7bd7f9fa165b3082f4e9534f5f055a9a24bdcbbee"},"suggested_fix":"Compare `passed` against the count the same filter lists (`--list`) less the ignored ones, or pin the module set.","summary":"The one-connection rerun adds about 8 s to the clax-core unit suite, and its >300 threshold only catches an empty filter","supersedes":"261a17c29ec590370be21b92ab1287ebaba7155eb131f5466c6959b10b640205","tags":["wasm","gate-speed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:34:48.037152Z","id":"0e614128b64826eaab00451309991932957bb663b05042ae8ac631931b9fafd9","body":{"detail":"An agent token is a bearer grant (grants.bearer = 1, its cxa_ token in grant_tokens, kept out of credential_index so it never passes the signed Clax-Grant path). The endpoint resolves Authorization: Bearer cxa_... with bearer_grant, then Store::grant_caller for its person and rights, and builds Caller::PersonAgent; no route accepts the token yet.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":750},"end":{"line":754},"content_hash":"6118ad026448bf7342835eef06f09082a183699f7c1c18391bc4c90fa653e306"},"summary":"Store::bearer_grant is how the remote MCP endpoint should authenticate an agent token","supersedes":"bbb5cb2dc70ecca74d83af47147f17b80fa830bcdea094effac4a0cddad38c00","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/exec.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:34:48.147528Z","id":"a2acf3c9bf34ebbd25500f66c76d46afa8cebc99407a6eaefdc47c9a1fd4f420","body":{"detail":"Seen in Linux perf runs: a single commit held up by the disk. The writer runs WAL with SQLite's default synchronous=FULL, so every commit syncs the WAL, and the background PASSIVE checkpoint runs every CHECKPOINT_INTERVAL (2 s). Every delivery of a write waits on its commit, so one slow commit moves a whole cluster of deliveries (scripts/perf-clients.py:23-29 explains how the realtime gate copes).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":240},"end":{"line":263},"content_hash":"19a1b1cc49fe118705a9d82f6b9227495d66a06ae11378ed14f24dfb809e7ed5"},"suggested_fix":"Measure commit times on Linux with synchronous=NORMAL (durable across a crash of the process, not of the machine, in WAL mode) and with a different checkpoint cadence before choosing.","summary":"On Linux, store commits occasionally take 25 to 120 ms","supersedes":"afa8b528e7374450a20a041d28d29d75deae1d2b3e7525ce1dcdbfe7fecc4df4","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:34:48.150230Z","id":"6fc18f07aa6c3ebd48e18878251280d0f668dd747e95e1e7ac4d72b0d8fec5ec","body":{"detail":"approve_owner_on_connect is the single approval made without a browser (spec section 21 item 3, M15). It is bounded to the connect: once per grant, within OWNER_ANSWER_SECS (10 minutes) of the tokens' issue, never once the person has made or revoked any approval of the owner (409 owner_answered, so a revocation in People stands; 409 answer_closed after the window), replays refused by accept_t first. Only the continuation token says it, never the access token agents sign with (crates/clax-server/tests/api_grants.rs a_connected_machine_approves_the_owner_through_its_continuation), and clax connect refuses on an agent channel (crates/clax-cli/tests/connect.rs connect_refuses_on_an_agent_channel). What remains: a process of the person's that reads remote.json within those ten minutes, before clax connect answers, could answer yes for them; the person can revoke it in People, and that revocation is final. Tests: store::people::tests::connecting_records_the_persons_approval_of_the_owner_once, the_answer_about_the_owner_never_overrides_the_person.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1481},"end":{"line":1573},"content_hash":"d5ef04715b7251bf982fd51818c94f17a2b0b3b2dd3450f46854211db24ca24d"},"summary":"The person's approval of the owner is recorded without a browser once, at connect: an agent present then could answer for the person","supersedes":"ac87751d1a8a52942ba49cc5a0775c7d47efaf8f2af9b32724233d490ef2834b","tags":["security","spec:6.3","spec:21","M15","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:34:48.152665Z","id":"4421e240e7ba216331404390601263308957e2c7716b5612e5ad9493c5e2ee39","body":{"detail":"For flow invite the grant's events carry grant_id and person but not invite_id, so the journal cannot join invite.create to the grant made from it except by person and time; invites.grant_id holds the link only while the row lives.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1092},"end":{"line":1106},"content_hash":"a055d17fb6d13921d9565129c8f0b702f534ab8d657151596b97465c24004831"},"suggested_fix":"Add invite_id to grant.request (flow invite) and to audit spec section 6.13 and multi-person spec section 20.2.","summary":"An invite-flow grant.request and grant.approve do not name the invite they redeemed","supersedes":"cbc85f9a803d271af33bf349533f7dddba36c4b96f24ceee8fe1611fb86a5a72","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:18.645161Z","id":"b015c6c0e4559849b7470d22198b35516427504a504dcab639d3cec2e4fe4189","body":{"detail":"ArtifactLocks (content/mod.rs) serialise version writes within one process, so there the loser waits and then sees Conflict (concurrent_publishes_with_same_if_version_yield_one_winner). Across processes the loser's content write fails first; it is mapped to Conflict only when the artifact has already moved past the expected version. Nothing is corrupted (the loser removes nothing it did not write). The daemon is the only writer of versions today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1146},"end":{"line":1152},"content_hash":"6f2dbb750ce61f4294ee41c543d304be8fa47aa432433385b4d54e4435384279"},"summary":"Two processes publishing the same version at once: the loser gets the content store's AlreadyExists error, not Conflict, while the winner has not yet recorded it","supersedes":"346934ac6486d35219631299974804ad12f76cc932b11ac5b49a03b3863ae6a7","tags":["content-store","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:18.706317Z","id":"36bddcd84e96406ff3274174c297caebbcc360962f1235491e89c2dd459f163b","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate of 346934ac6486d35219631299974804ad12f76cc932b11ac5b49a03b3863ae6a7, the other head of the same record; that one is re-anchored to crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs:1146:1152.","supersedes":"4f959f4e207e449f5acbd79d1eb0998f772719127b10103c939383b563d0bf3b","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:18.712183Z","id":"fa223296dc6f9cac78ab5e1a3ba1bdce08eccbddb57e61d7a34981b23279f2d4","body":{"detail":"Store::version_meta resolves p.person, else the session's person, else the owner, before the content write; version_authors (artifacts.rs:817) resolves the row's person again inside the transaction. They agree today (tests a_version_write_names_its_publisher_agent_and_note), but a change to one rule that misses the other makes git's Clax-Publisher disagree with the row.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1269},"end":{"line":1314},"content_hash":"f66737ba4a9dd7d9da9cdce5fcc6307c341c28fc26dd5d18049c8140d75255da"},"suggested_fix":"Resolve the person once before the content lock and pass it to version_authors.","summary":"The publisher the content store is told and the one the version row records are resolved by separate code","supersedes":"2b65f5930a4745777b415618c06886409eb54b36f6f6a04a97be021f4dbc0ea8","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:19.080022Z","id":"f2d8e56e2cd87ead18a180f4cbdeeeca7b0f115248d5b8aab7918b5e38b27f27","body":{"detail":"At 8446429: upsert_viewer(lan, 'Аlex') with no owner name succeeds; set_owner_name('Alex') then succeeds too, and both names stand. An agent registering from repository web is named 'web' beside a LAN viewer 'wеb'. New people are covered (check_person_name refuses a look-alike held by an uninvited viewer). The owner usually names themselves late, on a first comment, so pre-squatting is the likely order.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":64},"end":{"line":86},"content_hash":"1de938dd9fb1b372a1c0a4ff8a6d6621a8555d5847b284aed129ce694034651a"},"suggested_fix":"Mark it where names are shown: an unconnected viewer whose name looks like a protected name is flagged in the shell and in agent author lines (with spec section 9.6's '(not connected)', Task 17), rather than refusing the owner their own name.","summary":"The look-alike check runs only when the later name is set: a LAN viewer who took 'Аlex' before the owner named themselves 'Alex', or 'wеb' before an agent web went live, keeps it","supersedes":"63cb4ceee8070bb7ca207c0e3a295f4f748b3a05d00992033aa59925b306cc98","tags":["review","spec:9.6","revisit:task-17","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:19.083499Z","id":"e73ad5029989682362da4c71c44428d6e3106669fa40973a0101cb2c1f15b573","body":{"detail":"An invite that expires unredeemed records nothing (audit spec section 6.13 lists only invite.create and invite.revoke). When release_unconnected then returns its person to a plain viewer it sets person = 0 and rights_json = NULL in the sweep or a revoke, so rights set by invite.create's rights or person.rights change with no person.rights event: the journal's last word on that person's rights is wrong.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2302},"end":{"line":2313},"content_hash":"2ddd5903658167c04514801afdde1244c244a163cfb84079293eb4ae9676bcf3"},"summary":"An invite's lapse is not recorded, and release_unconnected clears a person's flag and rights without an event","supersedes":"f1deb673fd8027e9f0c220eabd61f66b8e9d49c60a03fb253d51c9d3cee7c468","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:19.086944Z","id":"0f6047ff4f10f7b1559a10e80ce283e75a0b77379e45b1cdffaef34bd26d1260","body":{"detail":"feedback.rs:1266 and clax-server/src/feedback.rs snapshot_path name versions/<n>/index.html under the home; thread clips (Home::clip_path, site.rs refile) stay files; backfill.rs hashes version files and assets on disk; stray_version_dirs (artifacts.rs:498), stray_asset_temp_files (assets.rs:350), AssetRow::path and clax doctor's version_files check read the FsContent layout. All are correct only for a store whose content is the home's files (the default).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1268},"end":{"line":1271},"content_hash":"62b8545b696db1906dc4334096cfb785b6a74d6d33e1d63932130cda23a2a0d9"},"summary":"Several paths still use the home's files directly, outside ContentStore: snapshot paths handed to agents, clip images, the audit backfill, and doctor's stray scans","supersedes":"8c05fce93257bb2ac3d7188ac15e9e386ac230a9065d20bc53288fe47cd2dbb8","tags":["content-store","wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:52:45.698233Z","id":"0f03209fab22a7d4d6c0ef2c586133261710f0c807456f6175bd0638a04d1eaf","body":{"detail":"An invite that expires unredeemed records nothing (audit spec section 6.13 lists only invite.create and invite.revoke). When release_unconnected then returns its person to a plain viewer it sets person = 0 and rights_json = NULL in the sweep or a revoke, so rights set by invite.create's rights or person.rights change with no person.rights event: the journal's last word on that person's rights is wrong.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2333},"end":{"line":2344},"content_hash":"3661554d9ec3b6ade08fbb453c62e14c05eacd1871b109bac087e43dd7492399"},"summary":"An invite's lapse is not recorded, and release_unconnected clears a person's flag and rights without an event","supersedes":"f1deb673fd8027e9f0c220eabd61f66b8e9d49c60a03fb253d51c9d3cee7c468","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:46:07.714394Z","id":"74144e335949ccfd8af4519de32993625199510204043e973648057bb088dce5","body":{"detail":"An invite that expires unredeemed records nothing (audit spec section 6.13 lists only invite.create and invite.revoke). When release_unconnected then returns its person to a plain viewer it sets person = 0 and rights_json = NULL in the sweep or a revoke, so rights set by invite.create's rights or person.rights change with no person.rights event: the journal's last word on that person's rights is wrong.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2341},"end":{"line":2352},"content_hash":"2ddd5903658167c04514801afdde1244c244a163cfb84079293eb4ae9676bcf3"},"summary":"An invite's lapse is not recorded, and release_unconnected clears a person's flag and rights without an event","supersedes":"e73ad5029989682362da4c71c44428d6e3106669fa40973a0101cb2c1f15b573","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:19:33.546466Z","id":"8e257b9da7500461ad5b445cbff9f22886089844cc9d2aefee32ab89b237a0af","body":{"detail":"routes/sessions.rs register calls end_bearer_sessions_beyond(gid, BEARER_SESSION_CAP - 1) and then register_session_restoring in separate transactions; concurrent initializes of one token can each count the same live set. The next registration trims it back. Accepted as a bound on build-up, not an exact limit.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1082},"end":{"line":1111},"content_hash":"8ef33f44d4f1cafe046fb180228494b8e47afb2f14aca6b7df5ba45bf9f7a4bc"},"summary":"Two agent-token registrations at once can each leave room for themselves, so a token briefly holds more than BEARER_SESSION_CAP live sessions","tags":["hosted","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:20:35.500669Z","id":"9a4f58ee20fb7e58f8a01519feb88a7b8800595d47aa7041438deb69cbb79601","body":{"detail":"release_owned_in (crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs) selects threads WHERE target_session_id = ?1, and Store::roster groups threads by target_session_id; crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs indexes neither. Both are full scans of threads: off the request hot paths (ends, the reaper, GET /api/agents) and cheap at today's sizes, but linear in all threads ever made.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1490},"end":{"line":1506},"content_hash":"ed1cb058eed0b38a9d4e07ae6c733539b4ca4c1c6388d6f7a4614ccf4b5c1af2"},"suggested_fix":"Add CREATE INDEX threads_by_target ON threads(target_session_id) WHERE target_session_id IS NOT NULL in the next migration.","summary":"Every session end and every roster read scans threads for target_session_id, which has no index","supersedes":"a3d0695a93efadfc5368992b5d4e4d1b040eff37d58ba1a6ce10d7be659a7bd0","tags":["perf","revisit:the next migration on this branch","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/forks.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:35:32.219721Z","id":"542e3136e6a50ba64d7f4028efb69c1bb2158332adf39407b1d7f7103cc3a19f","body":{"detail":"Store::fork_artifact_async copies version files only (ContentStore::fork). Assets are per artifact (content/mod.rs AssetKey.artifact) and not in git. A fork's page still points at the source's asset URLs: they break once the source is deleted (its assets go with it), and on a hosted daemon a reader of the fork who may not read the source is not handed the source's asset keys (hosted.rs asset_key). The hosted prototype (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts initFork) does not copy assets either.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":13},"end":{"line":14},"content_hash":"f58f8d887d87cc58a86164f841f02fa75222496da147750b95e672cbb1a45d68"},"suggested_fix":"Copy the source's assets into the fork under new IDs and rewrite their URLs in the copied files, or keep a fork's reads of the source's assets keyed to the fork.","summary":"A fork copies no assets, so a forked page that references the source's /_blob/<asset ID> URLs depends on the source's assets","tags":["forks","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/forks.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:35:32.220233Z","id":"859ed4c348f0d1f3a7f71f863ea1232a631803da1cbe0cf29269da44aee7c380","body":{"detail":"hosted/src/do/artifact.ts keeps a forks table on the original and broadcasts a fork event; spec 2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design H11 says the original lists its forks. Here only the fork records its source (artifacts.forked_from_id); listing a source's forks is a query on that column (no index yet) plus a filtered view.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":4},"content_hash":"34369e2e065901c8e4d6445f8a060034bbe43fae44330b7c5bc627d18c54d5b4"},"summary":"The source does not list its forks (the hosted prototype's Forks (n) and fork live events)","tags":["forks","revisit:when the artifact view gets a forks list","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:48:56.206061Z","id":"a768d0cd8dea941b68daa0d7c3057c13b04d011b670dc1d3764a2f91a385a35a","body":{"detail":"Measured on this machine (load average about 45): the clax-core lib tests take 12.4 s with --skip the_store_tests_pass_on_one_connection and 20.8 s with it, since the child runs 455 tests after the parent's. The threshold `passed > 300` passes with 455; a module dropped from the filter (or from test_util::store) loses its coverage on one connection without failing it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":739},"end":{"line":765},"content_hash":"b3bfd31319c95da4542d5ac7bd7f9fa165b3082f4e9534f5f055a9a24bdcbbee"},"suggested_fix":"Compare `passed` against the count the same filter lists (`--list`) less the ignored ones, or pin the module set.","summary":"The one-connection rerun adds about 8 s to the clax-core unit suite, and its >300 threshold only catches an empty filter","supersedes":"90c7d3726e0de58f0aaf99ca3998bfa1c3e317d15855b4c741a563d2e5e725df","tags":["wasm","gate-speed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:48:56.209542Z","id":"2ac8a07f9c4c66299aeeedf0179a48661d95b450b9c3a1550f33a73788d3db83","body":{"detail":"ArtifactLocks (content/mod.rs) serialise version writes within one process, so there the loser waits and then sees Conflict (concurrent_publishes_with_same_if_version_yield_one_winner). Across processes the loser's content write fails first; it is mapped to Conflict only when the artifact has already moved past the expected version. Nothing is corrupted (the loser removes nothing it did not write). The daemon is the only writer of versions today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1156},"end":{"line":1162},"content_hash":"6f2dbb750ce61f4294ee41c543d304be8fa47aa432433385b4d54e4435384279"},"summary":"Two processes publishing the same version at once: the loser gets the content store's AlreadyExists error, not Conflict, while the winner has not yet recorded it","supersedes":"b015c6c0e4559849b7470d22198b35516427504a504dcab639d3cec2e4fe4189","tags":["content-store","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:48:56.258951Z","id":"28379c61fa3cef7b6976b9ecb1af60533e6d601d7dad5260432a0c6b5de53030","body":{"detail":"Store::publisher_meta (through version_meta) resolves the person given, else the session's person, else the owner, before the content write; version_authors resolves the row's person again inside the transaction, and Store::fork_artifact_async (store/forks.rs, its `creator`) a third time. They agree today (tests a_version_write_names_its_publisher_agent_and_note, clax-content-git tests/store_fork.rs), but a change to one rule that misses the others makes git's Clax-Publisher disagree with the row.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1278},"end":{"line":1335},"content_hash":"2191ee2e4691438f937db6b89ac781fab05a30be0df704af5a2611bad91668d6"},"suggested_fix":"Resolve the person once before the content lock and pass it to version_authors and the fork's insert.","summary":"The publisher the content store is told and the one the version row records are resolved by separate code","supersedes":"fa223296dc6f9cac78ab5e1a3ba1bdce08eccbddb57e61d7a34981b23279f2d4","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/forks.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:12:08.216157Z","id":"cbd485707ad6f3d089924d54ac70eb02f83319f33ad9e30830f5282dd7fda19c","body":{"detail":"Store::fork_artifact_async copies version files only (ContentStore::fork). Pages reference assets by ID alone: the upload answers /_blob/<asset ID> (a hosted daemon's /_blob/<asset ID>?k=<key>, keyed by the asset ID only, hosted.rs asset_url), and routes/assets.rs blob looks the row up by ID (Store::get_asset). So the fork's page keeps loading the source's assets for every reader of the fork, a hosted one too (the key is in the page's bytes), until the source is deleted (delete_artifact_async removes its content, assets included) or its owner deletes that asset; the fork's own asset list (GET /api/artifacts/<fork>/assets) is empty. Copying under the same IDs is impossible: assets.id is the table's primary key (migration 1) and /_blob/<id> names no artifact. Copying under new IDs means rewriting the copied files' bytes, which changes the hashes and authors' bytes the fork keeps (content_sha256 equal to the source version's, crates/clax-core/src/store/forks.rs tests) and misses URLs a page builds in script. The hosted prototype has no assets.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":13},"end":{"line":14},"content_hash":"f58f8d887d87cc58a86164f841f02fa75222496da147750b95e672cbb1a45d68"},"suggested_fix":"Decide: (a) key assets by (artifact_id, id) with /_blob/<id> resolved within the page's artifact (a migration and a route that knows its artifact), then copy rows and bytes under the same IDs into the fork; (b) keep a deleted artifact's asset bytes while a live fork names it as its source; or (c) accept, and say in docs/contract.md's fork section that assets stay the source's.","summary":"A fork copies no assets, so a forked page's /_blob/<asset ID> URLs stay the source's and break when the source or that asset is deleted","supersedes":"542e3136e6a50ba64d7f4028efb69c1bb2158332adf39407b1d7f7103cc3a19f","tags":["forks","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:20.998214Z","id":"6eba3e92b317e95b653e14bf055bffbe61bfffcbda0cc6a32a79407ba06ee437","body":{"detail":"An agent token is a bearer grant (grants.bearer = 1, its cxa_ token in grant_tokens, kept out of credential_index so it never passes the signed Clax-Grant path). The endpoint resolves Authorization: Bearer cxa_... with bearer_grant, then Store::grant_caller for its person and rights, and builds Caller::PersonAgent; no route accepts the token yet.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":756},"end":{"line":760},"content_hash":"6118ad026448bf7342835eef06f09082a183699f7c1c18391bc4c90fa653e306"},"summary":"Store::bearer_grant is how the remote MCP endpoint should authenticate an agent token","supersedes":"0e614128b64826eaab00451309991932957bb663b05042ae8ac631931b9fafd9","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/pushes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:00:41.053281Z","id":"7b2635b3540db784921b8484ab9a997d1877ec21cbd1d15ad78a1c06f20fd0e3","body":{"detail":"Only the stand-in's RepoDO knows who pushed (the token's Holder, crates/clax-worker/src/repos/tokens.rs) and passes it to the reconcile it starts once the push is applied (crates/clax-worker/src/repos/worker.rs RepoDO::record_push). The reconcile every publish runs first (Store::write_version_then_async, crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs) and the Artifacts queue consumer (crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs queue) pass Pusher::default(), so a publish that takes the content lock between a push landing and RepoDO's call, or any push to Cloudflare Artifacts (whose pushed event, as clax_git::events parses it, names no pusher and whose tokens Artifacts checks itself), records the commits as the owner's: the owner becomes publisher and author of the changed files. Fix: keep the pusher with the pushed head (a ledger row per push, keyed by repository and new main commit) and let every reconcile read it; for Artifacts, map the event's token or actor to the ledger's Holder once its schema is known.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":125},"end":{"line":148},"content_hash":"76b68a54cea0e2aa9de9352d55ecfc115a80710a3da99148d77be0cf73965529"},"summary":"A pushed commit recorded by any reconcile but the push's own is credited to the owner, not the pusher","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/pushes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:00:41.053368Z","id":"efbb5619f10a7f124c292266382656aee2149adcd51ffd03cc65883fc92e1419","body":{"detail":"record_push credits whoever the token names; the push right was checked only when the token was minted (crates/clax-worker/src/repos/tokens.rs, Holder), so a person whose rights were narrowed or who was revoked while a token of theirs lived still has their push recorded as theirs. The hosted prototype also revokes, before recording, every agent git token whose person may not see the new versions' authors (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts recordPushes, revokeBlindBefore), since a clone cannot be filtered; nothing here does. Fix: on revoke_person and on rights narrowing, revoke that person's repository tokens; before recording, revoke the read tokens of agents who may not see the pusher.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":151},"end":{"line":151},"content_hash":"a4506805627bc7fc3f58e3b5d91eaf4e766aef268224742ab820148a0d91ff20"},"summary":"A pushed version neither rechecks the pusher's rights nor revokes agents' read tokens that may not see its authors","tags":["security","status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:00:41.053503Z","id":"dbc9b276c45085bcbfe861d2b1e4b283ad6b8743c29619b0a38cf030aa444eda","body":{"detail":"A push to Cloudflare Artifacts whose pushed event is lost, late or never delivered (no subscription, locally: the queue is simulated and receives none, crates/clax-worker/wrangler.jsonc queues) stays unrecorded until the next publish of the artifact, so viewers see the older version meanwhile. The prototype also reconciles lazily on reads, at most every RECONCILE_EVERY_MS (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts reconcileLazily). Fix: reconcile from the artifact read routes when main has moved past the current version's commit, rate-limited per artifact.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1122},"end":{"line":1132},"content_hash":"96be8028b3169b1e4cabbeed81457db6d73d69b3c4e2d1832869e81f65d7a148"},"summary":"Pushed commits are recorded on a push, an Artifacts event or a publish, but not when an artifact is read","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:33:40.341727Z","id":"db8e547c1f42d76824e5f88f42bff6e50d6134ff62f023eabab5478b0e328e5a","body":{"detail":"Measured on this machine (load average about 45): the clax-core lib tests take 12.4 s with --skip the_store_tests_pass_on_one_connection and 20.8 s with it, since the child runs 455 tests after the parent's. The threshold `passed > 300` passes with 455; a module dropped from the filter (or from test_util::store) loses its coverage on one connection without failing it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":747},"end":{"line":773},"content_hash":"b3bfd31319c95da4542d5ac7bd7f9fa165b3082f4e9534f5f055a9a24bdcbbee"},"suggested_fix":"Compare `passed` against the count the same filter lists (`--list`) less the ignored ones, or pin the module set.","summary":"The one-connection rerun adds about 8 s to the clax-core unit suite, and its >300 threshold only catches an empty filter","supersedes":"90c7d3726e0de58f0aaf99ca3998bfa1c3e317d15855b4c741a563d2e5e725df","tags":["wasm","gate-speed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:33:40.346002Z","id":"fc163ac86b24034a99b950c26b52c00bcf554fb67c8f3bd4f222b016f4391e8d","body":{"detail":"Store::version_meta resolves p.person, else the session's person, else the owner, before the content write; version_authors (artifacts.rs:817) resolves the row's person again inside the transaction. They agree today (tests a_version_write_names_its_publisher_agent_and_note), but a change to one rule that misses the other makes git's Clax-Publisher disagree with the row.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1361},"end":{"line":1406},"content_hash":"f66737ba4a9dd7d9da9cdce5fcc6307c341c28fc26dd5d18049c8140d75255da"},"suggested_fix":"Resolve the person once before the content lock and pass it to version_authors.","summary":"The publisher the content store is told and the one the version row records are resolved by separate code","supersedes":"fa223296dc6f9cac78ab5e1a3ba1bdce08eccbddb57e61d7a34981b23279f2d4","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:33:40.358744Z","id":"52efc8cf1dcb2f90828a3d760d44019837906384769b412643c383e800109719","body":{"detail":"ArtifactLocks (content/mod.rs) serialise version writes within one process, so there the loser waits and then sees Conflict (concurrent_publishes_with_same_if_version_yield_one_winner). Across processes the loser's content write fails first; it is mapped to Conflict only when the artifact has already moved past the expected version. Nothing is corrupted (the loser removes nothing it did not write). The daemon is the only writer of versions today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1229},"end":{"line":1238},"content_hash":"4904f3490dcc2f9f92baa1aaa49032071480c9eaf3740604defd236f4657e508"},"summary":"Two processes publishing the same version at once: the loser gets the content store's AlreadyExists error, not Conflict, while the winner has not yet recorded it","supersedes":"b015c6c0e4559849b7470d22198b35516427504a504dcab639d3cec2e4fe4189","tags":["content-store","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:33:40.369843Z","id":"6eb29bd424b71eeb4396d78e90ca369e00b87fb4bf6f6799b2907f999f5ac5d8","body":{"detail":"A push to Cloudflare Artifacts whose pushed event is lost, late or never delivered (no subscription, locally: the queue is simulated and receives none, crates/clax-worker/wrangler.jsonc queues) stays unrecorded until the next publish of the artifact, so viewers see the older version meanwhile. The prototype also reconciles lazily on reads, at most every RECONCILE_EVERY_MS (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts reconcileLazily). Fix: reconcile from the artifact read routes when main has moved past the current version's commit, rate-limited per artifact.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1122},"end":{"line":1142},"content_hash":"5aea8e38f17328396770571e0e3d99efadde21ae073543404d5fa024591c706c"},"summary":"Pushed commits are recorded on a push, an Artifacts event or a publish, but not when an artifact is read","supersedes":"dbc9b276c45085bcbfe861d2b1e4b283ad6b8743c29619b0a38cf030aa444eda","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/pushes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:33:40.393672Z","id":"778d089f83eef9647cccdbfa8abfe27c72e1f53e2afc39d15be6519d25de79d3","body":{"detail":"Pushes to Artifacts' own git endpoint never pass RepoDO, so RepoDO's ledger has no git_pushes row for their commits (crates/clax-worker/src/repos/db.rs record_push, written only by tokens::note_push from RepoDO's /git/ route), and the queue consumer reconciles with Pusher::default() (crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs queue). pushers_of then gives every such commit the fallback, the owner: the owner becomes the version's publisher and the author of its changed files, and Store::standing allows it, whoever held the Artifacts token. clax_git::events::event_repo reads only the repository's name; the event's documented payload (ref, before, after, commits; crates/clax-git/src/events.rs:21-25) names no token or actor that is known here. Fix: once the pushed event's schema names the token (Artifacts tokens are entered in git_tokens with hash NULL by tokens::mint) or the actor, have the queue consumer enter a git_pushes row for the event's after commit with that token's holder before it asks the instance to reconcile.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":416},"end":{"line":428},"content_hash":"38cc39ea7d33382de52e273c944e0c51a787210b5289531ea9b52b303e7a18bd"},"summary":"A push straight to Cloudflare Artifacts is credited to the owner and passes the rights recheck as the owner","tags":["security","revisit:Cloudflare Artifacts' pushed-event schema is known","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/pushes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:33:40.393764Z","id":"e820a816ed32bc46f1ccfea44a27cde49e9b02191cbaf3c876a1591b92a31e66","body":{"detail":"A refused commit stays on main (it is neither recorded nor tagged), and the stand-in refuses non-fast-forward pushes (clax-git ServeOptions deny_non_fast_forwards), so the only way past it is a push over it by someone who may publish. That commit is recorded with every file changed since the newest version authored by its pusher (record_push), so a refused or revoked person's changes reach other people's agents as, say, the owner's under the visibility filter; its note names the refused commits. The hosted prototype credits a changed blob to every author it already had in history (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts recordPushes, blobAuthors); here a refused commit's blobs have no recorded author. Fix: credit paths whose blob equals one in a refused commit to that commit's pusher as well, or refuse the commit over it until those paths match the newest version.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":141},"end":{"line":149},"content_hash":"8c34d7356614154fc05784b37020214d4aab0dc8a7a3271396030174350c9b1e"},"summary":"A commit recorded over refused commits carries their changes as its own pusher's words","tags":["security","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/pushes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:35:32.420834Z","id":"84a81797673b795a183b9cb9a0436a9fb2750e51b8c6e07af4ea744053570567","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9ddc2f13","summary":"Every reconcile now reads each pushed commit's pusher from RepoDO's ledger (git_pushes, entered by tokens::note_push before RepoDO answers anything else; served through DoLedger and ContentStore::pushers, cdec4be3 and 9ddc2f13). cargo test -p clax-content-git --test integration pushes: every_reconcile_credits_a_pushed_commit_to_whoever_pushed_it ok; (cd crates/clax-worker && cargo test): a_push_is_its_token_holders_whichever_reconcile_records_it_and_blind_agents_lose_their_tokens ok (a real git push with Rae's token, recorded by the publish's lazy reconcile, is Rae's). Pushes straight to Cloudflare Artifacts stay the owner's: concern 778d089f.","supersedes":"7b2635b3540db784921b8484ab9a997d1877ec21cbd1d15ad78a1c06f20fd0e3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/pushes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:35:32.425429Z","id":"c27f7bf1becee049bbb9fe24a6c8ccb2ece8f7ffa59f11438d7a9214b143b6bd","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:cdec4be3","summary":"Store::standing rechecks each pushed commit's pusher when it is recorded (person not revoked with update at the artifact; agent session live with its effective rights; else version.push_refused, not tagged, publish 409 push_refused), and revoke_blind_tokens revokes agents' repository tokens whose person may not see the new version's authors before it is recorded, as hosted/src/do/artifact.ts revokeBlindBefore does. cargo test -p clax-content-git --test integration pushes: 9 passed, among them a_push_by_someone_who_may_no_longer_publish_is_not_recorded_and_is_audited, an_agents_push_is_rechecked_against_its_rights_as_they_are_when_recorded, an_agents_token_that_may_not_see_a_pushed_version_is_revoked_before_it_is_recorded; cargo test -p clax-server --test integration api_pushes: 2 passed. Revoking holders' tokens on a rights change is left open: concern 11f3b0bc.","supersedes":"efbb5619f10a7f124c292266382656aee2149adcd51ffd03cc65883fc92e1419","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:12:33.139085Z","id":"15cfc12392187582eafefaa2433561413b0d6d30262047c597fd83b3a607e707","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"6eb29bd424b71eeb4396d78e90ca369e00b87fb4bf6f6799b2907f999f5ac5d8","summary":"The hosted/ files this record cites were removed in 60298c1d (the TypeScript prototype's retirement); read one at its parent with git show 60298c1d^:hosted/<path>","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/forks.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:12:33.139172Z","id":"5354b30fdf2274baca45cbadc7b3ecb203177bd6d5b5e6940c7c956b1a9ecc0b","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"859ed4c348f0d1f3a7f71f863ea1232a631803da1cbe0cf29269da44aee7c380","summary":"The hosted/ files this record cites were removed in 60298c1d (the TypeScript prototype's retirement); read one at its parent with git show 60298c1d^:hosted/<path>","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/pushes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:12:33.139254Z","id":"389610aff115f79a37c981ecb1a59a953d56c3332859787c225f2a7028bf0734","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"e820a816ed32bc46f1ccfea44a27cde49e9b02191cbaf3c876a1591b92a31e66","summary":"The hosted/ files this record cites were removed in 60298c1d (the TypeScript prototype's retirement); read one at its parent with git show 60298c1d^:hosted/<path>","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/pushes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:58:01.477582Z","id":"21edf3242c460fc3d1581dd84094e5fa5b4c5d69c6b105002bfc209d3e20d1c2","body":{"detail":"Pushes to Artifacts' own git endpoint never pass RepoDO, so RepoDO's ledger has no git_pushes row for their commits (crates/clax-worker/src/repos/db.rs record_push, written only by tokens::note_push from RepoDO's /git/ route), and the queue consumer reconciles with Pusher::default() (crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs queue). pushers_of then gives every such commit the fallback, the owner: the owner becomes the version's publisher and the author of its changed files, and Store::standing allows it, whoever held the Artifacts token. clax_git::events::event_repo reads only the repository's name; the event's documented payload (ref, before, after, commits; crates/clax-git/src/events.rs:21-25) names no token or actor that is known here. Fix: once the pushed event's schema names the token (Artifacts tokens are entered in git_tokens with hash NULL by tokens::mint) or the actor, have the queue consumer enter a git_pushes row for the event's after commit with that token's holder before it asks the instance to reconcile.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":421},"end":{"line":433},"content_hash":"38cc39ea7d33382de52e273c944e0c51a787210b5289531ea9b52b303e7a18bd"},"summary":"A push straight to Cloudflare Artifacts is credited to the owner and passes the rights recheck as the owner","supersedes":"778d089f83eef9647cccdbfa8abfe27c72e1f53e2afc39d15be6519d25de79d3","tags":["security","revisit:Cloudflare Artifacts' pushed-event schema is known","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:58:01.484713Z","id":"7db0f8bc4b896591df4384e1316204c757ab307eda378654d2022a905b6d039f","body":{"detail":"record_version_locked calls revoke_blind_tokens with the publisher for VersionStep::Write when expected > 0, which is ContentStore::repo_tokens (DoLedger: POST token/live to RepoDO) even when no token is held. That is one subrequest on every publish's path (time to usable), plus a Visibility per agent token. Skipping needs to know no agent token is live without asking RepoDO, for example a held-token count the instance keeps from mint and revoke answers.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1224},"end":{"line":1246},"content_hash":"a791ca23cf8107bccfd6950065f7527248cabd7d27c31964f2e4f1eeeeb672b6"},"summary":"Every publish of an existing artifact asks the push ledger for the repository's tokens before its commit: on the Worker one RepoDO call per publish","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:02:11.811716Z","id":"207b96651905997d3bcb50bb814b8b286468087737dd183ee1025e83d97767ef","body":{"detail":"Store::approves_first runs inside views_and_senders (crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs), which serves thread lists, every thread event and agents' thread reads (which then drop the field). With people present it reads the live sessions' persons and builds Visibility::for_reader for each, per call. Fine for a few people; no perf gate measures it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1585},"end":{"line":1625},"content_hash":"c3f2bd4bb7734900c24a41be13266490f98fa1d92159b2dcd6069f41271516b8"},"suggested_fix":"Compute it only for browser views (not agents' reads and deliveries), or cache per (generation, person) as owner_sees_all does.","summary":"Every thread view build with people present builds one Visibility per person with a live agent","tags":["task:22","perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:13:39.972409Z","id":"3d7ec763a78d801913bbb5d448477ace6c0baf05ff69202a6d1d8615548c9c42","body":{"detail":"Failure: a home at migration 25 where a person's agent asked a question (a dev home run on this branch) keeps that question's item with recipient NULL after 26, so it sits in the owner's inbox and crates/clax-server/src/inbox.rs render reads its question unscoped (st.question), showing the person's question and answers to the owner, while the person never gets the item. Main's homes hold no person sessions, so they are unaffected. Accepted: migrations 24-26 are unmerged (spec M27), so only a dev home run on this branch can hold such items; questions themselves get their person from their session (questions.person is filled in by the migration).","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":709},"end":{"line":712},"content_hash":"4611fbab17797ab78415d9f71e991c5b174e8ca88f75ff87d6685c7d8474fc79"},"summary":"Migration 26 leaves every existing inbox item the owner's, including question and finished items a connected person's agent made at schema 24-25","supersedes":"9faaa3589a643aa6554297355fee029411fa1b7f6868e33b55b19998f25b518c","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:13:39.976371Z","id":"b194108f740df12f0ce0f12d339d1c0dc26f8db78c69ff2b2b2ee3922732aeeb","body":{"detail":"An invite that expires unredeemed records nothing (audit spec section 6.13 lists only invite.create and invite.revoke). When release_unconnected then returns its person to a plain viewer it sets person = 0 and rights_json = NULL in the sweep or a revoke, so rights set by invite.create's rights or person.rights change with no person.rights event: the journal's last word on that person's rights is wrong.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2296},"end":{"line":2307},"content_hash":"3661554d9ec3b6ade08fbb453c62e14c05eacd1871b109bac087e43dd7492399"},"summary":"An invite's lapse is not recorded, and release_unconnected clears a person's flag and rights without an event","supersedes":"f1deb673fd8027e9f0c220eabd61f66b8e9d49c60a03fb253d51c9d3cee7c468","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:13:39.978681Z","id":"adfdd0fa9a4441e78eb88302cb291b32d5c045372647dc73d548363a18b74dbf","body":{"detail":"Registration derives a name from the repository and branch (spec section 11) without an event; session.start's body is harness, harness_session_id, cwd, transcript_path and pid. The first agent.name then reports previous: <derived name> with no earlier event naming it, and an @name in a comment cannot be tied to its session from the journal alone.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":208},"end":{"line":214},"content_hash":"2531645c1bbef5581474f3318cd70a2a599ab739af3be8223fbe8da994159a5b"},"suggested_fix":"Add name (classed as a name for redaction) to session.start and session.join bodies, and say so in audit spec section 6.8.","summary":"A session's derived name is never recorded, so agent.name's previous names a value the journal never held","supersedes":"7247b1a205dbb5ea493ac46ad1a42645a731c5afe155b24006ed7e18dfe759b2","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:13:39.980244Z","id":"15a2cbd552a5b3f8d51d001413e7735bcbc210ef74a5c3aee4b9a1b0b3ed31d4","body":{"detail":"release_owned_in (crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs) selects threads WHERE target_session_id = ?1, and Store::roster groups threads by target_session_id; crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs indexes neither. Both are full scans of threads: off the request hot paths (ends, the reaper, GET /api/agents) and cheap at today's sizes, but linear in all threads ever made.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1612},"end":{"line":1628},"content_hash":"ed1cb058eed0b38a9d4e07ae6c733539b4ca4c1c6388d6f7a4614ccf4b5c1af2"},"suggested_fix":"Add CREATE INDEX threads_by_target ON threads(target_session_id) WHERE target_session_id IS NOT NULL in the next migration.","summary":"Every session end and every roster read scans threads for target_session_id, which has no index","supersedes":"a3d0695a93efadfc5368992b5d4e4d1b040eff37d58ba1a6ce10d7be659a7bd0","tags":["perf","revisit:the next migration on this branch","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:37:11.637343Z","id":"86480a5fcda514f361d2261c01f67620ad69abc7ddc57a4d0e70a6c9b97452e0","body":{"detail":"Failure: grant session B (claude, harness_session_id b-h, parent_pid 100) is live; a join proving B with harness_session_id c-h, parent_pid 300, ancestor_pids [250, 100] answers 200 with B's row, and a registration proving B with harness_session_id c-h, parent_pid 300 answers 201 with B's row and overwrites B's parent_pid to 300 (harness_session_id stays b-h). Checked with a scratch test against crates/clax-server/tests/api_people.rs's people() fixture.\n\nproved_row's (None, Some(p)) arm takes the proved row p whenever nothing matched, without checking that p's harness_session_id is NULL or equal to the request's. Local join (join_session_proved, the ancestor loop) only matches parent and ancestor PIDs for rows whose harness_session_id IS NULL, so the remote path is wider than spec 2026-10-08 §6.8's \"in the order join matches\". The client side feeds it: RemoteSession::keys in crates/clax-cli/src/commands/hook.rs looks for <harness>-ppid-<pid>.json for the hook's parent and every ancestor, and the shim writes that file for every row with a parent PID (Claude Code's rows have both). So a claude run from another claude's shell (claude -p, a subagent process) whose SessionStart hook runs before its own shim has written its files finds the outer agent's ppid file through its ancestors, proves the outer session, joins it, and absorb() writes the inner harness session ID's file with the outer credential; the inner shim then registers with that file and owns the outer row too. The inner agent acts with the outer agent's elevation, and the inner agent's exit (end_session) ends the outer agent's session, whose shim then re-registers unnarrowed. A stale ppid file of a crashed harness whose session is still live (remote sessions idle out after 30 minutes) is picked up the same way by a new process that reuses the PID.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":339},"end":{"line":355},"content_hash":"9eb9947d213c95f7b307c572191c1e2fa7dda1ded99d68effa8d893205bd6cc9"},"suggested_fix":"In proved_row's (None, Some(p)) arm, refresh p only when p's harness_session_id is NULL or equals the request's harness_session_id (and, for a ppid-only key, when p's parent_pid is the request's parent or one of its ancestors); otherwise make a new row as an unproved request would. In RemoteSession::keys, use the parent and ancestor PID files only when the hook has no harness session ID file and the file's row has no harness session ID, matching join. Add a test for the nested case and for the hook's PID fallback (removing the ancestors from RemoteSession::keys, or making wait_for_credential return at once, fails no test today).","summary":"A grant's registration or join that proves a session refreshes that session's row whatever harness session ID and parent PID it carries, so a nested agent holding its parent's credential becomes the parent's session","tags":["review","security","spec:6.8","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:37:11.638431Z","id":"c3e112f9e34ed1934a3b62f9b3a99d5c9b98a00a60c25a9bf635a27db6fdc370","body":{"detail":"Failure: session S of a grant is narrowed to reading; a request proving S passes Identity::prove_session (crates/clax-server/src/identity.rs:284), S then ends before st.grant_caller (identity.rs:289) reads it; end_session cleared narrow_json, and this branch reads narrow_json without checking ended_at, so the request gets person_rights ∩ grant.narrow, without S's narrowing and without the other live narrowings a session-less request gets. ReadRights::current (crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs:745-756) re-reads rights the same way for a long-poll that outlives its session. The window is short and the request proved S, but spec §6.8 says a session-less request is never wider than any live narrowing, and an ended session should be no wider.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2367},"end":{"line":2392},"content_hash":"f51f6db526e5d783d5f02fd3fe6a6a9b5f37ee9a1851380cc99edd5c31d5abc7"},"suggested_fix":"When the row has ended_at set, return unknown_session (or fall back to sessionless_narrow); or prove and read rights in one read transaction.","summary":"grant_caller for an ended session gives the grant's rights without that session's narrowing, wider than a session-less request","tags":["review","spec:6.8","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:23:20.893725Z","id":"e414ec93c69188590ae16b8c691d608b2082f410777dc20c2513f499db1a29eb","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:903f2670","summary":"proved_row no longer adopts a proved row its call's harness session ID and parent PID do not match: matching nothing makes a new row, and a grant's row keeps its first parent PID. Evidence: api_people::a_nested_agent_proving_its_parents_session_gets_its_own (the reviewer's join with hsid c-h, ppid 300, ancestors [250, 100] and registration with ppid 300 now get rows of their own; the parent's hsid and parent PID unchanged) and connect::a_nested_agents_hook_never_becomes_its_parents_session pass; the mutation restoring the adoption is caught by the first, the one restoring adoption, ancestor-file use and the parent-PID rewrite together by all three (target/t19a/mutations2.txt).","supersedes":"86480a5fcda514f361d2261c01f67620ad69abc7ddc57a4d0e70a6c9b97452e0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:23:20.897991Z","id":"69473b44347adaec6d4d28cd2384a31752c703c1defa90fa5a72722ad0c11f2c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:903f2670","summary":"grant_caller_in answers invalid_session_proof for a session that has ended, so a request proved just before the end never gets the ended session's cleared rights; ReadRights::current goes through it too. Evidence: store::people::tests::a_grant_caller_has_the_persons_rights_within_every_narrowing_and_a_live_elevation asserts it and catches the mutation that drops the check.","supersedes":"c3e112f9e34ed1934a3b62f9b3a99d5c9b98a00a60c25a9bf635a27db6fdc370","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:23:46.411584Z","id":"457d6348d5c651eb7038a4d0103b8d083e7175c75dab1047a4b9252a17783c1e","body":{"detail":"An invite that expires unredeemed records nothing (audit spec section 6.13 lists only invite.create and invite.revoke). When release_unconnected then returns its person to a plain viewer it sets person = 0 and rights_json = NULL in the sweep or a revoke, so rights set by invite.create's rights or person.rights change with no person.rights event: the journal's last word on that person's rights is wrong.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2298},"end":{"line":2309},"content_hash":"3661554d9ec3b6ade08fbb453c62e14c05eacd1871b109bac087e43dd7492399"},"summary":"An invite's lapse is not recorded, and release_unconnected clears a person's flag and rights without an event","supersedes":"b194108f740df12f0ce0f12d339d1c0dc26f8db78c69ff2b2b2ee3922732aeeb","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:23:46.413845Z","id":"79df4925da3b3b5abf3080c782d1ee3eb8cfda2f3bb61b0c445c75af8fb17a18","body":{"detail":"release_owned_in (crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs) selects threads WHERE target_session_id = ?1, and Store::roster groups threads by target_session_id; crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs indexes neither. Both are full scans of threads: off the request hot paths (ends, the reaper, GET /api/agents) and cheap at today's sizes, but linear in all threads ever made.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1615},"end":{"line":1631},"content_hash":"ed1cb058eed0b38a9d4e07ae6c733539b4ca4c1c6388d6f7a4614ccf4b5c1af2"},"suggested_fix":"Add CREATE INDEX threads_by_target ON threads(target_session_id) WHERE target_session_id IS NOT NULL in the next migration.","summary":"Every session end and every roster read scans threads for target_session_id, which has no index","supersedes":"15a2cbd552a5b3f8d51d001413e7735bcbc210ef74a5c3aee4b9a1b0b3ed31d4","tags":["perf","revisit:the next migration on this branch","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:22:22.162354Z","id":"a0eaedef6e2d0c3950fee681e0849fee546b19cc992beefde05fa706602b9f94","body":{"detail":"Failure: on a daemon bound to the LAN with a connected person Sam who has a live agent, `curl http://<LAN IP>:<port>/api/artifacts/<aid>/threads` with no cookie (and the `thread` events of `GET /api/events`, built by publish_thread in crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs:65) returns `\"approves_first\": [\"u_<Sam>\"]` on every thread with a LAN viewer's comment, also on an artifact none of Sam's agents publishes or watches. Store::approves_first walks every person with a live session (`SELECT person FROM sessions WHERE ended_at IS NULL`), not the artifact's live participants, and crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs:612-617 adds the field to the reader-independent view, which only agent channels strip (Vis::filter_threads). Spec 2026-10-08 section 18 gives a LAN viewer no People or approvals view and a connected person only their own; section 10 asks for the hint only on agents that may receive the thread.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1585},"end":{"line":1625},"content_hash":"c3f2bd4bb7734900c24a41be13266490f98fa1d92159b2dcd6069f41271516b8"},"suggested_fix":"Compute it only for people with a live agent among the artifact's participants that may read it, and serve it only to the owner's and connected people's browsers: leave it out for Caller::Viewer and Caller::Anonymous, and out of the public `thread` event (the shell can refetch, or the event can carry it per topic subscriber). Add an api test that an unconnected LAN viewer's thread view and the anonymous event stream have no approves_first.","summary":"approves_first tells every browser, LAN viewers and anonymous /api/events subscribers included, which people have a live agent anywhere and that they have not approved a thread's authors","tags":["review","privacy","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/attention.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:22:22.163410Z","id":"777d98c6fe3493450d21592b819e7122099fe64fbb6831667eab3e8c864de41b","body":{"detail":"agent_person names the person with crate::feedback::person_name, i.e. display_name (crates/clax-core/src/feedback.rs:232), written for agent payload lines. The Send menu group ('<name>'s agents'), 'X approves first', the owner chip and its hover text therefore show a person invited as `<img src=x onerror=alert(1)>Samantha \"Sam\" Bartholomew-Long` as `<img src=x onerror=alert(1)>Samantha Sam`, while People shows the full name. Two people whose names share their first 40 characters get identical 'X's agents' groups in the Send menu.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":430},"end":{"line":441},"content_hash":"d345aba18067820ef0a65348efcffa9b7e8b8ad7d75fe9471655f44b90134143"},"suggested_fix":"Give browsers the stored display name (rendered as text, as Svelte does) and keep display_name for agent payloads; or serve both.","summary":"Browsers show people's names through the agent-payload sanitiser: cut to 40 characters, quotes and colons removed","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:22:22.163936Z","id":"39accad39031cbac3f2fb405d0d75d15626b73b191a51a6837719af0d3898fd0","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"207b96651905997d3bcb50bb814b8b286468087737dd183ee1025e83d97767ef","summary":"Measured: no difference beyond noise with 7 people and 8 live agents. Debug builds of a2378555 and f7a89d53 on copies of one home (100 threads, 4 comments each, 3 LAN authors), 150 requests each, interleaved 3 times: GET .../threads?include_resolved=true&limit=200 as the owner's browser, median 51.6/28.4/22.7 ms at a2378555 against 30.4/20.1/38.7 ms at f7a89d53; one thread 2.7/3.6/1.0 ms against 3.8/0.9/1.1 ms. The cost is still paid and thrown away on every agent read (Vis::filter_threads removes the field): computing it only when the caller is a browser would remove it from the agents' hot path.","tags":["review","perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:49:36.254077Z","id":"98457fcc40b019dce3fe8fc1a0ae7376f740909068bbceb52d1d26b473bc7b8b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:bb547990","summary":"approves_first left every thread view and event; the Send menu asks GET /api/artifacts/{aid}/approves-first as it opens, which answers only the owner's and connected people's browsers and names only people with a live agent owning or watching the artifact, computed per request. Evidence: api_approvals::who_approves_first_reaches_only_the_owner_and_connected_people passes (403 with no cookie, for a LAN viewer's cookie and for Sam's agent; no approves_first in thread or list views for anyone or in the anonymous /api/events stream; [] on an artifact none of Sam's agents touches); web/e2e/agent-strip.spec.ts sees the LAN viewer's menu get 403 and show no 'approves first'.","supersedes":"a0eaedef6e2d0c3950fee681e0849fee546b19cc992beefde05fa706602b9f94","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/attention.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:49:36.256768Z","id":"7e255352dbf8f30a3fa3184177610d719b6042c35b71e4a59e3b1faf4473fe4c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:bb547990","summary":"AgentPerson.name and a thread owner's person_name are the stored display name for browsers (browser_name in crates/clax-core/src/store/attention.rs); agent channels get display_name of them (mark_participants and Vis::filter_threads in crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs). Evidence: the single-owner golden check and api_approvals pass; the Send menu shows 'Sam's agents' from the stored name in web/e2e/agent-strip.spec.ts.","supersedes":"777d98c6fe3493450d21592b819e7122099fe64fbb6831667eab3e8c864de41b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:49:36.260138Z","id":"a7c042653cb74a24c83770886558a1c7b4219f9c9c24fba09fd16a687f88bab0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:bb547990","summary":"approves_first no longer runs in views_and_senders: only GET /api/artifacts/{aid}/approves-first computes it, for the people with a live agent on that artifact, when a browser's Send menu opens; agents' reads, deliveries and events never pay for it. Evidence: grep shows no approves_first in crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs; api_approvals passes.","supersedes":"207b96651905997d3bcb50bb814b8b286468087737dd183ee1025e83d97767ef","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:08:21.317340Z","id":"ba8eec0436c419504b7361b6dbce01b4586e84e3ed336c90756cfabc8d46808d","body":{"detail":"Failure: Lucy (LAN viewer) comments on a thread, the owner replies '+1', Sam allows the owner everywhere, and the owner sends the thread to Sam's agent. Sam's agent takes the '+1' (wait_for_feedback), which stamps placeholder_at on Lucy's held row. Sam declines the request for Lucy. Sam's agent replies, the owner comments 'Thanks!', and the agent takes that too. feedback_state stays {state: withheld, approver: Sam} at every step, so the owner's card reads 'waiting for Sam's approval' with no approval card above it (nothing is open), and Sam's agent sees the same state in comments_read. state_of now returns withheld when any undelivered row of any comment has placeholder_at set, whatever became of the request; before bb547990 that only held while the held comment was the thread's newest. Declining keeps rows held (spec 2026-10-08 section 9.3) but nothing is waiting any more.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1886},"end":{"line":1922},"content_hash":"760381a85127c694c5033b83960670ed530883e92bcb1f7ca66ff3f12767bc0f"},"suggested_fix":"Count a row of an earlier comment as waiting only while an open request covers it (requested), not for placeholder_at alone; keep placeholder_at for the latest comment's rows as today. Add an api test: decline, then a later comment delivered and acknowledged, and the state is not withheld.","summary":"A declined comment keeps its thread 'waiting for <person>'s approval' for good, even after the agent took and answered later comments","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:13:10.748497Z","id":"9acd539a8823db7db6b61a102065166aea8e50fb437e48ea1fe0c0348c7b7954","body":{"detail":"It is an outbound credential the daemon presents to the public Clax on every push, so it cannot be hashed like the inbound tokens the store verifies. The database lives in the home, which only its user reads; the token never appears in a view (Remote has no token field; tests/api_remotes.rs checks no listing carries cxa_), an event or an audit record. A home copied elsewhere carries it: revoke it on the public People page. Moving it to the OS keychain would protect a copied home but needs code the Durable Object build must not compile.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":303},"end":{"line":315},"content_hash":"fd9f0bd8892117130346d36e0afcd15890f15c5a754e582aba89c15a40ae038f"},"summary":"A remote's agent token is kept as it is in the home's database (remotes.token), not hashed","tags":["security","revisit:a home is synced or backed up off the machine","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:13:10.748885Z","id":"0f393eb404e738ed177d83bd58c7d1ba13136b85b4dda06602901f78d2b2555c","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":773},"end":{"line":784},"content_hash":"ff54731f13da1dbf09cc8a7ae4e835b7eaa3bd9ffe8bd279bf4f50cad4f26bf5"},"summary":"Migration 29 (publishing to a public Clax) takes the next number after 28 (forks) on akesling/clax-artifacts; it renumbers if another branch lands a 29 first","tags":["migrations","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/pushes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:18:07.373099Z","id":"2bb8f6cbd48adca1bc772379f27c4dc5e02bed603c0b6c7e3ed168925f75ae60","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"21edf3242c460fc3d1581dd84094e5fa5b4c5d69c6b105002bfc209d3e20d1c2","summary":"Since 4f1f7191 no member or member's agent gets a write token where pushes are credited to the owner (crates/clax-server/src/git_remotes.rs credited, push_unattributed), so the tokens this instance mints reach this path only for the owner and the owner's agents. A token minted on the Cloudflare dashboard or by the Artifacts API directly still pushes as the owner.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/pushes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:19:46.859440Z","id":"d3d39306f761505e22c91617ba07e03b3d0d05f07e38b10b367e7265619fe49f","body":{"detail":"A refused commit stays on main (it is neither recorded nor tagged), and the stand-in refuses non-fast-forward pushes (clax-git ServeOptions deny_non_fast_forwards), so the only way past it is a push over it by someone who may publish. That commit is recorded with every file changed since the newest version authored by its pusher (record_push), so a refused or revoked person's changes reach other people's agents as, say, the owner's under the visibility filter; its note names the refused commits. The hosted prototype credits a changed blob to every author it already had in history (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts recordPushes, blobAuthors); here a refused commit's blobs have no recorded author. Fix: credit paths whose blob equals one in a refused commit to that commit's pusher as well, or refuse the commit over it until those paths match the newest version.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":144},"end":{"line":152},"content_hash":"8c34d7356614154fc05784b37020214d4aab0dc8a7a3271396030174350c9b1e"},"summary":"A commit recorded over refused commits carries their changes as its own pusher's words","supersedes":"e820a816ed32bc46f1ccfea44a27cde49e9b02191cbaf3c876a1591b92a31e66","tags":["security","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/pushes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:19:46.865625Z","id":"6d8f2fc3f0005c574f3fa7db148b581a10291bbea550b61b60b17cadaeb9e0ab","body":{"detail":"Pushes to Artifacts' own git endpoint never pass RepoDO, so RepoDO's ledger has no git_pushes row for their commits (crates/clax-worker/src/repos/db.rs record_push, written only by tokens::note_push from RepoDO's /git/ route), and the queue consumer reconciles with Pusher::default() (crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs queue). pushers_of then gives every such commit the fallback, the owner: the owner becomes the version's publisher and the author of its changed files, and Store::standing allows it, whoever held the Artifacts token. clax_git::events::event_repo reads only the repository's name; the event's documented payload (ref, before, after, commits; crates/clax-git/src/events.rs:21-25) names no token or actor that is known here. Fix: once the pushed event's schema names the token (Artifacts tokens are entered in git_tokens with hash NULL by tokens::mint) or the actor, have the queue consumer enter a git_pushes row for the event's after commit with that token's holder before it asks the instance to reconcile.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":475},"end":{"line":487},"content_hash":"38cc39ea7d33382de52e273c944e0c51a787210b5289531ea9b52b303e7a18bd"},"summary":"A push straight to Cloudflare Artifacts is credited to the owner and passes the rights recheck as the owner","supersedes":"21edf3242c460fc3d1581dd84094e5fa5b4c5d69c6b105002bfc209d3e20d1c2","tags":["security","revisit:Cloudflare Artifacts' pushed-event schema is known","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"f20aca051889442db19a7cd27f7a0a371e39dd8899016bcdf7228093a8476745","body":{"detail":"ArtifactLocks (content/mod.rs) serialise version writes within one process, so there the loser waits and then sees Conflict (concurrent_publishes_with_same_if_version_yield_one_winner). Across processes the loser's content write fails first; it is mapped to Conflict only when the artifact has already moved past the expected version. Nothing is corrupted (the loser removes nothing it did not write). The daemon is the only writer of versions today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1262},"end":{"line":1271},"content_hash":"4904f3490dcc2f9f92baa1aaa49032071480c9eaf3740604defd236f4657e508"},"summary":"Two processes publishing the same version at once: the loser gets the content store's AlreadyExists error, not Conflict, while the winner has not yet recorded it","supersedes":"52efc8cf1dcb2f90828a3d760d44019837906384769b412643c383e800109719","tags":["content-store","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"cf48f5cba4caa68ac467bcc8b78055579987fede3b4f53fea52e804971160738","body":{"detail":"An invite that expires unredeemed records nothing (audit spec section 6.13 lists only invite.create and invite.revoke). When release_unconnected then returns its person to a plain viewer it sets person = 0 and rights_json = NULL in the sweep or a revoke, so rights set by invite.create's rights or person.rights change with no person.rights event: the journal's last word on that person's rights is wrong.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2345},"end":{"line":2356},"content_hash":"2ddd5903658167c04514801afdde1244c244a163cfb84079293eb4ae9676bcf3"},"summary":"An invite's lapse is not recorded, and release_unconnected clears a person's flag and rights without an event","supersedes":"457d6348d5c651eb7038a4d0103b8d083e7175c75dab1047a4b9252a17783c1e","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"6166fd3e2db5709106a3bc65071f99db02c217dfb40a59adc6ca0256ae12af21","body":{"detail":"release_owned_in (crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs) selects threads WHERE target_session_id = ?1, and Store::roster groups threads by target_session_id; crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs indexes neither. Both are full scans of threads: off the request hot paths (ends, the reaper, GET /api/agents) and cheap at today's sizes, but linear in all threads ever made.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1662},"end":{"line":1678},"content_hash":"ed1cb058eed0b38a9d4e07ae6c733539b4ca4c1c6388d6f7a4614ccf4b5c1af2"},"suggested_fix":"Add CREATE INDEX threads_by_target ON threads(target_session_id) WHERE target_session_id IS NOT NULL in the next migration.","summary":"Every session end and every roster read scans threads for target_session_id, which has no index","supersedes":"79df4925da3b3b5abf3080c782d1ee3eb8cfda2f3bb61b0c445c75af8fb17a18","tags":["perf","revisit:the next migration on this branch","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"662c3db594b21a7060f0afddc51aaf69ec84a89ba9bf35f8844f6667cdf936f3","body":{"detail":"Measured on this machine (load average about 45): the clax-core lib tests take 12.4 s with --skip the_store_tests_pass_on_one_connection and 20.8 s with it, since the child runs 455 tests after the parent's. The threshold `passed > 300` passes with 455; a module dropped from the filter (or from test_util::store) loses its coverage on one connection without failing it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":748},"end":{"line":774},"content_hash":"b3bfd31319c95da4542d5ac7bd7f9fa165b3082f4e9534f5f055a9a24bdcbbee"},"suggested_fix":"Compare `passed` against the count the same filter lists (`--list`) less the ignored ones, or pin the module set.","summary":"The one-connection rerun adds about 8 s to the clax-core unit suite, and its >300 threshold only catches an empty filter","supersedes":"db8e547c1f42d76824e5f88f42bff6e50d6134ff62f023eabab5478b0e328e5a","tags":["wasm","gate-speed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"a54936c253991bc950ddce220775bf87013ef3dd232e62983bebd29734850814","body":{"detail":"Spec §9.3: 'Declining keeps the rows held; a later ask there makes a new request only after 10 minutes'. request_in applies the same quiet period to routing, so a sender pressing Send again right after the approver declined does not re-announce the request; the rows are held and the agent's placeholder reads as not asked. If the owner wants a deliberate re-send to ask at once, drop the check for Cause::Routing.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1121},"end":{"line":1130},"content_hash":"cf9707d61e55687d29484ea3ec1da7a8faa513bbca583c591bf81438ce7a4e23"},"summary":"A routed send within ten minutes of a decline makes no request, though spec §9.3 names only ask","supersedes":"ea1fcd06efb9ffa14ac30061358d3f922277ec079550f1f2827e63b6bd8c50d0","tags":["people","spec:9.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"f44a993b894b9ddc111348acac69544749bd1a02dc0da23b82bed822bb6a2b03","body":{"detail":"withheld_in_thread counts the authors withheld from each comment body (the rows a take holds, spec M16). A thread whose comments the agent may see but whose anchor, clip or artifact title is another person's (spec §3.3 step 6) is delivered with those fields placeholdered and makes no request; the agent can ask for the artifact's content outside threads with ask {approval: {url_or_id}} (Store::ask_approval, withheld_outside_threads), which covers text fields, the current version, documents and assets, but not a thread's anchor.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1295},"end":{"line":1315},"content_hash":"2db7bc0ea49daabf8d49defd3d54488b8041d0c22a95068bc6531cfc23d68cee"},"summary":"Routing asks only for the authors of comment bodies; a withheld anchor, clip, batch note or title makes no request","supersedes":"b00f8f3b34bd3743dee054d554a2aca908864f9acb5a3a4751f5cc844c93ad67","tags":["people","spec:9.2","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"76a4396fc7dc41e1a920d8c820e4319193e1b260368943860c3f06549a3c38ce","body":{"detail":"The overflow marker (install row approval_overflow:<approver>) lists the [author, artifact, thread] places whose routed content request_in held without a request, past MAX_OPEN_REQUESTS (100) per approver or MAX_OPEN_PER_AUTHOR (20) per author. Only Store::decide_request rechecks them, dropping a place once its content is no longer held without a request (held_without_request: answered by an open or declined request, delivered, gone, or now visible). A withdrawal or an approval made outside a decision changes nothing until the next decision, so the banner can outlive what it counted.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1963},"end":{"line":1973},"content_hash":"73f004277ac55d0d5d175ac9d9633a7b394f8ae4a809ba5e85e370048b9398ee"},"summary":"People's overflow banner stays up after withdrawals bring an approver under the limit, until their next decision","supersedes":"0f0f13b253b8d8325d9ba5173c3b1bb2dc6c743bc19bd332167a9e10c2f467d3","tags":["people","spec:9.2","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"48e1e5e1883fa49109508fc5eebed9f11caa313dcc215d69f754f214b213a892","body":{"detail":"A push to Cloudflare Artifacts whose pushed event is lost, late or never delivered (no subscription, locally: the queue is simulated and receives none, crates/clax-worker/wrangler.jsonc queues) stays unrecorded until the next publish of the artifact, so viewers see the older version meanwhile. The prototype also reconciles lazily on reads, at most every RECONCILE_EVERY_MS (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts reconcileLazily). Fix: reconcile from the artifact read routes when main has moved past the current version's commit, rate-limited per artifact.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1132},"end":{"line":1152},"content_hash":"5aea8e38f17328396770571e0e3d99efadde21ae073543404d5fa024591c706c"},"summary":"Pushed commits are recorded on a push, an Artifacts event or a publish, but not when an artifact is read","supersedes":"6eb29bd424b71eeb4396d78e90ca369e00b87fb4bf6f6799b2907f999f5ac5d8","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"31efff25ca3c25b43875ceffaddbbad5b0b7fba39820bb242a7bdc34f7993c6b","body":{"detail":"An agent token is a bearer grant (grants.bearer = 1, its cxa_ token in grant_tokens, kept out of credential_index so it never passes the signed Clax-Grant path). The endpoint resolves Authorization: Bearer cxa_... with bearer_grant, then Store::grant_caller for its person and rights, and builds Caller::PersonAgent; no route accepts the token yet.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":802},"end":{"line":806},"content_hash":"6118ad026448bf7342835eef06f09082a183699f7c1c18391bc4c90fa653e306"},"summary":"Store::bearer_grant is how the remote MCP endpoint should authenticate an agent token","supersedes":"6eba3e92b317e95b653e14bf055bffbe61bfffcbda0cc6a32a79407ba06ee437","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"89caff5089f0864057eb1a101a833112aac5c33d084cc313153b2578a65ece6a","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":744},"end":{"line":746},"content_hash":"7b8c2cfc4b3987a8e331333cde1cdfbfbebd527f736765bcd9ae5f2176add692"},"summary":"Migration 27 (hosted sign-in) takes the next number after multi-person's 26; it renumbers if another branch lands first","supersedes":"1a769143fc51679984b3c9067cfcc62b06effe0f6a6fd8db39a16a82fb2eb1ee","tags":["hosted","merge","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"bdba21c35e648a55e17ed451f6538152b7656a55a8117129b54a4992b5f5c9af","body":{"detail":"routes/sessions.rs register calls end_bearer_sessions_beyond(gid, BEARER_SESSION_CAP - 1) and then register_session_restoring in separate transactions; concurrent initializes of one token can each count the same live set. The next registration trims it back. Accepted as a bound on build-up, not an exact limit.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1254},"end":{"line":1283},"content_hash":"8ef33f44d4f1cafe046fb180228494b8e47afb2f14aca6b7df5ba45bf9f7a4bc"},"summary":"Two agent-token registrations at once can each leave room for themselves, so a token briefly holds more than BEARER_SESSION_CAP live sessions","supersedes":"8e257b9da7500461ad5b445cbff9f22886089844cc9d2aefee32ab89b237a0af","tags":["hosted","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:31:12.155334Z","id":"23f7f049228a15bed6b11105deaaab06a529181039e8a5219cec098b1d4dcc00","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate head left by a merge: the same record as 52efc8cf1dcb2f90828a3d760d44019837906384769b412643c383e800109719 (kept), re-anchored on a parallel branch.","supersedes":"2ac8a07f9c4c66299aeeedf0179a48661d95b450b9c3a1550f33a73788d3db83","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:31:12.163134Z","id":"ee466131cdf449e14af3916ec7326fa44a89b0ffb7dddd045c729e17721ffbdd","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate head left by a merge: the same record as 457d6348d5c651eb7038a4d0103b8d083e7175c75dab1047a4b9252a17783c1e (kept), re-anchored on a parallel branch.","supersedes":"0f03209fab22a7d4d6c0ef2c586133261710f0c807456f6175bd0638a04d1eaf","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:31:12.170866Z","id":"6a6f30701861e7faf32382fc9de853a6461d2dca6a8087e514be299c0262fb1c","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate head left by a merge: the same record as 457d6348d5c651eb7038a4d0103b8d083e7175c75dab1047a4b9252a17783c1e (kept), re-anchored on a parallel branch.","supersedes":"74144e335949ccfd8af4519de32993625199510204043e973648057bb088dce5","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:31:12.178564Z","id":"33fb6d0b2749e1e13968411301d47361372ae3d6a5cf850a3fb341765d7a5ee7","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate head left by a merge: the same record as 79df4925da3b3b5abf3080c782d1ee3eb8cfda2f3bb61b0c445c75af8fb17a18 (kept), re-anchored on a parallel branch.","supersedes":"9a4f58ee20fb7e58f8a01519feb88a7b8800595d47aa7041438deb69cbb79601","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:31:12.186200Z","id":"42b62c1325e28ce3e0087a6d3230520528172367cdc65e8c16eeb524d78bb598","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate head left by a merge: the same record as db8e547c1f42d76824e5f88f42bff6e50d6134ff62f023eabab5478b0e328e5a (kept), re-anchored on a parallel branch.","supersedes":"a768d0cd8dea941b68daa0d7c3057c13b04d011b670dc1d3764a2f91a385a35a","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:31:12.193735Z","id":"f868228f85a7d724b0b1f6d5350b8fdb89beb799b12b6041cd1ed9718d82c113","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate head left by a merge: the same record as fc163ac86b24034a99b950c26b52c00bcf554fb67c8f3bd4f222b016f4391e8d (kept), re-anchored on a parallel branch.","supersedes":"28379c61fa3cef7b6976b9ecb1af60533e6d601d7dad5260432a0c6b5de53030","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:34:33.800076Z","id":"bc636cd890d48523064d21a02b3c2517554ba3ee433ebe549570fac15f40e761","body":{"detail":"state_of reports withheld (the target session's person as approver) from placeholder_at, which a take sets when it holds and tells a row, or while an open approval request of that person covers the row's comment author there (a send naming the agent, spec §10). A comment that joins no request (a send naming no agent, a later reply whose author has no open request there, an author held past the request limits) reads sent, waiting on its tier, until the agent's next take. Computing it from visibility at state time would build a Visibility per target session's person inside feedback_states_in, which listings call for every thread (spec §8.7 cost).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1908},"end":{"line":1918},"content_hash":"3edfebb08b996496021ae068b6b21a1a3edea4254039cca0c53fe55bf7e0f80b"},"summary":"A held row that no open request covers reads sent until a take holds it","supersedes":"514bd451a21893d051884cf0fbeda01ff745214b916836fb1bb26e76e9159282","tags":["people","spec:8.4","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:34:33.800076Z","id":"0007f8b821ba68e224e273c1e5f3091f8911bb4cd1fb07908b15a1e45f5a454c","body":{"detail":"Store::version_meta resolves p.person, else the session's person, else the owner, before the content write; version_authors (artifacts.rs:817) resolves the row's person again inside the transaction. They agree today (tests a_version_write_names_its_publisher_agent_and_note), but a change to one rule that misses the other makes git's Clax-Publisher disagree with the row.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1393},"end":{"line":1410},"content_hash":"48d111421f495d2e72c03035f37a629a7bd29de6662dec8fbd17c5f02aa85418"},"suggested_fix":"Resolve the person once before the content lock and pass it to version_authors.","summary":"The publisher the content store is told and the one the version row records are resolved by separate code","supersedes":"fc163ac86b24034a99b950c26b52c00bcf554fb67c8f3bd4f222b016f4391e8d","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:34:33.800076Z","id":"cf39d49f25cf3e1c15bc3803244ec8fac55e2d146a133212842eeafc6c435bfa","body":{"detail":"The prototype names a guest 'Name (guest)' wherever Clax shows a name to an agent or an approver. Here a guest is a plain viewer row with viewers.guest = 1; feedback, comments_read and approval views show the bare name. Names cannot collide with members' or other guests' (check_guest_name), which limits impersonation.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":282},"end":{"line":318},"content_hash":"fa6b1bcabd7d4ab1064bfd5c639d34232f3e0b5b95de9eb1b91c01616fba37b0"},"suggested_fix":"Mark guest authors in the agent-facing views and approval cards.","summary":"Guests are not labelled as guests to agents or approvers","supersedes":"b3c8598da46ce8a6053247f9a88f6e3aa31eefd37e034d7da75e9811bf3aa14c","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:09:04.864126Z","id":"73a4817f62ff8f182f1e479807ffe5b3c0a2e4b15e76e8ac112f25f784c0a63a","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":778},"end":{"line":900},"content_hash":"81d28a5a5d7d5d7c0afb566585eaf6cacea20053681ea5ebaef6e2b181507201"},"summary":"Migration 30 (publishing to a public Clax) follows akesling/clax-artifacts' 29 (sessions.client_name); it renumbers if another branch lands a 30 first. It also rebuilds inbox_items to add the `push` kind, as migration 26 left the table.","supersedes":"0f393eb404e738ed177d83bd58c7d1ba13136b85b4dda06602901f78d2b2555c","tags":["migrations","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:09:04.870176Z","id":"301ee474309f153f63d3fded73bf060881730caadf7f644779fef8c43da3bc34","body":{"detail":"Small rows, but they outlive the artifact and the grant. Dropping keys of revoked grants or older than some months would bound it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":858},"end":{"line":865},"content_hash":"3809d3eb40206bf1050d7706a17caa1d82c06599c44bd8c816fb14753e919899"},"summary":"publish_keys is never pruned: one row per version an agent token published with a key","tags":["deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/device.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:09:04.870225Z","id":"4e3bca1ddae092c5de3457ae0e5a81db73422cc79da007308d40bbd69a26400e","body":{"detail":"approve_device mints the bearer grant at approval; the token is only issued at the next poll, and the code expires after 600 s. Nobody holds the token, but the grant stays listed until revoked by hand.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":183},"end":{"line":209},"content_hash":"ce7e08161692dd5ed330e4a1c699eaaa3595d06aa0ec20426b822b2f2a187a6b"},"summary":"A device sign-in approved but never polled (the machine went away) leaves a live agent token on its person's People page","tags":["security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:09:17.075097Z","id":"ac2c115c8d3fa17746e2167224ec1d8464182a95cc245c4706eb3a633772d326","body":{"detail":"It is an outbound credential the daemon presents to the public Clax on every push, so it cannot be hashed like the inbound tokens the store verifies. It never appears in a view (Remote has no token field; tests/api_remotes.rs checks no listing carries cxa_), an event or an audit record. When a sign-in connects, the daemon makes the home 0700 and the database's files 0600 (crates/clax-server/src/routes/remotes.rs owner_only; checked in api_remotes's connect). A home copied elsewhere carries it: clax remote remove revokes it there, or the public People page does. Moving it to the OS keychain would protect a copied home but needs code the Durable Object build must not compile.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":316},"end":{"line":328},"content_hash":"fd9f0bd8892117130346d36e0afcd15890f15c5a754e582aba89c15a40ae038f"},"summary":"A remote's agent token is kept as it is in the home's database (remotes.token), not hashed","supersedes":"9acd539a8823db7db6b61a102065166aea8e50fb437e48ea1fe0c0348c7b7954","tags":["security","revisit:a home is synced or backed up off the machine","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:18:44.655403Z","id":"38119a4c1703e09942d65bb86491ef8e1216cb801c867aed68560827d4925ab0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:fb207faf","summary":"One predicate, StateRow::waits_for_approval: a row waits while undelivered for a live session and held under an open request, or told of (placeholder_at) with no request its person declined; deciding a decline announces the thread's state again. Evidence: api_approvals::a_declined_comment_leaves_its_thread_waiting_for_nothing passes with the reviewer's sequence (LAN comment, owner '+1', send to Sam's agent, the agent takes the '+1', Sam declines, the agent replies, owner 'Thanks!', the agent takes it): not withheld for the owner, in the event, or in Sam's agent's thread view; it fails when declined rows count. Chromium: target/t22/shots-r2/owner-after-decline-long-chip-* and person-after-decline-* read 'seen by the agent'.","supersedes":"ba8eec0436c419504b7361b6dbce01b4586e84e3ed336c90756cfabc8d46808d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T05:05:31.657396Z","id":"d77ce5d28133318c9457e08de5ad656360a7f455fed34bf4257b6f08aa9b6f7c","body":{"detail":"Failure: Sam writes a thread and sends it to Mia's agent (Mia has not approved Sam); Mia declines the request. From the decline on, every viewer (owner, Sam, Mia, a LAN viewer, no cookie) reads 'sent, waiting for the agent · <elapsed> · waiting on the agent finishing its current work', in the API (state sent, tier stop_hook) and in Chromium, live and after a reload. It stays so after the agent's take (which tells it of the withheld content, stamping placeholder_at) and after the author's later comments, which join no request (spec section 9.2) and are held silently. waits_for_approval leaves a declined row out, and state_of then reads the latest row as undelivered for a live target: Sent. Nothing is on its way to the agent, and the sender is never told the comment was declined. Record 514bd451 covers 'sent until a take holds it'; here it is sent for good. Spec section 10 says what the state reads while a comment is held under an open request or told of, and not what it reads once declined. Options: (a) a declined phase, worded per viewer ('Mia declined' to the people concerned, 'not delivered' to the rest); (b) fall through to the state of the thread's other rows, ignoring declined held rows; (c) keep withheld without an approver.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1855},"end":{"line":1867},"content_hash":"2505c2380656958e11d3b02feac90fd701196ffd31e0787d8b451e83ff3349a5"},"summary":"A declined comment's thread reads 'sent, waiting for the agent' for good","tags":["review","people","spec:10","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T05:05:31.657679Z","id":"eb7b98bb6369701b5e529235d1336bd0b5742792f6d2af9a868d3b80ba5bf21f","body":{"detail":"declined_in asks whether any request from this person for this author on this thread was ever declined. It does not ask whether an approval or a revocation came after it. Seen: Sam declines Mia on thread T. He later allows Mia everywhere (her comments are delivered) and then revokes that. Mia comments again, and the agent's take holds and tells it. T reads 'sent', not 'waiting for Sam's approval'. The same sequence on a thread with no earlier decline reads 'waiting for Sam's approval'. Compare the decision's created/decided time with the row's placeholder_at, or with the newest approval of that author.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1869},"end":{"line":1891},"content_hash":"4916128274d28d9b994f60103babd32393c9cf64a5f74280570cbca9a96d95a8"},"summary":"A decline still counts after a later approval and revocation, so a re-held comment reads sent instead of waiting","tags":["review","people","spec:9.4","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:21:22.866957Z","id":"f68702fa005ef9dcdaae6e19cac49ac624d1a45808c6666a61aa70a718d6255a","body":{"detail":"state_of reports withheld (the target session's person as approver) from placeholder_at, which a take sets when it holds and tells a row, or while an open approval request of that person covers the row's comment author there (a send naming the agent, spec §10). A comment that joins no request (a send naming no agent, a later reply whose author has no open request there, an author held past the request limits) reads sent, waiting on its tier, until the agent's next take. Computing it from visibility at state time would build a Visibility per target session's person inside feedback_states_in, which listings call for every thread (spec §8.7 cost).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1940},"end":{"line":1949},"content_hash":"58070c3dc3bfd0816571f2b422f4f5498db2d6bcc2400ea7e8d12f9c3497b53f"},"summary":"A held row that no open request covers reads sent until a take holds it","supersedes":"514bd451a21893d051884cf0fbeda01ff745214b916836fb1bb26e76e9159282","tags":["people","spec:8.4","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:21:22.867955Z","id":"d9e10887cdadd2188c1a0e14e22fa5637be5844ee1aa068fb99877df4e0aadef","body":{"detail":"Registration derives a name from the repository and branch (spec section 11) without an event; session.start's body is harness, harness_session_id, cwd, transcript_path and pid. The first agent.name then reports previous: <derived name> with no earlier event naming it, and an @name in a comment cannot be tied to its session from the journal alone.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":213},"end":{"line":219},"content_hash":"2531645c1bbef5581474f3318cd70a2a599ab739af3be8223fbe8da994159a5b"},"suggested_fix":"Add name (classed as a name for redaction) to session.start and session.join bodies, and say so in audit spec section 6.8.","summary":"A session's derived name is never recorded, so agent.name's previous names a value the journal never held","supersedes":"adfdd0fa9a4441e78eb88302cb291b32d5c045372647dc73d548363a18b74dbf","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:21:22.868923Z","id":"e01c18367829f04888159f9beae2cfd0917f7064eaa0a0953f40319f13429abb","body":{"detail":"release_owned_in (crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs) selects threads WHERE target_session_id = ?1, and Store::roster groups threads by target_session_id; crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs indexes neither. Both are full scans of threads: off the request hot paths (ends, the reaper, GET /api/agents) and cheap at today's sizes, but linear in all threads ever made.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1637},"end":{"line":1653},"content_hash":"ed1cb058eed0b38a9d4e07ae6c733539b4ca4c1c6388d6f7a4614ccf4b5c1af2"},"suggested_fix":"Add CREATE INDEX threads_by_target ON threads(target_session_id) WHERE target_session_id IS NOT NULL in the next migration.","summary":"Every session end and every roster read scans threads for target_session_id, which has no index","supersedes":"79df4925da3b3b5abf3080c782d1ee3eb8cfda2f3bb61b0c445c75af8fb17a18","tags":["perf","revisit:the next migration on this branch","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:02:04.319970Z","id":"3750505240e92643f760eead3c4285ad620562945aad78892edda039a5165df3","body":{"detail":"hook_row is pid none + name_source derived + repo present; a hook row already named from repository A (say web-chart-axis) that joins again from repository B (a SessionStart after /clear or a resume in another checkout) is renamed api-..., so `@web-chart-axis` stops resolving with no rename by anyone. The comment above says 'named from its harness alone'. register_session (sessions.rs:620-638) has the same condition.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":810},"end":{"line":823},"content_hash":"27996a57e97932459ccc143b4134f39f99763022da30c92616fa83b589f05a58"},"suggested_fix":"Rename only when the current name is the harness-derived one (names::derive(None, None, harness) or one of its candidates).","summary":"A join renames a hook's row on every join that carries a repository, not only a row named from its harness alone","tags":["review","names","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:55:01.440224Z","id":"4bde999e6cbcc202495e513d68f089efa8a56f5244cc1aa9f4e76505769963c6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7a06e2cd","summary":"A registration or join renames only a hook's row (no process) whose derived name is still the one its harness alone gives (names::named_after_harness); spec §11 amended in 7a06e2cd. Evidence: store::sessions::tests::names::a_hooks_join_names_its_row_after_the_repository (a row named from web keeps its name when a join or the adopting shim comes from docs) and names::tests::harness_names_are_told_from_repository_names pass; without the check the store test fails.","supersedes":"3750505240e92643f760eead3c4285ad620562945aad78892edda039a5165df3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:15:33.884860Z","id":"2e4fed83a2db695792cbf222fd0546b5bfad6b7f6477aa9d6d4093bf990690c1","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"d77ce5d28133318c9457e08de5ad656360a7f455fed34bf4257b6f08aa9b6f7c","summary":"Owner decision (2026-10-14): option (a), \"Declined by Mia\" for those concerned; everyone else reads the plain delivery state. Spec section 10 amended.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:15:33.884905Z","id":"5ea9f8eeb412224901f81e8b2a77c59317a7baae6bf552163e075556f4c76c76","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:86cc3ac0","summary":"state_of reads withheld, else declined (StateRow::was_declined, a decline in force), else plain_state, where a told row reads as seen by the agent; FeedbackState::public is the plain state. Evidence: api_approvals::a_declined_thread_reads_declined_to_the_people_concerned_and_plain_to_everyone_else passes (owner and Mia read declined by Sam, Sam reads it with mine; Lucy, no cookie and both agents read sent, then acknowledged after the take; a later comment by Mia stays declined); store::approvals::tests::a_routed_row_reads_withheld_before_any_take passes; Chromium shows 'declined by Sam', 'you declined' and 'seen by the agent' (target/t22/shots-r3/declined-*).","supersedes":"d77ce5d28133318c9457e08de5ad656360a7f455fed34bf4257b6f08aa9b6f7c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:15:33.887865Z","id":"56d0ef54a9907523ca6f850985e4bed7a6cb6fd17e936fb2284b262de13eb722","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:86cc3ac0","summary":"A decline is in force only until an approval of that author by that approver covering the thread is made or revoked after it (declines_in). Evidence: a_declined_thread_reads_declined_to_the_people_concerned_and_plain_to_everyone_else runs the sequence (decline, allow everywhere, take, revoke, a new comment by Mia, take) and the owner then reads withheld by Sam.","supersedes":"eb7b98bb6369701b5e529235d1336bd0b5742792f6d2af9a868d3b80ba5bf21f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:10:34.933970Z","id":"1165c03fc0203d074141af129ad8c3b613de7fdbe46a8ce8d3053b532557ffa3","body":{"detail":"Failure: a home at migration 25 where a person's agent asked a question (a dev home run on this branch) keeps that question's item with recipient NULL after 26, so it sits in the owner's inbox and crates/clax-server/src/inbox.rs render reads its question unscoped (st.question), showing the person's question and answers to the owner, while the person never gets the item. Main's homes hold no person sessions, so they are unaffected. Accepted: migrations 24-26 are unmerged (spec M27), so only a dev home run on this branch can hold such items; questions themselves get their person from their session (questions.person is filled in by the migration).","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":716},"end":{"line":719},"content_hash":"4611fbab17797ab78415d9f71e991c5b174e8ca88f75ff87d6685c7d8474fc79"},"summary":"Migration 26 leaves every existing inbox item the owner's, including question and finished items a connected person's agent made at schema 24-25","supersedes":"3d7ec763a78d801913bbb5d448477ace6c0baf05ff69202a6d1d8615548c9c42","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:10:34.935564Z","id":"9c2f1aab4db22698c249e81357053679e31a0b17b5b57c79a3fa3840e225eea0","body":{"detail":"An invite that expires unredeemed records nothing (audit spec section 6.13 lists only invite.create and invite.revoke). When release_unconnected then returns its person to a plain viewer it sets person = 0 and rights_json = NULL in the sweep or a revoke, so rights set by invite.create's rights or person.rights change with no person.rights event: the journal's last word on that person's rights is wrong.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2276},"end":{"line":2287},"content_hash":"3661554d9ec3b6ade08fbb453c62e14c05eacd1871b109bac087e43dd7492399"},"summary":"An invite's lapse is not recorded, and release_unconnected clears a person's flag and rights without an event","supersedes":"457d6348d5c651eb7038a4d0103b8d083e7175c75dab1047a4b9252a17783c1e","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/elevations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:10:35.648796Z","id":"49bd0874e6d45baf670f7c835da76ccc79a7aa5e94e870ee52415d09e888c064","body":{"detail":"grant_caller_in (crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs) runs given_in for a session-named grant request: for every creator elevation of the session, one viewers read and one rights read for its granter and one artifacts read per artifact it names (at most MAX_ACCESS x MAX_LOCATIONS = 256 per granter, crates/clax-core/src/rights.rs). An agent raised by several creators pays that per granter on every request; nothing is cached across requests. The reads are indexed point lookups and an elevation is one granter's raise, so this was left uncached; a per-generation cache keyed by session would remove it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":86},"end":{"line":118},"content_hash":"6ff8eef57418906969de42e75cf08da974f73461a3d7b1f745983c191cac2131"},"summary":"Each creator's elevation costs store reads on every request of its agent","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/elevations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:06:03.835622Z","id":"ead05fca2972317ec8196bf8188bb76384279c14d6ad0edef053c08b0d7e4305","body":{"detail":"Store::elevate_agent calls record(..) unconditionally. Any connected person can DELETE /api/agents/<handle>/elevate on any live agent and write an agent.elevate {access: null, granter: <them>} row whose description (crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/mod.rs:1271-1279, 'Cleared the elevation of the agent of session ...') names neither the granter nor that the owner's elevation is still there. Observed: Sam's DELETE on an agent he never raised recorded 'Cleared the elevation of the agent of session 01M4THVSTX...' while the owner's elevation stayed. Record only when a row changed (or when the caller had one), and put the granter in the description.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":347},"end":{"line":367},"content_hash":"5bdc3d5514acd338cfda11528e70e28180a9d58c7ec0940e13c6d2ee96311342"},"summary":"A DELETE that removes nothing still records agent.elevate, described as clearing the agent's elevation","tags":["review","audit","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/elevations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:06:03.835669Z","id":"88a0aa0b9188bd890adde2da65f4bfcae4318bad82f2d69f49a7ef9de6d66078","body":{"detail":"Rights::artifact_ids of an empty array is Some({}), so check_creator accepts it with no artifact checked and put_in stores access_json '[]' for that granter. Observed: Sam (creator of nothing relevant) PUT {access: []} on Mia's agent: 200, a session_elevations row (granter Sam, '[]'), and the owner's People card reads 'Raised by Sam until this session ends: ' on Mia's agent. Refuse an empty access (400, or treat it as DELETE).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":157},"end":{"line":174},"content_hash":"98cf8d1315596e21ac647a43089d2885b524167847a1f77f8521769f70bfb048"},"summary":"An empty access [] passes check_creator: any connected person can put an empty raise, shown as 'Raised by <them>', on any agent","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/elevations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:06:03.835709Z","id":"8fc95c4dee7b69ceca28cb098f686c14fb675a9a4f8a8b5019f55e45fd4e5093","body":{"detail":"Mutating crates/clax-server/src/routes/people.rs:776 to fill raisable whatever holds is, and holds_in's owner query (this span) to drop 'person IS NULL', both leave every test in clax-core, clax-server (api_people) green. Neither leaks beyond the participants list or the owner's own reach today, but GET /api/people/me/raises promises raisable empty unless creator and creator true for the owner only on the owner's artifacts (spec §7.4). Add assertions: Mia's ?artifact=<Sam's> raisable is [], and the owner's ?artifact=<Sam's> creator is false.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":123},"end":{"line":146},"content_hash":"9273e5cbf09a0b770f39bb15035401766361e09724c561f9b4d7b9022823da08"},"summary":"Two route rules survive mutation: raisable for a non-creator, and the owner counted as creator of a person's artifact","tags":["review","tests","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/elevations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:23:42.132574Z","id":"ba443929cc9407221556201bc8095e731beb616e26ed92febe879c33935f1221","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7329a263","summary":"Fixed: elevate_agent returns not_raised (404) before recording anything when a removal changes nothing, and the journal names a creator's raise's granter ('Cleared <granter>'s raise of the agent of session ...', crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/mod.rs). Evidence: store::elevations::tests::an_empty_raise_and_a_removal_of_nothing_change_and_record_nothing and api_people::a_raise_answers_a_person_with_their_own_raise_alone pass (no agent.elevate row added); the noop-delete mutation fails 6 tests. CLAX_TEST_BIN=<stable bin> cargo nextest run --workspace: 2198 passed, 10 skipped","supersedes":"ead05fca2972317ec8196bf8188bb76384279c14d6ad0edef053c08b0d7e4305","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/elevations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:23:42.133485Z","id":"119634a19d958b514cf0fa1700b474b2fb9ef93d5b96e508c354620fda400010","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7329a263","summary":"Fixed: elevate_agent refuses an empty access with 400 invalid_rights for every granter, owner included, before anything is stored. Evidence: an_empty_raise_and_a_removal_of_nothing_change_and_record_nothing and a_raise_answers_a_person_with_their_own_raise_alone (PUT {access: []} from Sam and from the owner: 400 invalid_rights) pass; the empty-ok mutation fails 4 tests.","supersedes":"88a0aa0b9188bd890adde2da65f4bfcae4318bad82f2d69f49a7ef9de6d66078","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/elevations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:23:42.134428Z","id":"cdd327aebd2fe80b237e18884f97339bc073d7fc7850cd4baa1f75a66dba9ffb","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7329a263","summary":"Fixed: api_people::only_the_creator_reads_what_a_raise_could_give_and_reach pins both rules (Mia, on Sam's artifact with her agent watching it, and the owner read creator false, holds null, raisable []). Evidence: it passes, and both mutations now fail it: raisable filled for every caller (2 failing) and owner holds at a person's artifact (2 failing).","supersedes":"8fc95c4dee7b69ceca28cb098f686c14fb675a9a4f8a8b5019f55e45fd4e5093","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:23:42.136280Z","id":"bfbea9c19c1d88bffb0afb242d144103241ffddecb3c6f85a71ad20a25b63df8","body":{"detail":"An invite that expires unredeemed records nothing (audit spec section 6.13 lists only invite.create and invite.revoke). When release_unconnected then returns its person to a plain viewer it sets person = 0 and rights_json = NULL in the sweep or a revoke, so rights set by invite.create's rights or person.rights change with no person.rights event: the journal's last word on that person's rights is wrong.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2272},"end":{"line":2300},"content_hash":"21c6a12d5da90d6d5c16c6ff28c6c0e9001be65589ae337c9755bc64876f5506"},"summary":"An invite's lapse is not recorded, and release_unconnected clears a person's flag and rights without an event","supersedes":"9c2f1aab4db22698c249e81357053679e31a0b17b5b57c79a3fa3840e225eea0","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:23:53.536958Z","id":"5c61f8cdc9ca61119fe6d45b1d3a6d5e72cb29c3f046d72133c490117747feb6","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"bfbea9c19c1d88bffb0afb242d144103241ffddecb3c6f85a71ad20a25b63df8","summary":"Partly addressed by 7329a263: a release now drops every raise the released person gave, each recorded as agent.elevate with reason person_released; the release itself (the person flag and rights cleared) is still not recorded.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/elevations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:06:18.516177Z","id":"7a1e5ef9584b07842a55f049a3a0020be141b208bd7e6c37726478ef4a049edf","body":{"detail":"grant_caller_in (crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs) runs given_in for a session-named grant request: for every creator elevation of the session, one viewers read and one rights read for its granter and one artifacts read per artifact it names (at most MAX_ACCESS x MAX_LOCATIONS = 256 per granter, crates/clax-core/src/rights.rs). An agent raised by several creators pays that per granter on every request; nothing is cached across requests. The reads are indexed point lookups and an elevation is one granter's raise, so this was left uncached; a per-generation cache keyed by session would remove it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":91},"end":{"line":123},"content_hash":"6ff8eef57418906969de42e75cf08da974f73461a3d7b1f745983c191cac2131"},"summary":"Each creator's elevation costs store reads on every request of its agent","supersedes":"49bd0874e6d45baf670f7c835da76ccc79a7aa5e94e870ee52415d09e888c064","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:06:18.519756Z","id":"2d21f56a4b4511fc3bf65ec7d3c434c1d2152d0b8aa2110bd78a7da8c8793b53","body":{"detail":"Failure: a home at migration 25 where a person's agent asked a question (a dev home run on this branch) keeps that question's item with recipient NULL after 26, so it sits in the owner's inbox and crates/clax-server/src/inbox.rs render reads its question unscoped (st.question), showing the person's question and answers to the owner, while the person never gets the item. Main's homes hold no person sessions, so they are unaffected. Accepted: migrations 24-26 are unmerged (spec M27), so only a dev home run on this branch can hold such items; questions themselves get their person from their session (questions.person is filled in by the migration).","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":717},"end":{"line":720},"content_hash":"4611fbab17797ab78415d9f71e991c5b174e8ca88f75ff87d6685c7d8474fc79"},"summary":"Migration 26 leaves every existing inbox item the owner's, including question and finished items a connected person's agent made at schema 24-25","supersedes":"1165c03fc0203d074141af129ad8c3b613de7fdbe46a8ce8d3053b532557ffa3","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:30:59.641143Z","id":"a46997617b3ca1555833ce9fa3888eca2a5786df759a1ea426a412e73a39b949","body":{"detail":"Failure: Mia's thread sent to Sam's agent; the agent takes (the row is held and told); Sam approves. Before the approval every visitor reads the plain state acknowledged (since = the take). release_told clears placeholder_at, so plain_state (crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs:2062-2126) no longer counts the row as told: a LAN viewer's or anonymous GET of the thread reads 'sent' again, since = the comment's time, with no new comment (seen in Chromium: Lucy's card goes from 'seen by the agent' to 'sent, waiting for the agent' on reload). apply_decision (crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs:557) wakes the target, and its take publishes a feedback_state (acknowledged, tier 'wait', a new since) to /api/events for a thread whose newest comment has not changed; for a waiting agent or a push tier that event follows the decision at once. Turning the owner's *unconnected switch on does the same: anonymous /api/events heard 'delivered' (queue) 1 ms after the POST /api/approvals. Spec 2026-10-08 section 10 (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md:1480-1484) says a decision 'publishes none' and 'no one else sees a decision as an event or a change of timing'. The test's nothing_of_before (crates/clax-server/tests/api_approvals.rs:2447) checks a decline only. Options: keep a released row reading as seen by the agent at its told time until delivered, and publish no feedback_state when the plain state does not change; or amend section 10 to accept that an approval shows as a delivery.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":182},"end":{"line":241},"content_hash":"94a207d7c6e73a3c8362a070b86f25c8ec00343a90bd1a9aa325041e617b7907"},"summary":"An approval is visible to LAN viewers and anonymous callers: the released told row falls back from 'seen by the agent' to 'sent', and the next take publishes a second feedback_state","tags":["review","people","spec:10","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:30:59.641345Z","id":"b30c668d8eb95df9d36f3b06830c53f8089d80a611a4ff0d571465a3528ee931","body":{"detail":"Failure: any comment held by a take. plain_state reads a told row as acknowledged with tier_of(r), and a told row has no delivery_tier, so the state is {state: acknowledged, tier: null}. Every delivered or acknowledged row carries its tier (piggyback, wait, stop_hook, queue, inject). Seen on a scratch daemon: Sam's own thread to his agent reads acknowledged/tier 'wait' to a LAN viewer; Mia's thread held by the same agent reads acknowledged/tier null to the LAN viewer, to no cookie and in the anonymous /api/events stream. For a stop_hook or queue target the held thread also skips 'delivered'. The shell's label is the same ('seen by the agent'), but the API and events give LAN viewers what spec section 10 (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md:1476-1478) says they never read: that the comment was withheld. Give a told row's plain state the tier the take used (or the session's waiting tier).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2062},"end":{"line":2126},"content_hash":"a0533624a4da2fb890b133c202028edbfc45564278e5ee3bcb0615562626d066"},"summary":"The plain state of a held take reads acknowledged with tier null, which no delivered take has, so every visitor and every feedback_state event marks a withheld comment","tags":["review","people","spec:10","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:18:37.733839Z","id":"fd012b6c8af1990436fa7032a7fbe0d316dce2765f18ab52e07b50abbc78d4e0","body":{"detail":"The owner's selection, verbatim: 'Only \"sent\"'. LAN viewers, anonymous views and /api/events never see delivery progress for a sent thread: no acknowledged, delivered, tier or since change. A thread reads \"sent to <agent>\"; agent replies still appear as ordinary replies. Anonymous events for delivery state stop entirely; they still get new comments and replies. So the released row's fallback to sent, the second feedback_state at the take after a decision, and a told row's null tier (record b30c668d) reach no visitor. Stated in docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md section 10 (Who reads which), sections 17 and 18, and section 19 item 9.","kind":"comment","references":"a46997617b3ca1555833ce9fa3888eca2a5786df759a1ea426a412e73a39b949","summary":"Decided (owner, 2026-10-14): 'Only \"sent\"': LAN viewers and anonymous callers never read a sent thread's delivery progress","tags":["status:decided","spec:10","owner-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:34:34.438074Z","id":"f7946e2c662b96abc5d3a491bb56c5b63408819e0525d65bdc7583bf9b197b58","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:628b724a","summary":"Fixed: LAN viewers and anonymous callers read no delivery state (Delivery::view of DeliveryViewer::Visitor sees no row, crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs), /api/events carries no feedback_state, and thread events carry none. cargo nextest run -p clax-server -E 'test(=api_approvals::visitors_read_sent_and_nothing_of_any_decision)' passes: a decline, an approval, a revocation and the *unconnected switch turned on, with the agents' takes after each, change nothing in Lucy's or no-cookie's thread view and put no event of the thread on anonymous /api/events or Lucy's /api/stream. Mutation M2 (a visitor reads every row) and M9 (/api/events carries delivery events) are caught by it.","supersedes":"a46997617b3ca1555833ce9fa3888eca2a5786df759a1ea426a412e73a39b949","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:34:34.439372Z","id":"75389682b5da15f0a677f03f652413bbe6e9d0f4edaaca70fadbc5ad80b00843","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:628b724a","summary":"Fixed: a told row's state (acknowledged, tier null) is read only by the readers of that row: the owner, its approver, its content's author and the agent it was sent to, each of whom reads the hold anyway; LAN viewers, anonymous callers, other people and other agents read no delivery state. api_approvals::visitors_read_sent_and_nothing_of_any_decision and api_approvals::agents_read_the_state_of_threads_sent_to_them_alone pass.","supersedes":"b30c668d8eb95df9d36f3b06830c53f8089d80a611a4ff0d571465a3528ee931","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:34:34.446728Z","id":"5dbaa32411558a7c288b19f7a8000bccb45c4c22af84898b93387b020986ad18","body":{"detail":"state_of reports withheld (the target session's person as approver) from placeholder_at, which a take sets when it holds and tells a row, or while an open approval request of that person covers the row's comment author there (a send naming the agent, spec §10). A comment that joins no request (a send naming no agent, a later reply whose author has no open request there, an author held past the request limits) reads sent, waiting on its tier, until the agent's next take. Computing it from visibility at state time would build a Visibility per target session's person inside feedback_states_in, which listings call for every thread (spec §8.7 cost).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2064},"end":{"line":2073},"content_hash":"c65b0f968699e8cc0c38af1592e8e7b90d060df9c18a71599f611feba41154f4"},"summary":"A held row that no open request covers reads sent until a take holds it","supersedes":"f68702fa005ef9dcdaae6e19cac49ac624d1a45808c6666a61aa70a718d6255a","tags":["people","spec:8.4","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:34:34.459173Z","id":"19f483ce4918d760c6decbeb30aa5e631248615690f969f79a2e59fca21b8291","body":{"detail":"Delivery::changed_for tells a person of a change only when their rows' newest time (StateRow::stamp: created, delivered, acknowledged, told, untargeted, last sent, session end) is the thread's newest. A change that sets no time (a watch armed or disarmed, which changes a sent row's waiting tier; a codex queue failure; a handoff that keeps a row's times) is published to the owner but to no person, so a connected person's open card keeps the old tier until the thread is fetched again. The owner hears every change.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2024},"end":{"line":2031},"content_hash":"a0352ae277d3e1bd4888457d701a8ee4f88820b6751df49739bcfa70ab5c97a5"},"summary":"A change that stamps no row reaches only the owner live; a person sees it at their next fetch","tags":["people","spec:10","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:56:08.271456Z","id":"0e7b9b6c9a52d1bcbed7dfde2f4fe44fc12357c9ae3efa91328f1f5eef06c61b","body":{"detail":"Failure: a fresh home where an agent reads before the owner's browser first loads (register a session, publish, then open the artifact in the owner's browser and comment): the agent's feedback reads author 'Alex (not connected)'. Store::owner_viewer (crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs:540-557) INSERTs the owner row without calling visibility_changed(), so Store::connected() (crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs:447-467) keeps the Connected it cached at that generation, read with no owner, and Connected::label (crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs:342-348) suffixes the owner's own name in feedback, comments_read and hook payloads until something else bumps the generation (an approval, an invite) or the daemon restarts. This is why web/e2e/comment-loop.spec.ts:44 and web/e2e/whole-comment.spec.ts:58 fail on a fresh worker daemon (record 31593a13) and pass after other tests ran there. main has no such mark (git grep NOT_CONNECTED main is empty) and passes both specs. Fix: call self.visibility_changed() in owner_viewer's write (only when the INSERT made a row), with a store test that reads connected(), makes the owner and reads it again. Checked: with that one line both specs pass alone (3 passed), and fail again (3 failed) with the line removed.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":540},"end":{"line":557},"content_hash":"571fa168230ca7f5a644c8b67833279de7f840f3637ab1d6dec0c13fba0cd47f"},"summary":"Making the owner's viewer row does not bump the visibility generation, so a Connected cached before it marks the owner '(not connected)' to agents","tags":["review","people","spec:9.6","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:56:08.271893Z","id":"65115b61caf59c714db5ba09e9ecb2002b362618e9dca9b9e197d4fc63806a06","body":{"detail":"A watch armed or disarmed, a codex queue failure and a handoff that keeps times change only the tier text of a sent row ('waiting on the agent finishing its current work' and the like); every decision reaches its approver and author (publish_decision), so no person keeps a stale hold, decline or approval from these. Two gaps remain: (1) a comment a page wrote has several authors (page_authors), and a decision's parties name only the request's author, so the page's other authors read the row (Delivery::sees) but hear nothing of the decision until they fetch; code reading. (2) The hub's repeat suppression (crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs project, ch.delivery) remembers the last state sent per recipient key and channel, not what the client applied, so a reader whose client dropped a state (a new thread's state arriving before its thread event: record on crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs:539-573) or that fetched after an unsent change is not sent that state again.","kind":"comment","references":"19f483ce4918d760c6decbeb30aa5e631248615690f969f79a2e59fca21b8291","summary":"Assessment: the unstamped changes only move a waiting tier, which misleads no one; two cases do leave a person reading a wrong state","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:22:24.390371Z","id":"968a4bad0b5113873f756b0c3e80b22292203de4e380a4b1e747f0c4f5813926","body":{"detail":"approve_owner_on_connect is the single approval made without a browser (spec section 21 item 3, M15). It is bounded to the connect: once per grant, within OWNER_ANSWER_SECS (10 minutes) of the tokens' issue, never once the person has made or revoked any approval of the owner (409 owner_answered, so a revocation in People stands; 409 answer_closed after the window), replays refused by accept_t first. Only the continuation token says it, never the access token agents sign with (crates/clax-server/tests/api_grants.rs a_connected_machine_approves_the_owner_through_its_continuation), and clax connect refuses on an agent channel (crates/clax-cli/tests/connect.rs connect_refuses_on_an_agent_channel). What remains: a process of the person's that reads remote.json within those ten minutes, before clax connect answers, could answer yes for them; the person can revoke it in People, and that revocation is final. Tests: store::people::tests::connecting_records_the_persons_approval_of_the_owner_once, the_answer_about_the_owner_never_overrides_the_person.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1480},"end":{"line":1572},"content_hash":"d5ef04715b7251bf982fd51818c94f17a2b0b3b2dd3450f46854211db24ca24d"},"summary":"The person's approval of the owner is recorded without a browser once, at connect: an agent present then could answer for the person","supersedes":"ac87751d1a8a52942ba49cc5a0775c7d47efaf8f2af9b32724233d490ef2834b","tags":["security","spec:6.3","spec:21","M15","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:22:24.391793Z","id":"db2b92e84f37710c8ddb5ff6f993e0e5a854f18187c6319bc5a009c932d99be4","body":{"detail":"For flow invite the grant's events carry grant_id and person but not invite_id, so the journal cannot join invite.create to the grant made from it except by person and time; invites.grant_id holds the link only while the row lives.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1091},"end":{"line":1105},"content_hash":"a055d17fb6d13921d9565129c8f0b702f534ab8d657151596b97465c24004831"},"suggested_fix":"Add invite_id to grant.request (flow invite) and to audit spec section 6.13 and multi-person spec section 20.2.","summary":"An invite-flow grant.request and grant.approve do not name the invite they redeemed","supersedes":"cbc85f9a803d271af33bf349533f7dddba36c4b96f24ceee8fe1611fb86a5a72","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:22:24.393139Z","id":"d84547101f6be54ada9cde90858e5c3cb8ae05eebe901de48c2c656c97c161fb","body":{"detail":"An invite that expires unredeemed records nothing (audit spec section 6.13 lists only invite.create and invite.revoke). When release_unconnected then returns its person to a plain viewer it sets person = 0 and rights_json = NULL in the sweep or a revoke, so rights set by invite.create's rights or person.rights change with no person.rights event: the journal's last word on that person's rights is wrong.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2276},"end":{"line":2304},"content_hash":"21c6a12d5da90d6d5c16c6ff28c6c0e9001be65589ae337c9755bc64876f5506"},"summary":"An invite's lapse is not recorded, and release_unconnected clears a person's flag and rights without an event","supersedes":"bfbea9c19c1d88bffb0afb242d144103241ffddecb3c6f85a71ad20a25b63df8","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:22:24.394526Z","id":"9ff7c7c21f80bf4b33878d0c83f959688219648381ee99d75de00406c2cf89a2","body":{"detail":"state_of reports withheld (the target session's person as approver) from placeholder_at, which a take sets when it holds and tells a row, or while an open approval request of that person covers the row's comment author there (a send naming the agent, spec §10). A comment that joins no request (a send naming no agent, a later reply whose author has no open request there, an author held past the request limits) reads sent, waiting on its tier, until the agent's next take. Computing it from visibility at state time would build a Visibility per target session's person inside feedback_states_in, which listings call for every thread (spec §8.7 cost).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2079},"end":{"line":2088},"content_hash":"c65b0f968699e8cc0c38af1592e8e7b90d060df9c18a71599f611feba41154f4"},"summary":"A held row that no open request covers reads sent until a take holds it","supersedes":"5dbaa32411558a7c288b19f7a8000bccb45c4c22af84898b93387b020986ad18","tags":["people","spec:8.4","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:22:24.402958Z","id":"2703ce8e69ca16cf6c48ef4a1bd8c19546648333ad2f6978a692bb454e843869","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c84e0d7a","summary":"Fixed: Store::owner_viewer bumps the visibility generation when its INSERT makes the owner's row, as does the invite flow's owner row (crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs, InvitePerson::Owner). store::viewers::tests::making_the_owners_row_after_an_agent_read_connects_the_owner passes (connected() read first, then the row: the owner's name reads 'Alex', not marked); store::approvals::tests::every_visibility_change_bumps_the_generation_once now expects the owner-row invite's bump. web/e2e/comment-loop.spec.ts (2 passed) and whole-comment.spec.ts (1 passed) pass alone, and the full Playwright run passes (414 passed, 48 skipped). Removing either bump is caught by those store tests. The other writes of owner or person rows (a person by invite or grant, a viewer made a person, a released person, an owner claim) already bump.","supersedes":"0e7b9b6c9a52d1bcbed7dfde2f4fe44fc12357c9ae3efa91328f1f5eef06c61b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:22:24.410600Z","id":"9d4a110b5dd8b549a3b269babcfa5ba8278cb9a5d40d656251ce24154b0d5a48","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"19f483ce4918d760c6decbeb30aa5e631248615690f969f79a2e59fca21b8291","summary":"Two gaps reply 65115b61 named are closed in c84e0d7a: a decision now reaches the content's co-authors (Delivery::decision_people), and the hub forgets what it sent a person when a stream of theirs subscribes or resumes. The tier staleness this record describes stays.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:22:24.461841Z","id":"c9b296f35d9a9cda7a6d47da94276baed30c5a23026585954e095336dacf5236","body":{"detail":"Delivery::changed_for tells a person of a change only when their rows' newest time (StateRow::stamp: created, delivered, acknowledged, told, untargeted, last sent, session end) is the thread's newest. A change that sets no time (a watch armed or disarmed, which changes a sent row's waiting tier; a codex queue failure; a handoff that keeps a row's times) is published to the owner but to no person, so a connected person's open card keeps the old tier until the thread is fetched again. The owner hears every change.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2039},"end":{"line":2046},"content_hash":"a0352ae277d3e1bd4888457d701a8ee4f88820b6751df49739bcfa70ab5c97a5"},"summary":"A change that stamps no row reaches only the owner live; a person sees it at their next fetch","supersedes":"19f483ce4918d760c6decbeb30aa5e631248615690f969f79a2e59fca21b8291","tags":["people","spec:10","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T04:35:19.106495Z","id":"0c8e500238b5f777fab10f129156289c84b5a7bcb4564ebc0db2647ae3bbae14","body":{"detail":"state_of reports withheld (the target session's person as approver) from placeholder_at, which a take sets when it holds and tells a row, or while an open approval request of that person covers the row's comment author there (a send naming the agent, spec §10). A comment that joins no request (a send naming no agent, a later reply whose author has no open request there, an author held past the request limits) reads sent, waiting on its tier, until the agent's next take. Computing it from visibility at state time would build a Visibility per target session's person inside feedback_states_in, which listings call for every thread (spec §8.7 cost).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2120},"end":{"line":2129},"content_hash":"c65b0f968699e8cc0c38af1592e8e7b90d060df9c18a71599f611feba41154f4"},"summary":"A held row that no open request covers reads sent until a take holds it","supersedes":"9ff7c7c21f80bf4b33878d0c83f959688219648381ee99d75de00406c2cf89a2","tags":["people","spec:8.4","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T04:35:19.108061Z","id":"960818583267ea3b810a357ceaed86e63826dd2c43a42e704e83a339ecf64f35","body":{"detail":"Delivery::changed_for tells a person of a change only when their rows' newest time (StateRow::stamp: created, delivered, acknowledged, told, untargeted, last sent, session end) is the thread's newest. A change that sets no time (a watch armed or disarmed, which changes a sent row's waiting tier; a codex queue failure; a handoff that keeps a row's times) is published to the owner but to no person, so a connected person's open card keeps the old tier until the thread is fetched again. The owner hears every change.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2080},"end":{"line":2087},"content_hash":"a0352ae277d3e1bd4888457d701a8ee4f88820b6751df49739bcfa70ab5c97a5"},"summary":"A change that stamps no row reaches only the owner live; a person sees it at their next fetch","supersedes":"c9b296f35d9a9cda7a6d47da94276baed30c5a23026585954e095336dacf5236","tags":["people","spec:10","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T04:35:19.112501Z","id":"cf81562b9fbd848071e907d636d5e49d79173eb48c9c9a94ddda6246f88b6660","body":{"detail":"Held::finish stamps placeholder_at on no_access rows (crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs:700-706) to tell the session once, as spec section 7.5 says (held as withheld). Two consequences: StateRow::waits_for_approval then reports the thread as waiting for the person's approval, which no approval releases (the person's rights or a narrowing must change); and if the session may read the artifact again while a body on the row is still withheld, the row counts as told, so the session never gets the withheld-comments line for it (it is still delivered once approved). A complete version keeps a separate told-of-no-access marker (a column) so each condition is told once on its own and the state can say 'no access'.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":700},"end":{"line":706},"content_hash":"f1df07ff057eb934bf5fbfc7d476aed5e966ed6ba0081ae009d1c8253a6e8cff"},"summary":"A row held because its session may no longer read the artifact shares placeholder_at with withheld bodies, so its thread reads waiting for approval and is never told as withheld later","tags":["people","spec:7.5","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:10:36.209456Z","id":"27748a78b6a6de36de3e756d68fcb208f7f3c9f75ef880dd015480e78ab1b297","body":{"detail":"Failure: a home at migration 25 where a person's agent asked a question (a dev home run on this branch) keeps that question's item with recipient NULL after 26, so it sits in the owner's inbox and crates/clax-server/src/inbox.rs render reads its question unscoped (st.question), showing the person's question and answers to the owner, while the person never gets the item. Main's homes hold no person sessions, so they are unaffected. Accepted: migrations 24-26 are unmerged (spec M27), so only a dev home run on this branch can hold such items; questions themselves get their person from their session (questions.person is filled in by the migration).","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":718},"end":{"line":721},"content_hash":"4611fbab17797ab78415d9f71e991c5b174e8ca88f75ff87d6685c7d8474fc79"},"summary":"Migration 26 leaves every existing inbox item the owner's, including question and finished items a connected person's agent made at schema 24-25","supersedes":"2d21f56a4b4511fc3bf65ec7d3c434c1d2152d0b8aa2110bd78a7da8c8793b53","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:10:36.211261Z","id":"30530f99bbfe9d3e42558b5abf8ece7da078cba354d4b87a633f903660d92f97","body":{"detail":"state_of reports withheld (the target session's person as approver) from placeholder_at, which a take sets when it holds and tells a row, or while an open approval request of that person covers the row's comment author there (a send naming the agent, spec §10). A comment that joins no request (a send naming no agent, a later reply whose author has no open request there, an author held past the request limits) reads sent, waiting on its tier, until the agent's next take. Computing it from visibility at state time would build a Visibility per target session's person inside feedback_states_in, which listings call for every thread (spec §8.7 cost).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2158},"end":{"line":2167},"content_hash":"c65b0f968699e8cc0c38af1592e8e7b90d060df9c18a71599f611feba41154f4"},"summary":"A held row that no open request covers reads sent until a take holds it","supersedes":"0c8e500238b5f777fab10f129156289c84b5a7bcb4564ebc0db2647ae3bbae14","tags":["people","spec:8.4","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:10:36.212902Z","id":"9d50c0714f9a9df3448e06edde2c7a74b0cec326ba950b84a3aab88d3f1b1afd","body":{"detail":"Delivery::changed_for tells a person of a change only when their rows' newest time (StateRow::stamp: created, delivered, acknowledged, told, untargeted, last sent, session end) is the thread's newest. A change that sets no time (a watch armed or disarmed, which changes a sent row's waiting tier; a codex queue failure; a handoff that keeps a row's times) is published to the owner but to no person, so a connected person's open card keeps the old tier until the thread is fetched again. The owner hears every change.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2118},"end":{"line":2125},"content_hash":"a0352ae277d3e1bd4888457d701a8ee4f88820b6751df49739bcfa70ab5c97a5"},"summary":"A change that stamps no row reaches only the owner live; a person sees it at their next fetch","supersedes":"960818583267ea3b810a357ceaed86e63826dd2c43a42e704e83a339ecf64f35","tags":["people","spec:10","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:10:36.244995Z","id":"3d17f304fcd62b09108ec29b42142fdddef8c45c8b00fb90221d1b726d7ed632","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:da2ba575","summary":"Fixed: holds for lost access now use their own column, feedback.no_access_at (migration 25), cleared when the session may read again. Delivery::view reads them as the no_access phase for the owner and the agent's person only (plain for authors and the agent, nothing for visitors), never as waiting for an approval unless a request is open; access back tells the withheld line and delivers once approved; losing access again tells again. Evidence: cargo nextest run -p clax-core -E 'test(a_no_access_hold_has_its_own_state_and_access_back_tells_the_withheld_line) | test(a_row_held_for_lost_access_reads_no_access_before_any_approval)' passes; api_visibility::a_persons_agent_that_may_no_longer_read_a_page_is_told_once_on_every_tier passes (owner's browser reads no_access, Mia's reads sent; access back: the withheld line, then delivered once approved, on piggyback, stop_hook, prompt_hook, wait and inject); the first commit alone passes clax-core, clax-server and clax-cli (2045 tests); workspace nextest 2259 passed.","supersedes":"cf81562b9fbd848071e907d636d5e49d79173eb48c9c9a94ddda6246f88b6660","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:49:30.467719Z","id":"4a02c39d152f433b92d6e0d6c2ecf90dd21166cc795a0874cdfa0b7286782e93","body":{"detail":"Failure: with an open approval request in the owner's inbox (an `approval` item, unread), pressing Mark all read in the shell's Inbox or in the extension panel's Inbox tab (web/extension/src/panel/InboxTab.svelte:125-135, `inbox-mark-all` -> POST /api/inbox/read {all: true}) marks it read while the request is still open: the MarkAll UPDATE here filters on recipient, read_at, text and upto, never on kind. The one-item route does the same (MARK_READ, line 529), so the row's dot also marks an undecided request read. The item only turns unread again if new withheld content joins the request (approval_reannounced). The panel's own row press leaves it unread (InboxTab.svelte:155-158), so only these two paths break the rule. A panel-side filter cannot fix `all: true`; the rule belongs in the store, which serves the shell, the panel and the CLI alike.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":365},"end":{"line":385},"content_hash":"fe14f9a6ef5f30ed890b36875641b649038f88fbcc4266ab7a53c5fd9a3faa58"},"suggested_fix":"In MarkAll and MARK_READ, leave out `kind = 'approval'` items whose request is still open (approval_closed marks them read once decided). Add a store test: an open approval item stays unread through mark-all and a one-item mark, and is read after the decision.","summary":"Mark all read marks open approval items read, against spec 2026-10-08 section 9.5 ('approval items, unread until decided')","tags":["review","spec:9.5","task:23","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T04:05:29.982362Z","id":"2e9ad895381344fa72722489a9e70c57011ca0e5f3f1833cba983ef5e82ced8d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:21d2a440","summary":"Mark all read (Shape::MarkAll) and MARK_READ now leave out an approval item whose request is open (UNDECIDED); deciding or withdrawing still reads it (approval_closed). Shell, panel and CLI inherit it through the inbox routes; the read dot is disabled on such a row and Mark all read is offered only while something readable is unread. Evidence: store::inbox::tests::an_undecided_approval_item_stays_unread_whoever_marks_it, api_approvals::an_approval_item_stays_unread_until_decided_whoever_marks_it (unread count unchanged after both marks), Panel.test 'Mark all read leaves an undecided approval request unread...', inbox-page.test 'offers Mark all read only while...', inbox-row.test, and the chrome-overlay LAN e2e (Mark all read in the panel, the request still unread on the daemon) pass; cargo nextest -p clax-core -p clax-server -p clax-cli: 2034 passed.","supersedes":"4a02c39d152f433b92d6e0d6c2ecf90dd21166cc795a0874cdfa0b7286782e93","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:30:31.538143Z","id":"9c75976cb60ff3069031f9208a0c0968718bc54656da9a7fef8b39062b65cf8b","body":{"detail":"Failure: Mia comments on a thread sent to Sam's agent; Sam has not approved Mia; a take holds the comment and tells the agent (placeholder_at set; no request open, no decline). Sam then narrows the agent so it may no longer read the artifact, and its next take stamps no_access_at. waits_for_approval (these lines) now excludes the row because no_access_at is set, and Delivery::view's knows closure (feedback.rs:2072-2076) hides no_access from Mia, so state_of (feedback.rs:2254-2304) falls through to plain_state, where a told row reads acknowledged. Mia's thread changes from 'waiting for Sam's approval' to 'seen by the agent': false (the agent never saw the body), different from spec 2026-10-08 section 10's Withheld reading (a told row with no decline in force is Withheld for the author), and a visible change that follows Sam's change of his agent's rights. The unit test a_row_held_for_lost_access_reads_no_access_before_any_approval (feedback.rs:2451-2471) asserts Mia reads Acknowledged. docs/contract.md:1994 says others read 'sent', which this case contradicts.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1952},"end":{"line":1958},"content_hash":"7ef409aa95a92560ab38fbdd910a2f3c390abae807cf2d6bf1200e0a70573fe6"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the no_access_at exclusion only for readers whom knows lets read no_access (the owner and the agent's person); for everyone else evaluate waits_for_approval as if no_access_at were unset, so the author keeps reading 'waiting for Sam's approval'. Assert that in the unit test and correct docs/contract.md:1994.","summary":"An author reads 'seen by the agent' instead of 'waiting for <approver>'s approval' once the approver's agent loses access","tags":["review","task:24","people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:30:31.538502Z","id":"a7145e762a23423e7fff8abe8a88100d6ceb5d99b8aaa8933d5b5fc8661ede5f","body":{"detail":"state_of checks waits_for_approval before lost_access, and waits_for_approval is true whenever `requested` is, whatever no_access_at says. When an agent with an open approval request loses read access to the artifact, the owner and the agent's person keep reading 'waiting for Sam's approval'; Sam approving delivers nothing until the agent may read the page again, and nothing tells Sam the agent lost access. The no_access reading (docs/contract.md:1994, 3142) applies only when no request is open.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2275},"end":{"line":2301},"content_hash":"402e8a70d88099259c837f59fad61969049fe36a3cf332e1bf3276436371ad3f"},"suggested_fix":"For readers that knows admits, check lost_access before the withheld reading (or let a lost-access row's withheld reading carry the no_access state), and add the open-request case to a_no_access_hold_has_its_own_state_and_access_back_tells_the_withheld_line.","summary":"With an approval request open, a hold for lost access reads 'waiting for <person>'s approval', never no_access","tags":["review","task:24","people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:30:31.538710Z","id":"97f30b63590f74dfe9caa2ccbf03624fffe0988caf9151a7616a6773b106a141","body":{"detail":"da2ba575 adds `ALTER TABLE feedback ADD COLUMN no_access_at TEXT` to the migration that already added placeholder_at. A home migrated by an earlier build of this branch (~/.clax-dev from just dev or just watch, or a scratch home kept across builds) already counts that migration as applied, never gets the column, and fails every take and delivery-state read with 'no such column: f.no_access_at' (TAKE_FEEDBACK and FEEDBACK_STATES read it). Homes built from main are unaffected, since this migration is not on main.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":678},"end":{"line":678},"content_hash":"6069d2b6053a37ec74f7d44a1bd0144bde67a8b97016989a13cae33602e049ca"},"suggested_fix":"Either accept it and say so in the branch's merge notes (dev homes are rebuilt), or move the column to its own migration before merge.","summary":"no_access_at is added inside the branch's existing migration rather than as a new one","tags":["review","task:24","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:30:31.538835Z","id":"1e6477e81aa6b7dfa923875df942a113159b483ec992a6f5b970d4cebe6024fa","body":{"detail":"comment_agent gives the owner's agents person = the owner's public ID (agent_person_id's COALESCE in COMMENT_SELECT and COMMENTS_OF_MANY), while thread.owner.person is null for the owner's agents in the same thread view (checked: a LAN viewer's GET /api/artifacts/<aid>/threads carried owner.person null and comments[1].agent.person 'u_…' for the same agent). person_name comes from crate::feedback::person_name, the payload-safe form (display_name: '\"' and ':' become spaces, cut to 40 characters), and is what browsers print in web/shell/src/view/sidebar-model.ts authorLabel and the extension panel, so a person named 'Dr: Who' reads 'Dr  Who's agent'. Neither leaks anything section 18 withholds; they are inconsistencies a client has to know about.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":572},"end":{"line":585},"content_hash":"f1b05d3707fa9799aa65b2b3e348ce3c4e6e4232296765f784ee7b2fc1252cfa"},"suggested_fix":"Use one convention for the owner in both fields, and give browsers the display name as stored (the agent filter already rewrites author lines for agents).","summary":"comment.agent names the owner by public ID and person_name by its payload-safe form, unlike thread.owner in the same view","tags":["review","task:24","people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:58:13.897685Z","id":"f7b7275e0e01c4ca1e44d2659416e3e4064fa4c310535285864d559efbec90db","body":{"detail":"state_of reports withheld (the target session's person as approver) from placeholder_at, which a take sets when it holds and tells a row, or while an open approval request of that person covers the row's comment author there (a send naming the agent, spec §10). A comment that joins no request (a send naming no agent, a later reply whose author has no open request there, an author held past the request limits) reads sent, waiting on its tier, until the agent's next take. Computing it from visibility at state time would build a Visibility per target session's person inside feedback_states_in, which listings call for every thread (spec §8.7 cost).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2156},"end":{"line":2165},"content_hash":"c65b0f968699e8cc0c38af1592e8e7b90d060df9c18a71599f611feba41154f4"},"summary":"A held row that no open request covers reads sent until a take holds it","supersedes":"30530f99bbfe9d3e42558b5abf8ece7da078cba354d4b87a633f903660d92f97","tags":["people","spec:8.4","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:58:13.899864Z","id":"4efdda9acca40ae1f1a8fd869b728897e018f04e73e7207bcf56e5240a9cebd2","body":{"detail":"Delivery::changed_for tells a person of a change only when their rows' newest time (StateRow::stamp: created, delivered, acknowledged, told, untargeted, last sent, session end) is the thread's newest. A change that sets no time (a watch armed or disarmed, which changes a sent row's waiting tier; a codex queue failure; a handoff that keeps a row's times) is published to the owner but to no person, so a connected person's open card keeps the old tier until the thread is fetched again. The owner hears every change.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2116},"end":{"line":2123},"content_hash":"a0352ae277d3e1bd4888457d701a8ee4f88820b6751df49739bcfa70ab5c97a5"},"summary":"A change that stamps no row reaches only the owner live; a person sees it at their next fetch","supersedes":"9d50c0714f9a9df3448e06edde2c7a74b0cec326ba950b84a3aab88d3f1b1afd","tags":["people","spec:10","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:58:13.966282Z","id":"01e0d2228fec95346ab2730cf183ab566a2df5271f6662ce3f48f9e247811f9b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:af61599b","summary":"Fixed: waits_for_approval no longer excludes rows held for lost access, so an author reads a told or requested row as 'waiting for Sam's approval' whatever the agent's access; a row held only for lost access reads plain 'sent' to everyone but the owner and the agent's person. docs/contract.md's state table and spec §10 say so. Evidence: cargo nextest run -p clax-core -E 'test(a_withheld_row_whose_agent_lost_access_still_waits_for_approval_for_its_author) | test(a_row_held_only_for_lost_access_reads_sent_to_its_author) | test(a_no_access_hold_has_its_own_state_and_access_back_tells_the_withheld_line)' passes (the reviewer's case: told withheld, no request, then lost access: Mia reads Withheld, approver Sam); workspace nextest 2266 passed; golden passes.","supersedes":"9c75976cb60ff3069031f9208a0c0968718bc54656da9a7fef8b39062b65cf8b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:58:14.014311Z","id":"c489292a9d441a6dd15485dfb2f91c96b6d2f0e4bfe3539090cc6ae49bdc9638","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:af61599b","summary":"Fixed: a withheld or declined reading carries FeedbackState.no_access for the owner and the agent's person when a row is held for lost access too; the shell reads 'waiting for Sam's approval · the agent no longer has access', clax comments '…; the agent no longer has access'; spec §10 states it. Evidence: an_open_request_on_a_row_whose_agent_lost_access_reads_both passes; web/e2e/lost-access.spec.ts passes (owner 'waiting for Sam's approval · the agent no longer has access', Sam 'waiting for your approval · …', the LAN author 'sent to sam-notes'), checked in Chromium at 1280 and 390 px, light and dark, as the owner and as Sam.","supersedes":"a7145e762a23423e7fff8abe8a88100d6ceb5d99b8aaa8933d5b5fc8661ede5f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:58:14.065191Z","id":"280f4afbf126e4a5b0c3f79b0238ac47210317194164eb26bddce3967706506d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:18155bf9","summary":"Fixed: comment.agent.person is null for the owner's agents, as thread.owner.person is, and person_name is the stored display name via browser_name, as thread.owner.person_name; the inbox agent's person_name is the stored name too; agents keep the payload-safe author line. Evidence: a_comment_agents_person_is_named_as_stored and agent_comments_name_the_harness_never_the_session pass; api_visibility::an_agent_reply_names_the_agent_its_person_and_its_harness asserts person null for the owner's agent; sidebar-model and Panel vitest pass; web/e2e/agent-replies.spec.ts passes.","supersedes":"1e6477e81aa6b7dfa923875df942a113159b483ec992a6f5b970d4cebe6024fa","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:58:14.250010Z","id":"cf4473c0d8af60db81fe31100d0a212cee63066eceec7db7f76b28601d77324e","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"97f30b63590f74dfe9caa2ccbf03624fffe0988caf9151a7616a6773b106a141","summary":"Ruling (relayed by the coordinator, 2026-10-15): unmerged migrations are edited in place by practice; dev homes migrated by earlier builds of this unmerged branch are reset, not upgraded. AGENTS.md's migrations bullet now says so (73c2b8e3).","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:58:14.300840Z","id":"4bdea0b8924190f61fcaf71ecbb7e648b136a2f239b7e2836c285ed6e05a6300","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:73c2b8e3","summary":"Accepted per the ruling in the reply above: no_access_at stays in migration 25, edited in place; AGENTS.md states the practice (73c2b8e3).","supersedes":"97f30b63590f74dfe9caa2ccbf03624fffe0988caf9151a7616a6773b106a141","tags":["reason:wontfix","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:59:02.546796Z","id":"2c203bee4d6c5645ee879b0d9ff18798dd68c7b8294d4b3652378f193d1343fd","body":{"detail":"TAKE_FEEDBACK returns the session's pending rows, the held ones included, and take_feedback_readable runs each through Sight on every take. Measured with a release build at 09672011 (two people, Sam's agent): an empty feedback poll took 0.38 to 0.44 ms with nothing held and 2.24 to 2.65 ms with 150 of Mia's rows held, about 13 us per held row; resolving the threads withdrew the rows and the poll went back to 0.33 to 0.55 ms. Held rows stay until their approver decides, so an agent whose person ignores a busy author's requests polls slower and slower, wait_for_feedback's every wake included. scripts/perf-daemon.py resolves the held threads after each sample so its budget measures the spec's shape, not the pile. A complete version would skip rows whose hold has not changed since the last take (by the visibility generation), or keep held rows out of the pending query until an approval or rights change.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1193},"end":{"line":1240},"content_hash":"147b170e01178ec6c347e8b43a8d35d167e67abbd2b24e38514e894795667c4f"},"summary":"Every take reads the session's held rows again, so each held row costs every later poll of that agent","tags":["perf","visibility","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/elevations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:59:02.546877Z","id":"fe8587433e940954156a4cbbe77f9e9b691f03808fbae16daf17cf209195c401","body":{"detail":"Release build at 09672011, two people: Sam's agent's empty feedback poll took 0.36 to 0.40 ms (minimum) unraised and 0.74 to 0.88 ms once Mia raised it on 16 of her artifacts and the owner on one; its threads read (200 comments) went from 1.36 to 1.65-1.84 ms (minimum). scripts/perf-daemon.py now times the threads read raised (Mia on 8 artifacts, the owner on 1) against the threads budget: 2.85 ms median in the full run, 2.80 ms measured again, limit 2.84 ms.","kind":"comment","references":"7a1e5ef9584b07842a55f049a3a0020be141b208bd7e6c37726478ef4a049edf","summary":"Measured: one creator's raise on 16 artifacts plus the owner's adds about 0.4 ms to every request of the raised agent","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T21:13:03.392735Z","id":"17c0323364773916c0976a5a9d6655028ee51604386f02c58b7113d8703234d8","body":{"detail":"Every take runs Sight::row on each of its session's held rows again (thread_in, the comment's authors through the view), about 13 us a row measured at 09672011, before 7c10f0c1 indexed the request reads a held row's placeholder makes. A held row's hold changes only with the visibility generation (approvals, rights, people, claims) or when its row leaves the pending query (resolve, delete, delivery), so an in-memory map per session of (generation, held feedback IDs) would let a take skip each told held row while the generation is unchanged; the generation lives in memory, so the map must too. Not taken: after 7c10f0c1, 7fd02f8a and b24b98e0 the perf gate's vis_feedback_poll_ms read 1.46-1.54 ms per round in its quietest run (limit 1.78 ms), and scripts/perf-daemon.py withdraws the held rows after each poll, so a pile of held rows is not what it times.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1279},"end":{"line":1291},"content_hash":"014f358e63a6a09fa987dc7c09362de304393d1a90fd4797054e615bc5e0dac1"},"summary":"Skip a take's told held rows while the visibility generation they were last found held at holds","tags":["revisit:vis_feedback_poll_ms over its limit again, or an agent's poll slowed by held rows its person leaves undecided","perf","visibility","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T21:13:32.380177Z","id":"ed625c0dd4e5cfd812aeeff04defbb5204fb29fd9b8a49e7df2ce5bfd04cf31a","body":{"detail":"Every take runs Sight::row on each of its session's held rows again (thread_in, the comment's authors through the view), about 13 us a row measured at 09672011, before 7c10f0c1 indexed the request reads a held row's placeholder makes. A held row's hold changes only with the visibility generation (approvals, rights, people, claims) or when its row leaves the pending query (resolve, delete, delivery), so an in-memory map per session of (generation, held feedback IDs) would let a take skip each told held row while the generation is unchanged; the generation lives in memory, so the map must too. Not taken: with 7c10f0c1 and 7fd02f8a the perf gate's vis_feedback_poll_ms read 1.46, 1.54 and 1.51 ms per round in its quietest run (limit 1.78 ms), and with b24b98e0 as well 1.53 ms in its quietest round (load about 10 on 12 cores); scripts/perf-daemon.py withdraws the held rows after each poll, so a pile of held rows is not what it times.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1279},"end":{"line":1291},"content_hash":"014f358e63a6a09fa987dc7c09362de304393d1a90fd4797054e615bc5e0dac1"},"summary":"Skip a take's told held rows while the visibility generation they were last found held at holds","supersedes":"17c0323364773916c0976a5a9d6655028ee51604386f02c58b7113d8703234d8","tags":["revisit:vis_feedback_poll_ms over its limit again, or an agent's poll slowed by held rows its person leaves undecided","perf","visibility","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T21:13:32.382641Z","id":"2a55e4e5ba6848afb310d811da5bbc3b5629bfd44db22a04b9010828af4e3a71","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7c10f0c1","summary":"Decided not to skip held rows now; the option and when to revisit it are the alternative on crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs:1279:1291 (Skip a take's told held rows while the visibility generation ... holds). Most of a held row's cost was its placeholder's request read, a walk of approval_requests that 7c10f0c1 indexes (request_reads_are_indexed_whatever_the_pile pins the plan).","supersedes":"2c203bee4d6c5645ee879b0d9ff18798dd68c7b8294d4b3652378f193d1343fd","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/elevations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T21:13:32.386562Z","id":"9b382e5c5318ae40be33a1e6f54c067fa16d796dbf19617aad96f5084c695459","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7c10f0c1","summary":"The raised threads read is within budget: vis_threads_ms (raised) medians before (e7896d1b) 3.08, 3.17, 7.79 ms over three full gate runs (limit 2.84 ms), after 7c10f0c1 1.80, 1.63, 1.68 ms, after 7fd02f8a 1.51 ms in the quietest run, per round 1.49 to 1.77 ms. Most of the cost was the threads views' request reads walking approval_requests (indexed in 7c10f0c1); b24b98e0 also reads a creator's raised artifacts in one json_each query and reads the raised rights once per request.","supersedes":"7a1e5ef9584b07842a55f049a3a0020be141b208bd7e6c37726478ef4a049edf","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/exec.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T21:14:18.577186Z","id":"c1fa8f663d2f022bec819ffe35b4e35a957db78410975a92beb0a46488798e4f","body":{"detail":"Seen in Linux perf runs: a single commit held up by the disk. The writer runs WAL with SQLite's default synchronous=FULL, so every commit syncs the WAL, and the background PASSIVE checkpoint runs every CHECKPOINT_INTERVAL (2 s). Every delivery of a write waits on its commit, so one slow commit moves a whole cluster of deliveries (scripts/perf-clients.py:23-29 explains how the realtime gate copes).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":66},"end":{"line":89},"content_hash":"19a1b1cc49fe118705a9d82f6b9227495d66a06ae11378ed14f24dfb809e7ed5"},"suggested_fix":"Measure commit times on Linux with synchronous=NORMAL (durable across a crash of the process, not of the machine, in WAL mode) and with a different checkpoint cadence before choosing.","summary":"On Linux, store commits occasionally take 25 to 120 ms","supersedes":"afa8b528e7374450a20a041d28d29d75deae1d2b3e7525ce1dcdbfe7fecc4df4","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T21:14:18.580267Z","id":"b6fbbf0e2ff0440519bcf54b1b7c115ae2851700d8e17cc409849af834becd24","body":{"detail":"withheld_in_thread counts the authors withheld from each comment body (the rows a take holds, spec M16). A thread whose comments the agent may see but whose anchor, clip or artifact title is another person's (spec §3.3 step 6) is delivered with those fields placeholdered and makes no request; the agent can ask for the artifact's content outside threads with ask {approval: {url_or_id}} (Store::ask_approval, withheld_outside_threads), which covers text fields, the current version, documents and assets, but not a thread's anchor.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1292},"end":{"line":1312},"content_hash":"2db7bc0ea49daabf8d49defd3d54488b8041d0c22a95068bc6531cfc23d68cee"},"summary":"Routing asks only for the authors of comment bodies; a withheld anchor, clip, batch note or title makes no request","supersedes":"b00f8f3b34bd3743dee054d554a2aca908864f9acb5a3a4751f5cc844c93ad67","tags":["people","spec:9.2","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T21:14:18.582424Z","id":"ca20c8cae63653348299c4cc6ecc3676428e073c4d2e5ec806a6ea0758a851b6","body":{"detail":"Spec §9.3: 'Declining keeps the rows held; a later ask there makes a new request only after 10 minutes'. request_in applies the same quiet period to routing, so a sender pressing Send again right after the approver declined does not re-announce the request; the rows are held and the agent's placeholder reads as not asked. If the owner wants a deliberate re-send to ask at once, drop the check for Cause::Routing.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1118},"end":{"line":1127},"content_hash":"cf9707d61e55687d29484ea3ec1da7a8faa513bbca583c591bf81438ce7a4e23"},"summary":"A routed send within ten minutes of a decline makes no request, though spec §9.3 names only ask","supersedes":"ea1fcd06efb9ffa14ac30061358d3f922277ec079550f1f2827e63b6bd8c50d0","tags":["people","spec:9.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T21:14:18.584671Z","id":"7f5b5747e53e1b339c625904a62dfb478d44e6af2fefc90e855fc94f69838cc6","body":{"detail":"The overflow marker (install row approval_overflow:<approver>) lists the [author, artifact, thread] places whose routed content request_in held without a request, past MAX_OPEN_REQUESTS (100) per approver or MAX_OPEN_PER_AUTHOR (20) per author. Only Store::decide_request rechecks them, dropping a place once its content is no longer held without a request (held_without_request: answered by an open or declined request, delivered, gone, or now visible). A withdrawal or an approval made outside a decision changes nothing until the next decision, so the banner can outlive what it counted.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1904},"end":{"line":1914},"content_hash":"e605efbaa1b77ac65394cb92bbe3b8380e6925c8a3c4e43692703b6852ef04e5"},"summary":"People's overflow banner stays up after withdrawals bring an approver under the limit, until their next decision","supersedes":"0f0f13b253b8d8325d9ba5173c3b1bb2dc6c743bc19bd332167a9e10c2f467d3","tags":["people","spec:9.2","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T21:14:18.586802Z","id":"fbaca2aabd674f7dca2ec3c27dcb211fc7db64bbd0f2ef76e12275c3f3c67474","body":{"detail":"approve_owner_on_connect is the single approval made without a browser (spec section 21 item 3, M15). It is bounded to the connect: once per grant, within OWNER_ANSWER_SECS (10 minutes) of the tokens' issue, never once the person has made or revoked any approval of the owner (409 owner_answered, so a revocation in People stands; 409 answer_closed after the window), replays refused by accept_t first. Only the continuation token says it, never the access token agents sign with (crates/clax-server/tests/api_grants.rs a_connected_machine_approves_the_owner_through_its_continuation), and clax connect refuses on an agent channel (crates/clax-cli/tests/connect.rs connect_refuses_on_an_agent_channel). What remains: a process of the person's that reads remote.json within those ten minutes, before clax connect answers, could answer yes for them; the person can revoke it in People, and that revocation is final. Tests: store::people::tests::connecting_records_the_persons_approval_of_the_owner_once, the_answer_about_the_owner_never_overrides_the_person.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1477},"end":{"line":1569},"content_hash":"d5ef04715b7251bf982fd51818c94f17a2b0b3b2dd3450f46854211db24ca24d"},"summary":"The person's approval of the owner is recorded without a browser once, at connect: an agent present then could answer for the person","supersedes":"968a4bad0b5113873f756b0c3e80b22292203de4e380a4b1e747f0c4f5813926","tags":["security","spec:6.3","spec:21","M15","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T21:14:18.590836Z","id":"b5059e16624c0d267922097dc173ae96980c5a0a1adaa9e508d7accc51259757","body":{"detail":"For flow invite the grant's events carry grant_id and person but not invite_id, so the journal cannot join invite.create to the grant made from it except by person and time; invites.grant_id holds the link only while the row lives.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1088},"end":{"line":1102},"content_hash":"a055d17fb6d13921d9565129c8f0b702f534ab8d657151596b97465c24004831"},"suggested_fix":"Add invite_id to grant.request (flow invite) and to audit spec section 6.13 and multi-person spec section 20.2.","summary":"An invite-flow grant.request and grant.approve do not name the invite they redeemed","supersedes":"db2b92e84f37710c8ddb5ff6f993e0e5a854f18187c6319bc5a009c932d99be4","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T21:14:18.602698Z","id":"1d272fa3e6589aca0f8f8650ffbf36c5e1b044a45c667c77381648ed93984e33","body":{"detail":"An invite that expires unredeemed records nothing (audit spec section 6.13 lists only invite.create and invite.revoke). When release_unconnected then returns its person to a plain viewer it sets person = 0 and rights_json = NULL in the sweep or a revoke, so rights set by invite.create's rights or person.rights change with no person.rights event: the journal's last word on that person's rights is wrong.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2273},"end":{"line":2301},"content_hash":"21c6a12d5da90d6d5c16c6ff28c6c0e9001be65589ae337c9755bc64876f5506"},"summary":"An invite's lapse is not recorded, and release_unconnected clears a person's flag and rights without an event","supersedes":"d84547101f6be54ada9cde90858e5c3cb8ae05eebe901de48c2c656c97c161fb","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T21:14:18.617575Z","id":"5367fcc4689814242a680d9584e3d3bf9fc8dbd0f19447b827af1efaa70fb5d1","body":{"detail":"Failure: a home at migration 25 where a person's agent asked a question (a dev home run on this branch) keeps that question's item with recipient NULL after 26, so it sits in the owner's inbox and crates/clax-server/src/inbox.rs render reads its question unscoped (st.question), showing the person's question and answers to the owner, while the person never gets the item. Main's homes hold no person sessions, so they are unaffected. Accepted: migrations 24-26 are unmerged (spec M27), so only a dev home run on this branch can hold such items; questions themselves get their person from their session (questions.person is filled in by the migration).","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":724},"end":{"line":727},"content_hash":"4611fbab17797ab78415d9f71e991c5b174e8ca88f75ff87d6685c7d8474fc79"},"summary":"Migration 26 leaves every existing inbox item the owner's, including question and finished items a connected person's agent made at schema 24-25","supersedes":"27748a78b6a6de36de3e756d68fcb208f7f3c9f75ef880dd015480e78ab1b297","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T21:14:18.649581Z","id":"ddeebf95200fc5fa9f333fc90c0217f46a2d00120c7a8ae126f14941aaa93d3f","body":{"detail":"state_of reports withheld (the target session's person as approver) from placeholder_at, which a take sets when it holds and tells a row, or while an open approval request of that person covers the row's comment author there (a send naming the agent, spec §10). A comment that joins no request (a send naming no agent, a later reply whose author has no open request there, an author held past the request limits) reads sent, waiting on its tier, until the agent's next take. Computing it from visibility at state time would build a Visibility per target session's person inside feedback_states_in, which listings call for every thread (spec §8.7 cost).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2160},"end":{"line":2169},"content_hash":"c65b0f968699e8cc0c38af1592e8e7b90d060df9c18a71599f611feba41154f4"},"summary":"A held row that no open request covers reads sent until a take holds it","supersedes":"f7b7275e0e01c4ca1e44d2659416e3e4064fa4c310535285864d559efbec90db","tags":["people","spec:8.4","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T22:16:49.647560Z","id":"4592becd364b79b95ef78b2d35b84edd211d42730c6eddc3bd352be1549af6f0","body":{"detail":"take_feedback builds each item's `url` and the text line 'Comment sent to you on \"<title>\" (<url>)' from the daemon's fixed browser_base (crates/clax-server/src/state.rs:80, passed in at crates/clax-server/src/routes/feedback.rs:308; the same base at crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs:1752). For a PersonAgent on another machine the shim's own URLs use remote.json's LAN address (watch answered http://192.168.0.65:<port>/a/<id>), but every delivered comment (wait_for_feedback, piggyback, the Stop and prompt hooks' text, Pi's inject) says http://127.0.0.1:<port>/a/<id>. Reproduced: daemon bound 0.0.0.0, a machine connected by invite, its shim watched an artifact, the owner sent a comment to it; the payload's url and text named 127.0.0.1. An agent that tells its person to open that link sends them to their own machine. Passing the URL back as url_or_id still resolves (path-based), so only the person-facing link is wrong.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1427},"end":{"line":1427},"content_hash":"406d5eff8db2352902ed56661b9b3b06de9426de72fd6f7bd91a7a69ce4a1d44"},"suggested_fix":"For an agent caller with a grant, build payload URLs from the request's Host (the signed one, which is the LAN address the machine connected to), or have the agent side (shim, hooks, Pi) rewrite the daemon's browser_base prefix to remote.json's url as the clip lines are rewritten.","summary":"A remote agent's feedback payload names the daemon's loopback URL (http://127.0.0.1:<port>/a/<id>), which on the person's own machine points nowhere","tags":["review","remote","final-review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T22:24:19.594714Z","id":"b72ba63ac705499b5462e0c53a9af5da5caff403f47fe899f6f06ac890a06ed3","body":{"detail":"Only approve and deny mark a `connection` item read. A request that expired (the machine stopped waiting after 10 minutes) shows in the owner's inbox under Unread as \"Expired: the machine stopped waiting\", with no unread dot to press; it leaves only with Mark all read.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1380},"end":{"line":1385},"content_hash":"37faa7c25489c7bb21c58449a00b215ba4670c56c30156fd84acd0324fb5acb1"},"summary":"An expired connection request stays unread with nothing to mark it read","tags":["review","final-review-ui","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T01:10:27.137720Z","id":"4904fab7ef3ab2c6b6dd612149445e0dc467c7e8c8e6b9701d9f0647d9605a57","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:998f5172","summary":"Fixed in 998f5172: the feedback poll and notices routes build a grant caller's links from its signed Host (crates/clax-server/src/routes/feedback.rs agent_base). Evidence: api_people::a_persons_agent_gets_links_on_the_address_it_reached passes (notices and tiers wait, piggyback, stop_hook, prompt_hook, inject all name http://192.0.2.1:<port>/a/<id>, never the loopback base); it failed before the fix with url http://127.0.0.1:<port>/a/<id>.","supersedes":"4592becd364b79b95ef78b2d35b84edd211d42730c6eddc3bd352be1549af6f0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T01:10:27.161573Z","id":"93ccd2ddf531783d69d8779bbe40218bfef6813834fce9289cf143b637c8bc60","body":{"detail":"Migration 24 hashes every existing viewer's row ID into viewer_cookies with legacy = 1 so existing LAN viewers keep their identity; a legacy cookie never names a person (VIEWER_BY_COOKIE), a viewer made a person loses its legacy cookies (create_invite), and GET /api/viewers/me replaces one with a cxv_ secret (reissue_viewer_cookie). Until that call, someone who minted viewers in the same millisecond as the victim on main could still act as that anonymous viewer (comment, rename): the pre-branch exposure, now bounded to unvisited anonymous viewers. Retiring every legacy cookie at once (say, at the first daemon start after a fixed date) would close it at the cost of those viewers' identities.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":210},"end":{"line":227},"content_hash":"eb67b28f4eb876abf1e6a465accff8beafc260d507309387730941ad0daef894"},"summary":"An anonymous LAN viewer migrated from main keeps its guessable legacy cookie (its row ID, a monotonic ULID) until that browser next calls GET /api/viewers/me","tags":["final-review","security","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T03:13:17.322735Z","id":"1716804ec84a5aac950bdaae7aa5258518a4b8cffa6aae48f83c0d68ec11428f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:2eb5ce4a","summary":"An unread connection card that no longer waits (expired, gone) offers Mark read, which marks the item read through the inbox's toggle. Evidence: ConnectionCard.test.ts 'offers Mark read on an unread request that expired, and on no pending one' passes. Lapsing a request takes 10 minutes, so it was not reproduced in a browser; 0118687f (the lapse paths leave the item unread) stays open.","supersedes":"b72ba63ac705499b5462e0c53a9af5da5caff403f47fe899f6f06ac890a06ed3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T03:13:17.330561Z","id":"e955bc71350bc41fad212d8d442a9e9fe2ccac88738698ddb94307ff3f4ede0d","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"0118687f2dc557d8b4b673cfea9e3a7e7911afa2f991c90dad88cf4e6622b3cb","summary":"The owner can now mark such an item read from its card (ConnectionCard's Mark read, 2eb5ce4a); the lapse paths still leave it unread.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T04:16:26.695505Z","id":"28447b52deee8016a0061ede51bf2a8c73a9e91b5dc6e9c969d976d38469b20d","body":{"detail":"Probed at e5eca81b: GET /api/viewers/me with clax_viewer=cxv_AAAA…A (client-chosen, well-formed) answered 200 with a new viewer and no Set-Cookie; the hash was stored legacy=0. After naming it 'Dana' and the owner inviting that viewer (POST /api/people/invites {viewer}), the same chosen value got 200 from /api/people/me and /api/inbox. The browser-link path is safe (it always sets a fresh secret; a carried cookie is not folded; a second tossed value beside the person's makes read() refuse both). This is fixation, not guessing; main accepted any ULID the same way, so it is not a regression, but spec §21.4 now says a browser cookie cannot be guessed and docs/contract.md:1241 already treats another local server's cookies as a threat.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":163},"end":{"line":183},"content_hash":"36032c5b2dd730ffe465225e7725374f3f4afc83b5dfac6e744db42f1d170fed"},"suggested_fix":"Treat an unknown cookie like no cookie: mint a fresh secret and Set-Cookie it, never binding a presented value; or, when the owner makes a viewer a person, forget all its cookies so only a browser link carries the person.","summary":"A cxv_ cookie the daemon never minted is accepted and bound to a new viewer, so a cookie fixed into a browser (another local server can set it: cookies ignore ports) carries a person's authority once the owner invites that viewer","tags":["review","final-rereview","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T04:55:21.650714Z","id":"c44a4bd3903e1bc4e5132846f4dabed7b326a4e030fc2680cf85ae30aecaae4e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:25c71077","summary":"Fixed in 25c71077: GET /api/viewers/me answers a cookie that names no viewer with a new viewer under a freshly minted secret, and Identity::ensure_viewer only finds viewers (never makes one from a cookie), so a planted value never binds. Evidence: api_people::a_planted_cookie_never_binds_to_a_viewer passes (planted cxv_ value: new Set-Cookie, the planted value names no one, a seen write with it makes no viewer); with the previous code it fails ('a minted cookie replaces the planted one').","supersedes":"28447b52deee8016a0061ede51bf2a8c73a9e91b5dc6e9c969d976d38469b20d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:24:17.791502Z","id":"bcb6cc4e965c3365ff6c06117df03fd5fe8d53056a98c1a3838fd6f6cc47858a","body":{"detail":"release_owned_in (crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs) selects threads WHERE target_session_id = ?1, and Store::roster groups threads by target_session_id; crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs indexes neither. Both are full scans of threads: off the request hot paths (ends, the reaper, GET /api/agents) and cheap at today's sizes, but linear in all threads ever made.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1639},"end":{"line":1655},"content_hash":"20c6bc83236711f3d0fd91be27eb8807d928e32beb5474638e9b1e8ace251388"},"suggested_fix":"Add CREATE INDEX threads_by_target ON threads(target_session_id) WHERE target_session_id IS NOT NULL in the next migration.","summary":"Every session end and every roster read scans threads for target_session_id, which has no index","supersedes":"e01c18367829f04888159f9beae2cfd0917f7064eaa0a0953f40319f13429abb","tags":["perf","revisit:the next migration on this branch","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:24:17.794286Z","id":"fd6040ef7d2358f9590d2f05a7474abea5df12064faedca715a213273ec1b57b","body":{"detail":"At 8446429: upsert_viewer(lan, 'Аlex') with no owner name succeeds; set_owner_name('Alex') then succeeds too, and both names stand. An agent registering from repository web is named 'web' beside a LAN viewer 'wеb'. New people are covered (check_person_name refuses a look-alike held by an uninvited viewer). The owner usually names themselves late, on a first comment, so pre-squatting is the likely order.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":64},"end":{"line":84},"content_hash":"c06ab88428e27667bd6b67987ffbae3548c38076beedd1bad8e86ea2a4ee39ac"},"suggested_fix":"Mark it where names are shown: an unconnected viewer whose name looks like a protected name is flagged in the shell and in agent author lines (with spec section 9.6's '(not connected)', Task 17), rather than refusing the owner their own name.","summary":"The look-alike check runs only when the later name is set: a LAN viewer who took 'Аlex' before the owner named themselves 'Alex', or 'wеb' before an agent web went live, keeps it","supersedes":"63cb4ceee8070bb7ca207c0e3a295f4f748b3a05d00992033aa59925b306cc98","tags":["review","spec:9.6","revisit:task-17","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:50:04.053454Z","id":"33053daa29b8c958c75e57a4d6bffae5fb00693d73d5bf4a970c37ac796940f4","body":{"detail":"Failure: at load average 38, `fresh` (registered after the 300 ms sleep) was more than 200 ms old when reap_sessions(200 ms) ran, so it was reaped too and reaped.ended.len() was 3, not 2. It passed when rerun alone. The test measures idleness by the wall clock (std::thread::sleep, then a fixed limit), which the repository's test rules (AGENTS.md, Code) reserve for injected clocks.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2264},"end":{"line":2279},"content_hash":"16f02efa7807605004f5ea6b2d933316c5883e439d41718811276850897ae21a"},"suggested_fix":"Give reap_sessions the current time (or a Clock) so the test advances it instead of sleeping, and drop the sleep.","summary":"reaper_ends_only_idle_sessions_with_dead_or_unknown_pids sleeps against a 200 ms idle limit and fails on a loaded machine","tags":["flaky-test","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:32:05.047678Z","id":"1e165437762c0e77252d5db1eb5a2027ec806c6738ee7d7b27c00fe88ff1a42a","body":{"detail":"Spec §9.3: 'Declining keeps the rows held; a later ask there makes a new request only after 10 minutes'. request_in applies the same quiet period to routing, so a sender pressing Send again right after the approver declined does not re-announce the request; the rows are held and the agent's placeholder reads as not asked. If the owner wants a deliberate re-send to ask at once, drop the check for Cause::Routing.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1112},"end":{"line":1121},"content_hash":"cf9707d61e55687d29484ea3ec1da7a8faa513bbca583c591bf81438ce7a4e23"},"summary":"A routed send within ten minutes of a decline makes no request, though spec §9.3 names only ask","supersedes":"ca20c8cae63653348299c4cc6ecc3676428e073c4d2e5ec806a6ea0758a851b6","tags":["people","spec:9.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:32:05.050502Z","id":"9f25f03b61c4feda1b96fd40cffaa7d0cbc6d165032e5bb7bb459051af3ef0f1","body":{"detail":"withheld_in_thread counts the authors withheld from each comment body (the rows a take holds, spec M16). A thread whose comments the agent may see but whose anchor, clip or artifact title is another person's (spec §3.3 step 6) is delivered with those fields placeholdered and makes no request; the agent can ask for the artifact's content outside threads with ask {approval: {url_or_id}} (Store::ask_approval, withheld_outside_threads), which covers text fields, the current version, documents and assets, but not a thread's anchor.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1286},"end":{"line":1306},"content_hash":"2db7bc0ea49daabf8d49defd3d54488b8041d0c22a95068bc6531cfc23d68cee"},"summary":"Routing asks only for the authors of comment bodies; a withheld anchor, clip, batch note or title makes no request","supersedes":"b6fbbf0e2ff0440519bcf54b1b7c115ae2851700d8e17cc409849af834becd24","tags":["people","spec:9.2","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:32:05.053170Z","id":"bfa6b632771fa16d4b38772ce25992196baf295156e890a57833a7b60dcd7938","body":{"detail":"The overflow marker (install row approval_overflow:<approver>) lists the [author, artifact, thread] places whose routed content request_in held without a request, past MAX_OPEN_REQUESTS (100) per approver or MAX_OPEN_PER_AUTHOR (20) per author. Only Store::decide_request rechecks them, dropping a place once its content is no longer held without a request (held_without_request: answered by an open or declined request, delivered, gone, or now visible). A withdrawal or an approval made outside a decision changes nothing until the next decision, so the banner can outlive what it counted.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1898},"end":{"line":1908},"content_hash":"e605efbaa1b77ac65394cb92bbe3b8380e6925c8a3c4e43692703b6852ef04e5"},"summary":"People's overflow banner stays up after withdrawals bring an approver under the limit, until their next decision","supersedes":"7f5b5747e53e1b339c625904a62dfb478d44e6af2fefc90e855fc94f69838cc6","tags":["people","spec:9.2","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/visibility.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:32:05.055730Z","id":"1ce7014035ba6eb7ffb039525e4da90decc5ba9a92ea27f400b7548e57075993","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs:330-337, record b8541bce.\n\nUnattributed history is marked '(not connected)' (owner's decision on 7fdbaaf5). Comments the owner's browser made between migrations 12 and 15 carry a viewer row with minted_local NULL that claim_for_owner (crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs) never claims, so they are marked on real installs too. Matching names is spoofable (spec §21.2); an explicit fold by the owner in the browser is not.","kind":"alternative","ref":"git:cbca495ec17bb7b2d7d70077d1b1b1dbb113fdb3","span":{"start":{"line":72},"end":{"line":79},"content_hash":"31b72a09f53496f8d927466a9d2f661853a503a3fd7274e62dbae25d003fa4ac"},"summary":"An owner-only, browser-only 'this was me' in People that folds a legacy viewer row (or claims unattributed comments) into the owner, unmarking that history without trusting names","tags":["revisit:owners report their own old comments marked as not connected","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:42:34.239840Z","id":"0e4e3742056f85f91f26506893b033d95f2302528c1d0914b0fc9bb413e73013","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","summary":"Moved to crates/clax-store/src/approvals.rs:1115:1124 as 7d14c47b in git:9f99ad87","supersedes":"1e165437762c0e77252d5db1eb5a2027ec806c6738ee7d7b27c00fe88ff1a42a","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
