{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/github.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:42:09.106391Z","id":"51658b1bf2325e11dd58547c8b1d019274512c8d10cc1b933fb269642a2584f4","body":{"detail":"check_quota counts the person's live artifacts (MemberCaps::max_artifacts, MEMBER_MAX_ARTIFACTS / [hosted] member_max_artifacts, default 200) and is called from create_artifact_async (crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs) and fork_artifact_async (crates/clax-core/src/store/forks.rs). Nothing bounds the bytes a member writes: new versions of their own artifacts, asset uploads and pushed commits are uncounted, so one member can fill the content store within MAX_ASSET_BYTES per upload and the version size limits. A byte cap needs a running per-account counter charged in the version and asset transactions (record_version_locked, upload_asset).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":305},"end":{"line":340},"content_hash":"15906e486096e7696147bd11eeffb664687bc6851388db8b5581955b31076521"},"summary":"A GitHub member's account is capped by artifact count alone: no cap on stored bytes","tags":["deferred","hosted","github","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/github.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:42:09.106478Z","id":"a0ccecca72086ca75c0f165f6bd73262a1c43ce259879974de9c5eea7b3ea1e2","body":{"detail":"member_rights grants create at * and every artifacts, comments and db action at own, and nothing of clax-ask, so a member's agents cannot ask their person questions (crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs need! QuestionsPoll and ApprovalsAsk need Ask). Left out because who answers a member's agent's question was not settled; the owner can widen a person's rights on People.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":96},"end":{"line":104},"content_hash":"e3d1d65ddf6be5020839bd081d3693ffdd249d123fe385e1980864d3a4b523e4"},"summary":"GitHub members' default rights leave out clax-ask","tags":["hosted","github","revisit:a member's agent needs to ask its person a question or an approval","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/github.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:42:09.106511Z","id":"a57972fc2ba1f449adb70c3b8baba948adce2ac55fba61daa49e085296909fbd","body":{"detail":"block_in sets github_identities.blocked_at when the owner revokes the person (Store::revoke_person in crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs), and github_sign_in refuses an account whose row is blocked or whose person is revoked. Nothing clears blocked_at, and People offers no unblock: the owner would have to edit the database to let the account back in.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":348},"end":{"line":354},"content_hash":"486b8783435225a3efdbef07b2d4303c54f3f0933cfac0fe9f56f203b15132be"},"summary":"A blocked GitHub account cannot be unblocked","tags":["hosted","github","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T02:42:09.106666Z","id":"f6b70331a5488de143e69751e04d123dbe8cabfa5bccedef065108a602f10b06","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":901},"end":{"line":918},"content_hash":"35ab1c3601e03d88addb1eff7ff7a3d1cbe46a10641e5c15a33cf6c41d818878"},"summary":"Migration 31 (GitHub identities) follows akesling/clax-artifacts' 30 (publishing to a public Clax); it renumbers if another branch lands a 31 first","tags":["migrations","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/shares.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:59:09.395574Z","id":"68ea5a3389c99503e036a16bf751d9e0e5a7e20ca97eada6c140cb51d94c61bf","body":{"detail":"Store::public_artifacts lists every artifact shared by link with link_listed set, newest first, up to MAX_PUBLIC_LISTED (200). PUT /api/hosted/artifacts/<aid>/link {listed: true} is allowed to the owner and to the artifact's maker (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs may_share), and on a hosted daemon with GitHub sign-in anyone with a GitHub account is a member who makes artifacts. So any GitHub account can put titles (and pages) on the signed-out sign-in page's 'Public on Clax' list (web/shell/src/hosted/SignIn.svelte), and push the owner's out of the 200 shown. GET /api/hosted/public itself is not rate limited (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs public_list).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":506},"end":{"line":525},"content_hash":"66533e84f0d40474901dc75c7dd7974aab36bbf3e2b8c61711159640e5d3ade7"},"suggested_fix":"Either let only the owner list publicly (a maker may still share by link), or keep members' listings off the landing page until the owner approves them; and count GET /api/hosted/public in Limits.","summary":"Any member may list their artifacts on the public page, which signed-out visitors see first, and the listing has no rate or count limit per member","tags":["security","abuse","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/shares.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:59:09.395799Z","id":"da6660c8e4d8ce6971cbbb0ec46d124ad6b8541cf86441d5c4798c769c1bf3a6","body":{"detail":"share_artifact resolves a login through github_identities.login, which is refreshed only at each sign-in (crates/clax-core/src/store/github.rs link). If account A signed in as 'octo', later renamed on GitHub and never signed in here again, and someone else now holds 'octo' on GitHub, a share to '@octo' binds to A's person, not to whoever owns the login today. A login no one here has signed in with waits and binds at its first sign-in, which is safe: from then on the share follows the person, not the login (tested in shares.rs a_login_share_waits_for_its_first_sign_in_then_follows_the_person).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":330},"end":{"line":345},"content_hash":"0f48399d24676bee458098b796956398d96ef690dc90960df446288dc6c15847"},"suggested_fix":"Look the login up on GitHub's API (GET /users/<login>) when sharing, and bind by numeric ID.","summary":"A share by GitHub login binds at once to whichever account last signed in with that login here, which may be stale after a rename","tags":["security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/shares.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T04:17:42.528628Z","id":"a355483969be6730fde57f9bffd05a535f73503f371f318b6dbb016aab8b3824","body":{"detail":"ShareAccess::Editor grants clax-artifacts update at its artifact. PATCH /api/artifacts/<aid> (crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs patch, need ArtifactsPatch = update) passes pinned and capabilities to Store::update_meta, which writes artifacts.pinned and artifacts.capabilities_json (crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs:309-316). artifacts.pinned is one flag per artifact, not per viewer, so a person shared Can edit pins or unpins the page for everyone, and can add or drop declared capabilities (db, comments) on a page they do not own. Nothing a share grants beyond 'publish new versions' is listed in the dialog's note (web/shell/src/ui/ShareDialog.svelte).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":48},"end":{"line":51},"content_hash":"04b2ce1d284ec0b7af25875a1b0115b61a4d02427535dd1d7cc895b63af84609"},"suggested_fix":"Decide whether Can edit covers metadata; if not, refuse pinned and capabilities in update_meta to a caller who holds update only through a share (the maker and the owner keep them).","summary":"An editor's update right also lets them set the artifact's pinned flag and replace its capabilities through PATCH /api/artifacts/<aid>","tags":["security","sharing","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/shares.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T04:17:42.528733Z","id":"bdf27a495da332ac06aaed9e8107c95921ffc6fa65f24fdeae2f81e804a0aa85","body":{"detail":"share_artifact's login lookup (github_identities joined to viewers) checks only that the row is not the owner's; it does not read github_identities.blocked_at or viewers.person_revoked_at. ShareTo::Person refuses a revoked person (unknown_person), so the two paths disagree. No access follows (a blocked account cannot sign in and a revoked person's grants end), but the sharer sees the share as granted to a named person rather than refused.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":332},"end":{"line":345},"content_hash":"32639782b0a4356b493eedf2bea40b3ee1b0c257d7eecf9ed56009cab56ffc0f"},"suggested_fix":"Refuse such a login as ShareTo::Person refuses a revoked person, or show the share as blocked.","summary":"A share by login binds to an account whose GitHub identity is blocked or whose person is revoked, and the dialog lists it as an ordinary person","tags":["sharing","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/shares.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T04:27:09.653894Z","id":"933f4118c67f9feda6229dee0a66a3736856ecfa5a97622302184966448aabd7","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:b67cf05e","summary":"No one may list a page while the public gallery is off, which is the default ([hosted] public_gallery / PUBLIC_GALLERY=1 turns it on): PUT /link with listed:true answers 403 public_gallery_off and GET /api/hosted/public lists nothing. cargo test -p clax-server --test integration -- public_gallery no_one_lists: 2 passed, among them with_the_public_gallery_off_no_one_lists_a_page. With the gallery turned on, members may still list their own pages; that limit needs revisiting before it is.","supersedes":"68ea5a3389c99503e036a16bf751d9e0e5a7e20ca97eada6c140cb51d94c61bf","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:57:35.240838Z","id":"73044f1d375391dc59e5a787126cb70d57cc417b74442142c0c15790099e2c82","body":{"detail":"A hosted daemon keeps every key a linked local daemon's up-sends named (crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs comment_key), as publish_keys keeps every publish's. Rows are small, but nothing removes them, not even when the thread or grant is deleted.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1022},"end":{"line":1029},"content_hash":"4ba09b7472a4ca6e5001974915649601eee612783ece3677d8a9dc4398698508"},"suggested_fix":"Delete a grant's keys with the grant and a thread's with the thread, or prune keys older than the outbox could resend (a day).","summary":"comment_keys is never pruned: one row per thread or comment an agent token wrote with an Idempotency-Key","tags":["review","status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:57:35.241021Z","id":"996fae6b913df2e7f6f682e1d39a61df95c7a8109f193b88dec89bad33c52908","body":{"detail":"threads records no reopener, so scan_linked queues every reopen of a linked thread, while resolves go up only when the owner or an owner's agent resolved (resolved_by, resolved_by_person). Another local person who can see a linked thread and reopens it is reported there as the owner's person.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":768},"end":{"line":780},"content_hash":"68b1d810d48a25f82d340e55584a56333546f845fa14c5ade1f6e019b04812b5"},"suggested_fix":"Record who reopened a thread (reopened_by) and queue a reopen only when it is the owner's or an owner's agent's.","summary":"A reopen goes up as the token's person whoever reopened it here","tags":["review","security","status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:57:35.241079Z","id":"04eaeec1d22e332b025da1b09785964fb796a81674961e19fb7f01ab58553977","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-15-linked-threads-design (Authors) says a mirrored comment is stored with author kind remote. comments.author_kind carries CHECK (author_kind IN ('viewer','agent')) from migration 3, and feedback rows reference comments, so adding a kind needs a table rebuild under foreign keys. The comment is written as a viewer comment with no local public ID (or an agent comment of no session) and its remote kind, public ID and name are kept in linked_comments; views add linked.origin remote and agents read the author as '<name> (on <remote>)'. The author is never a local person either way.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":567},"end":{"line":600},"content_hash":"1d315f12504beb532832435e36692c31c1b338debf63539814fd73b5727f1649"},"summary":"Mirrored comments keep a local author_kind viewer or agent, with the remote author in linked_comments, instead of author_kind remote","tags":["design","revisit:the comments table is next rebuilt","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:57:35.241185Z","id":"5b138f7eb7d9f95675c8f4c6c90737c5e19af06f68f3f4e3ad32340476bbca73","body":{"detail":"remote_versions is written by pushes from migration 33 on. For an artifact pushed before, only the link's pushed_n/remote_n pair is known, so a public thread on an older public version is placed on the newest pushed local version and shown as 'on <remote> v<n>' though a twin exists.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":318},"end":{"line":322},"content_hash":"9a418a8e6498501aaef54bc63beafb59ae3045a16669f5a7f718a92c47fb405b"},"suggested_fix":"Backfill remote_versions on the next push by pairing the public copy's versions with the local ones in order when the link was never moved (no fork, no new).","summary":"Versions pushed before linked threads have no recorded twin but the link's last push","tags":["review","status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T15:06:18.492878Z","id":"8194fd2ad48a9483b2ee82fdf3775c9785cb3ed8dcb90ba9f0eb82fe584f6b43","body":{"detail":"thread_id is the PRIMARY KEY; scan_linked queues a fresh local thread only when no linked_threads row names it (crates/clax-core/src/store/linked.rs scan_linked), so the first remote scanned takes it and the other never gets it, nor its replies. Threads mirrored from either remote are separate local threads.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":971},"end":{"line":984},"content_hash":"422e16fad9ac387965892c1a684d9f7f45d108c71b2cd3fbe0fa9890e34ef65e"},"summary":"linked_threads is keyed by the local thread alone, so an artifact linked to two remotes sends its local threads to only one of them","tags":["review","linked-threads","revisit:an artifact is pushed to a second remote","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T15:06:18.493129Z","id":"9fb253f94d798bb05ebace71d75013f8034a0e44ec2eb1e82e356eb84cd2e0ab","body":{"detail":"Sync::mirror looks a remote thread up by (remote, remote thread ID) alone, so a remote that lists, under one public artifact, a thread ID belonging to another artifact linked to it writes into that other artifact's local thread. Only artifacts linked to that remote are reachable, and the remote can write to them anyway, so this is consistency rather than access.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":439},"end":{"line":450},"content_hash":"5d646f16c65cb93420f8638cd10f761cdf837fa7a9cf4122734478ccc796ece1"},"suggested_fix":"Also match remote_artifact_id (or artifact_id) of the link being read.","summary":"linked_thread_by_remote is not scoped to the link's artifact","tags":["review","linked-threads","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T18:33:48.213340Z","id":"9359e05259d026fe9bf2746633dce84ad47780888565af9b66a61fe29b49bf22","body":{"kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1065},"end":{"line":1071},"content_hash":"40e0ef842deae344eeb6cb9ab562cb44f1e01fd90bba9720a79e05d2a441f941"},"summary":"question_keys is never pruned: one row per question an agent token asked with an Idempotency-Key","tags":["linked-threads","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T18:45:53.322474Z","id":"03c16835e344bed9114ccfa22f5221c4e5e9e40316659fbf554b3c1519f1dc06","body":{"detail":"Store::session_or_keyed_question lets any live session of grant G read (GET /api/sessions/<sid>/questions/<qid>, which also takes an answered question) and withdraw a question another of G's sessions asked under an Idempotency-Key, and Store::create_question_keyed answers a resend of that key from any of G's sessions with the question, answers included. Per-session secrets (crates/clax-server/src/identity.rs Identity::prove_session) exist so a sibling agent of the same machine cannot act as a session; for keyed questions that line now falls back to the grant. Reaching it takes the question ID or the key, which the asking agent chose. The linked-question sync needs it because its session there changes on reconnect (crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs Sync::question).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":752},"end":{"line":779},"content_hash":"dc38eaf7317053c13d26207e4c8460c08892bd5336e26301f365731bbe5e8515"},"suggested_fix":"Options: (a) keep, since the asker opts in by keying; (b) reach a keyed question only from sessions of the grant whose harness and name match the asker's (the sync's own sessions); (c) keep one sync session there across reconnects and drop the cross-session reach.","summary":"A keyed question is reachable from every session of its agent token, so a sibling agent on that machine may read its answers, withdraw it, or replay its key","tags":["review","security","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/shares.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T00:45:42.023705Z","id":"8172b7708b13aee948b7c42dd1c76e1686bb3a76934024743abed95ed9c281af","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7e77d482","summary":"Owner decision (2026-10-15): 'Only admin should be able to change access. Edit just means change contents.' Fixed: a change to the pinned flag or capabilities, by PATCH /api/artifacts/<aid> or a publish, is 403 admin_only unless the caller administers the artifact (crate::agent::administers: the owner, the page's maker, and their agents). Evidence: cargo test -p clax-server --test integration api_hosted passes 53/53 (an_artifact_shared_with_a_person_opens_to_them_at_its_access_alone: an editor's agent's pin and capability change are refused admin_only, its retitle passes); the full integration suite passes 825.","supersedes":"a355483969be6730fde57f9bffd05a535f73503f371f318b6dbb016aab8b3824","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T00:45:42.072690Z","id":"b04d9a52ba996c62ebd1e17dafbd61fc9dd0f27f50f3ccc96418ca06d98106af","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Owner decision (2026-10-15): 'An agent token should be able to see the things it created.' A keyed question stays reachable from every session of the agent token that created it; no change.","supersedes":"03c16835e344bed9114ccfa22f5221c4e5e9e40316659fbf554b3c1519f1dc06","tags":["reason:wontfix","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T17:02:53.470173Z","id":"fa65f5c2c639e1c28844c8c937ddc55b46bb4fb175e0e1d6896fd2090c662c40","body":{"detail":"Every grant session takes its clip as a reference (clax-clip:<artifact>/<thread>, crates/clax-core/src/clips.rs reference), since remote mode's shim fetches and caches it (crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs fetch_clips). A bearer grant's session (an agent token over /mcp or /mcp/json) is a grant session too, but its tools are ClaxTools::for_remote_agent on the hosted Clax itself, whose client is not remote, so nothing rewrites the reference: the agent reads 'Clip: clax-clip:...' and a clip_path it cannot open. Options: hand such agents the thread's clip_url at the public origin (it needs the token as a bearer, which the agent's MCP client holds but its file tools do not), return the clip as MCP image content in comments_read and the feedback handover, or say only that the thread has a clip. Read from the code; not exercised in a test.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1301},"end":{"line":1314},"content_hash":"11792d1a2aa2eac0be441ac8818dcac09eb510254d372c12d658ecc7841997b7"},"summary":"An agent token's agent on a hosted Clax is handed a clip reference it has no client to resolve","tags":["hosted","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/github.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T18:23:57.773860Z","id":"353f96196debdfc8f4d5ef13001abd97b1ed3dac749388ebad359389045b7b07","body":{"detail":"member_rights() (given to GitHub sign-ups, and by crates/clax-server/src/routes/grants.rs to every hosted invitee and request, \"their own space\") holds no clax-ask, while the collaborator and reader presets in crates/clax-core/src/rights.rs both include it. So on a hosted daemon an agent token's agent of anyone but the owner gets 403 not_permitted \"this agent may not ask (clax-ask) here\" from `ask`, even on its own person's artifact, and a hosted member's linked local Clax cannot have its questions asked on the hosted copy. Observed: a member's agent over POST /mcp/json calling ask on an artifact shared with that member at Can edit. Asking reaches only the agent's own person, so adding clax-ask looks harmless, but questions on hosted were a non-goal in docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-11-clax-dev-hosted-design.md section 1. Decide whether hosted members' agents may ask.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":91},"end":{"line":103},"content_hash":"2fa2367eedeea4f4bc8d7f9bd838701af1dab6fab8a894dc3203b30604da2e82"},"summary":"A hosted person's agents cannot ask their own person a question","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/github.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T03:24:58.783056Z","id":"fdb68bb12cee4b9441a504f390a1b530b1c468e79a308ce46aaa0143ce83d483","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:95d2a88d","summary":"status:decided: the owner decided hosted members' agents may ask their own person. member_rights() now holds clax-ask, and migration 36 updates people whose stored rights were exactly the earlier member rights. Evidence: cargo test -p clax-server --test integration api_hosted::an_agent_tokens_ask_reaches_its_person_alone_and_returns_their_answer passes with two default members: the asker's person answers, the other gets 404 reading and answering. cargo test -p clax-core --lib migration_36 passes.","supersedes":"353f96196debdfc8f4d5ef13001abd97b1ed3dac749388ebad359389045b7b07","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T19:07:12.535981Z","id":"8bde684486985671192d98ac8464b6688d0d9da62635f182a015aa4a484bc546","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:719c7835","summary":"Owner's decision (2026-10-16): 'a on demand': the clip reaches an agent token's agent as the image itself, in an MCP tool result, only when it reads that one thread; listings carry a stable link and a note. Built in 719c7835: thread views name the clip at its keyed address /_clip/<aid>/<tid>?k=<key> (clip: {url, note}), comments_read with thread_id attaches the image within 1 MiB and 4096 px a side, and the feedback poll of an agent token's session renders 'Clip: <url> (<note>)' in place of the clax-clip: reference, which signed remote shims still fetch. cargo test -p clax-server --test integration clip: 10 passed (api_hosted::an_agent_tokens_agent_reads_a_clip_by_link_in_listings_and_as_an_image_in_its_thread, an_oversized_clip_is_noted_and_not_attached, a_clip_withheld_from_an_agent_or_on_an_artifact_it_may_not_read_reaches_it_not, a_local_daemons_agent_reads_its_clip_by_path_as_before among them).","supersedes":"fa65f5c2c639e1c28844c8c937ddc55b46bb4fb175e0e1d6896fd2090c662c40","tags":["reason:fixed","status:decided","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:21.760777Z","id":"5df9c89339dbe142495d9233397a03ae885eae865fe04f1e6a3033baa819eb87","body":{"detail":"Spec §9.3: 'Declining keeps the rows held; a later ask there makes a new request only after 10 minutes'. request_in applies the same quiet period to routing, so a sender pressing Send again right after the approver declined does not re-announce the request; the rows are held and the agent's placeholder reads as not asked. If the owner wants a deliberate re-send to ask at once, drop the check for Cause::Routing.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1128},"end":{"line":1137},"content_hash":"cf9707d61e55687d29484ea3ec1da7a8faa513bbca583c591bf81438ce7a4e23"},"summary":"A routed send within ten minutes of a decline makes no request, though spec §9.3 names only ask","supersedes":"ca20c8cae63653348299c4cc6ecc3676428e073c4d2e5ec806a6ea0758a851b6","tags":["people","spec:9.3","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:21.772692Z","id":"ffffcf0f921fe5b0e2555173277a13bd4f67b7c73eeb7e6f979770160087726c","body":{"detail":"withheld_in_thread counts the authors withheld from each comment body (the rows a take holds, spec M16). A thread whose comments the agent may see but whose anchor, clip or artifact title is another person's (spec §3.3 step 6) is delivered with those fields placeholdered and makes no request; the agent can ask for the artifact's content outside threads with ask {approval: {url_or_id}} (Store::ask_approval, withheld_outside_threads), which covers text fields, the current version, documents and assets, but not a thread's anchor.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1302},"end":{"line":1322},"content_hash":"2db7bc0ea49daabf8d49defd3d54488b8041d0c22a95068bc6531cfc23d68cee"},"summary":"Routing asks only for the authors of comment bodies; a withheld anchor, clip, batch note or title makes no request","supersedes":"b6fbbf0e2ff0440519bcf54b1b7c115ae2851700d8e17cc409849af834becd24","tags":["people","spec:9.2","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:21.784482Z","id":"232ba48326e18bef014574ed4faddb279ee6fab0fc2aa9b56a57c400ea3dd167","body":{"detail":"The overflow marker (install row approval_overflow:<approver>) lists the [author, artifact, thread] places whose routed content request_in held without a request, past MAX_OPEN_REQUESTS (100) per approver or MAX_OPEN_PER_AUTHOR (20) per author. Only Store::decide_request rechecks them, dropping a place once its content is no longer held without a request (held_without_request: answered by an open or declined request, delivered, gone, or now visible). A withdrawal or an approval made outside a decision changes nothing until the next decision, so the banner can outlive what it counted.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1914},"end":{"line":1924},"content_hash":"e605efbaa1b77ac65394cb92bbe3b8380e6925c8a3c4e43692703b6852ef04e5"},"summary":"People's overflow banner stays up after withdrawals bring an approver under the limit, until their next decision","supersedes":"7f5b5747e53e1b339c625904a62dfb478d44e6af2fefc90e855fc94f69838cc6","tags":["people","spec:9.2","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:21.796328Z","id":"f6358543642e3a2d386b72ba1074dc0e4623fefb9876305d8e52b93f7d967b3d","body":{"detail":"A push to Cloudflare Artifacts whose pushed event is lost, late or never delivered (no subscription, locally: the queue is simulated and receives none, crates/clax-worker/wrangler.jsonc queues) stays unrecorded until the next publish of the artifact, so viewers see the older version meanwhile. The prototype also reconciles lazily on reads, at most every RECONCILE_EVERY_MS (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts reconcileLazily). Fix: reconcile from the artifact read routes when main has moved past the current version's commit, rate-limited per artifact.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1154},"end":{"line":1174},"content_hash":"5aea8e38f17328396770571e0e3d99efadde21ae073543404d5fa024591c706c"},"summary":"Pushed commits are recorded on a push, an Artifacts event or a publish, but not when an artifact is read","supersedes":"48e1e5e1883fa49109508fc5eebed9f11caa313dcc215d69f754f214b213a892","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:21.808575Z","id":"8c8d734d18513991babc6b7efbe7ec4e91975c13b16ef466999dadcbeec6fc6d","body":{"detail":"record_version_locked calls revoke_blind_tokens with the publisher for VersionStep::Write when expected > 0, which is ContentStore::repo_tokens (DoLedger: POST token/live to RepoDO) even when no token is held. That is one subrequest on every publish's path (time to usable), plus a Visibility per agent token. Skipping needs to know no agent token is live without asking RepoDO, for example a held-token count the instance keeps from mint and revoke answers.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1246},"end":{"line":1268},"content_hash":"a791ca23cf8107bccfd6950065f7527248cabd7d27c31964f2e4f1eeeeb672b6"},"summary":"Every publish of an existing artifact asks the push ledger for the repository's tokens before its commit: on the Worker one RepoDO call per publish","supersedes":"7db0f8bc4b896591df4384e1316204c757ab307eda378654d2022a905b6d039f","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:21.820931Z","id":"bd81b2ff873229cda873725593c2f7f493cd12c47ab38ed5a00d0274b1dc7f88","body":{"detail":"ArtifactLocks (content/mod.rs) serialise version writes within one process, so there the loser waits and then sees Conflict (concurrent_publishes_with_same_if_version_yield_one_winner). Across processes the loser's content write fails first; it is mapped to Conflict only when the artifact has already moved past the expected version. Nothing is corrupted (the loser removes nothing it did not write). The daemon is the only writer of versions today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1284},"end":{"line":1293},"content_hash":"4904f3490dcc2f9f92baa1aaa49032071480c9eaf3740604defd236f4657e508"},"summary":"Two processes publishing the same version at once: the loser gets the content store's AlreadyExists error, not Conflict, while the winner has not yet recorded it","supersedes":"f20aca051889442db19a7cd27f7a0a371e39dd8899016bcdf7228093a8476745","tags":["content-store","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:21.833327Z","id":"7e5112883ca067ca2e67799d47dd780f555293abdadf59e0dd10b7bb64d228be","body":{"detail":"Store::version_meta resolves p.person, else the session's person, else the owner, before the content write; version_authors (artifacts.rs:817) resolves the row's person again inside the transaction. They agree today (tests a_version_write_names_its_publisher_agent_and_note), but a change to one rule that misses the other makes git's Clax-Publisher disagree with the row.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1415},"end":{"line":1432},"content_hash":"48d111421f495d2e72c03035f37a629a7bd29de6662dec8fbd17c5f02aa85418"},"suggested_fix":"Resolve the person once before the content lock and pass it to version_authors.","summary":"The publisher the content store is told and the one the version row records are resolved by separate code","supersedes":"0007f8b821ba68e224e273c1e5f3091f8911bb4cd1fb07908b15a1e45f5a454c","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/exec.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:21.845584Z","id":"fbfa68ba04bf6b254044323071b6039ec6fecd4ed983422b6c2c0f7cc48b2d5a","body":{"detail":"Seen in Linux perf runs: a single commit held up by the disk. The writer runs WAL with SQLite's default synchronous=FULL, so every commit syncs the WAL, and the background PASSIVE checkpoint runs every CHECKPOINT_INTERVAL (2 s). Every delivery of a write waits on its commit, so one slow commit moves a whole cluster of deliveries (scripts/perf-clients.py:23-29 explains how the realtime gate copes).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":246},"end":{"line":269},"content_hash":"19a1b1cc49fe118705a9d82f6b9227495d66a06ae11378ed14f24dfb809e7ed5"},"suggested_fix":"Measure commit times on Linux with synchronous=NORMAL (durable across a crash of the process, not of the machine, in WAL mode) and with a different checkpoint cadence before choosing.","summary":"On Linux, store commits occasionally take 25 to 120 ms","supersedes":"c1fa8f663d2f022bec819ffe35b4e35a957db78410975a92beb0a46488798e4f","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/exec.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:21.857777Z","id":"7600eccb0f63062b3c4a030e40cc9d897ec0be95857caa8c9d4b4122cf7be585","body":{"detail":"On the pool a started job runs to completion on its worker (call_on_worker), but inline the request future owns the job: a client gone or a timeout layer dropping the handler between ContentStore::write_version and the version transaction (store/artifacts.rs:1145) skips both the record and the remove_version that a failed transaction runs. FsContent and a create-only git backend then refuse version n as already present (artifacts.rs a_stray_version_directory_refuses_the_publish_and_records_nothing), so the artifact cannot be published again until the stray is removed (clax doctor natively; nothing on a Durable Object). A dropped clipped thread creation leaves an unreferenced clip; a dropped create_artifact a zero-version row. Removing an unrecorded n before writing it is safe only where one process writes the content (a Durable Object), not natively with several daemons (record 4f959f4e).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":916},"end":{"line":946},"content_hash":"68f7616e26a49e70da13008ab0b933c12adca6dea763e30fb402f4ea0f4602dd"},"suggested_fix":"On one connection, make an unrecorded version n replaceable: when write_version reports n present and the row still says n - 1, remove_version(n) under the content lock and write again; or run the job to completion detached from the request (ctx.waitUntil on a Worker).","summary":"A call_async job awaited inline (one connection, wasm32) stops wherever its future is dropped, so a cancelled publish can leave version n written but unrecorded, which refuses every later publish of n","supersedes":"53321d53c63416d674f21c59c46cdadadeb8105aca2fbd3ecaca55cbb8f6b402","tags":["content-store","wasm","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:21.870023Z","id":"9e8e75ed8ec8cc55633ffb9da20cbe4f48ec15fe669f275af2fe68b89fc84b06","body":{"detail":"feedback.rs:1266 and clax-server/src/feedback.rs snapshot_path name versions/<n>/index.html under the home; thread clips (Home::clip_path, site.rs refile) stay files; backfill.rs hashes version files and assets on disk; stray_version_dirs (artifacts.rs:498), stray_asset_temp_files (assets.rs:350), AssetRow::path and clax doctor's version_files check read the FsContent layout. All are correct only for a store whose content is the home's files (the default).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1347},"end":{"line":1350},"content_hash":"62b8545b696db1906dc4334096cfb785b6a74d6d33e1d63932130cda23a2a0d9"},"summary":"Several paths still use the home's files directly, outside ContentStore: snapshot paths handed to agents, clip images, the audit backfill, and doctor's stray scans","supersedes":"0f6047ff4f10f7b1559a10e80ce283e75a0b77379e45b1cdffaef34bd26d1260","tags":["content-store","wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:21.882266Z","id":"58db64c518380cb23459282791a63f32bdb09daca5b95c68ec976b6a6743480b","body":{"detail":"Every take runs Sight::row on each of its session's held rows again (thread_in, the comment's authors through the view), about 13 us a row measured at 09672011, before 7c10f0c1 indexed the request reads a held row's placeholder makes. A held row's hold changes only with the visibility generation (approvals, rights, people, claims) or when its row leaves the pending query (resolve, delete, delivery), so an in-memory map per session of (generation, held feedback IDs) would let a take skip each told held row while the generation is unchanged; the generation lives in memory, so the map must too. Not taken: with 7c10f0c1 and 7fd02f8a the perf gate's vis_feedback_poll_ms read 1.46, 1.54 and 1.51 ms per round in its quietest run (limit 1.78 ms), and with b24b98e0 as well 1.53 ms in its quietest round (load about 10 on 12 cores); scripts/perf-daemon.py withdraws the held rows after each poll, so a pile of held rows is not what it times.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1286},"end":{"line":1298},"content_hash":"014f358e63a6a09fa987dc7c09362de304393d1a90fd4797054e615bc5e0dac1"},"summary":"Skip a take's told held rows while the visibility generation they were last found held at holds","supersedes":"ed625c0dd4e5cfd812aeeff04defbb5204fb29fd9b8a49e7df2ce5bfd04cf31a","tags":["revisit:vis_feedback_poll_ms over its limit again, or an agent's poll slowed by held rows its person leaves undecided","perf","visibility","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:21.894576Z","id":"d3cc1f6f6b087587646825b824c070450e6071812525e483164d7f269aec2cbf","body":{"detail":"Delivery::changed_for tells a person of a change only when their rows' newest time (StateRow::stamp: created, delivered, acknowledged, told, untargeted, last sent, session end) is the thread's newest. A change that sets no time (a watch armed or disarmed, which changes a sent row's waiting tier; a codex queue failure; a handoff that keeps a row's times) is published to the owner but to no person, so a connected person's open card keeps the old tier until the thread is fetched again. The owner hears every change.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2136},"end":{"line":2143},"content_hash":"a0352ae277d3e1bd4888457d701a8ee4f88820b6751df49739bcfa70ab5c97a5"},"summary":"A change that stamps no row reaches only the owner live; a person sees it at their next fetch","supersedes":"4efdda9acca40ae1f1a8fd869b728897e018f04e73e7207bcf56e5240a9cebd2","tags":["people","spec:10","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:21.906895Z","id":"b3d6f93efa15e68034ef3a272af6a4ea2207028dec5e577a83b3d6a2d3ba651a","body":{"detail":"state_of reports withheld (the target session's person as approver) from placeholder_at, which a take sets when it holds and tells a row, or while an open approval request of that person covers the row's comment author there (a send naming the agent, spec §10). A comment that joins no request (a send naming no agent, a later reply whose author has no open request there, an author held past the request limits) reads sent, waiting on its tier, until the agent's next take. Computing it from visibility at state time would build a Visibility per target session's person inside feedback_states_in, which listings call for every thread (spec §8.7 cost).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2180},"end":{"line":2189},"content_hash":"c65b0f968699e8cc0c38af1592e8e7b90d060df9c18a71599f611feba41154f4"},"summary":"A held row that no open request covers reads sent until a take holds it","supersedes":"ddeebf95200fc5fa9f333fc90c0217f46a2d00120c7a8ae126f14941aaa93d3f","tags":["people","spec:8.4","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/github.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:21.919124Z","id":"d40983d3f9b6613b44201e1ff271e2cad220ae7a97a0379946380b99a868825e","body":{"detail":"check_quota counts the person's live artifacts (MemberCaps::max_artifacts, MEMBER_MAX_ARTIFACTS / [hosted] member_max_artifacts, default 200) and is called from create_artifact_async (crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs) and fork_artifact_async (crates/clax-core/src/store/forks.rs). Nothing bounds the bytes a member writes: new versions of their own artifacts, asset uploads and pushed commits are uncounted, so one member can fill the content store within MAX_ASSET_BYTES per upload and the version size limits. A byte cap needs a running per-account counter charged in the version and asset transactions (record_version_locked, upload_asset).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":313},"end":{"line":348},"content_hash":"15906e486096e7696147bd11eeffb664687bc6851388db8b5581955b31076521"},"summary":"A GitHub member's account is capped by artifact count alone: no cap on stored bytes","supersedes":"51658b1bf2325e11dd58547c8b1d019274512c8d10cc1b933fb269642a2584f4","tags":["deferred","hosted","github","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/github.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:21.931444Z","id":"77469ed51b775faf5aca34ae5dedb848b032c0b68ac526a619b47086386d75eb","body":{"detail":"block_in sets github_identities.blocked_at when the owner revokes the person (Store::revoke_person in crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs), and github_sign_in refuses an account whose row is blocked or whose person is revoked. Nothing clears blocked_at, and People offers no unblock: the owner would have to edit the database to let the account back in.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":356},"end":{"line":362},"content_hash":"486b8783435225a3efdbef07b2d4303c54f3f0933cfac0fe9f56f203b15132be"},"summary":"A blocked GitHub account cannot be unblocked","supersedes":"a57972fc2ba1f449adb70c3b8baba948adce2ac55fba61daa49e085296909fbd","tags":["hosted","github","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:21.943691Z","id":"245fe67c0c5ce77476183f204c94ed537bf809add88b76b3d09364c29b0500c2","body":{"detail":"The prototype names a guest 'Name (guest)' wherever Clax shows a name to an agent or an approver. Here a guest is a plain viewer row with viewers.guest = 1; feedback, comments_read and approval views show the bare name. Names cannot collide with members' or other guests' (check_guest_name), which limits impersonation.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":297},"end":{"line":333},"content_hash":"fa6b1bcabd7d4ab1064bfd5c639d34232f3e0b5b95de9eb1b91c01616fba37b0"},"suggested_fix":"Mark guest authors in the agent-facing views and approval cards.","summary":"Guests are not labelled as guests to agents or approvers","supersedes":"cf39d49f25cf3e1c15bc3803244ec8fac55e2d146a133212842eeafc6c435bfa","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:21.956014Z","id":"3ac434ed3f059948aece6973692ec4739a235cdfdd1e69793df60ef7b6b6a42e","body":{"detail":"An agent token is a bearer grant (grants.bearer = 1, its cxa_ token in grant_tokens, kept out of credential_index so it never passes the signed Clax-Grant path). The endpoint resolves Authorization: Bearer cxa_... with bearer_grant, then Store::grant_caller for its person and rights, and builds Caller::PersonAgent; no route accepts the token yet.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":858},"end":{"line":862},"content_hash":"6118ad026448bf7342835eef06f09082a183699f7c1c18391bc4c90fa653e306"},"summary":"Store::bearer_grant is how the remote MCP endpoint should authenticate an agent token","supersedes":"31efff25ca3c25b43875ceffaddbbad5b0b7fba39820bb242a7bdc34f7993c6b","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:21.968351Z","id":"059505cb2183ff76186b05984f319e64e68a328073db27f076badf8f2c7217b8","body":{"detail":"connection_decided reads a connection item only when the owner approves or denies the request (crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs approve_grant, deny_grant). A pending request that expires after 10 minutes (request_grant's stale sweep, expire_grants) leaves its item unread in the owner's inbox; once the unapproved row is purged a day later the item renders gone with connection null. Reading it at the lapse, or touching it so the shell shows the expired status, would need the lapse paths to call into the inbox.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1405},"end":{"line":1410},"content_hash":"37faa7c25489c7bb21c58449a00b215ba4670c56c30156fd84acd0324fb5acb1"},"summary":"A connection request that lapses unanswered keeps its connection item unread","supersedes":"0118687f2dc557d8b4b673cfea9e3a7e7911afa2f991c90dad88cf4e6622b3cb","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:21.980666Z","id":"cfb08a0569a73d6b4de593f603eb93947f898ea7e71f73ecdfd9ad8f5844b526","body":{"detail":"note_finished makes the finished item for the session's person. A first publish by a person's agent reaches both the person and the owner (note_version), since a new artifact appears in the owner's gallery; finished work was left to the person, per spec §18 ('Inbox, questions: own').","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1637},"end":{"line":1641},"content_hash":"a0fa4a8c2b1a39edfb532ddd9c70fe377bd2d0458f5500bbff31400339dff010"},"summary":"A connected person's agent's finished work reaches its person only, not the owner","supersedes":"6014047ed460f730c0d943908ca30e650fbc8a9a67e42512bb4345d3c23bbe94","tags":["revisit:the owner asks to follow other people's agents' work in their inbox","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:21.993311Z","id":"064e84c8da1aef5339466ea34180d996e283581fdf2ab1042d1436b3ba28ffcf","body":{"detail":"remote_versions is written by pushes from migration 33 on. For an artifact pushed before, only the link's pushed_n/remote_n pair is known, so a public thread on an older public version is placed on the newest pushed local version and shown as 'on <remote> v<n>' though a twin exists.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":378},"end":{"line":382},"content_hash":"9a418a8e6498501aaef54bc63beafb59ae3045a16669f5a7f718a92c47fb405b"},"suggested_fix":"Backfill remote_versions on the next push by pairing the public copy's versions with the local ones in order when the link was never moved (no fork, no new).","summary":"Versions pushed before linked threads have no recorded twin but the link's last push","supersedes":"5b138f7eb7d9f95675c8f4c6c90737c5e19af06f68f3f4e3ad32340476bbca73","tags":["review","status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.006219Z","id":"27a175c424f9bdf8e8ec694e7f407618fad6d82993af512ec3134b0803647c44","body":{"detail":"Sync::mirror looks a remote thread up by (remote, remote thread ID) alone, so a remote that lists, under one public artifact, a thread ID belonging to another artifact linked to it writes into that other artifact's local thread. Only artifacts linked to that remote are reachable, and the remote can write to them anyway, so this is consistency rather than access.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":497},"end":{"line":508},"content_hash":"5d646f16c65cb93420f8638cd10f761cdf837fa7a9cf4122734478ccc796ece1"},"suggested_fix":"Also match remote_artifact_id (or artifact_id) of the link being read.","summary":"linked_thread_by_remote is not scoped to the link's artifact","supersedes":"9fb253f94d798bb05ebace71d75013f8034a0e44ec2eb1e82e356eb84cd2e0ab","tags":["review","linked-threads","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.019384Z","id":"51707e9f39b91b1d79d31c6e6159464c12c0da7b484b638d6776a6418492c6a9","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-15-linked-threads-design (Authors) says a mirrored comment is stored with author kind remote. comments.author_kind carries CHECK (author_kind IN ('viewer','agent')) from migration 3, and feedback rows reference comments, so adding a kind needs a table rebuild under foreign keys. The comment is written as a viewer comment with no local public ID (or an agent comment of no session) and its remote kind, public ID and name are kept in linked_comments; views add linked.origin remote and agents read the author as '<name> (on <remote>)'. The author is never a local person either way.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":632},"end":{"line":665},"content_hash":"1d315f12504beb532832435e36692c31c1b338debf63539814fd73b5727f1649"},"summary":"Mirrored comments keep a local author_kind viewer or agent, with the remote author in linked_comments, instead of author_kind remote","supersedes":"04eaeec1d22e332b025da1b09785964fb796a81674961e19fb7f01ab58553977","tags":["design","revisit:the comments table is next rebuilt","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.032275Z","id":"0d4172d09adf1346edc3e235c031038bb7a540ff8d89f221bf16ca8ef839d61a","body":{"detail":"threads records no reopener, so scan_linked queues every reopen of a linked thread, while resolves go up only when the owner or an owner's agent resolved (resolved_by, resolved_by_person). Another local person who can see a linked thread and reopens it is reported there as the owner's person.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":838},"end":{"line":850},"content_hash":"68b1d810d48a25f82d340e55584a56333546f845fa14c5ade1f6e019b04812b5"},"suggested_fix":"Record who reopened a thread (reopened_by) and queue a reopen only when it is the owner's or an owner's agent's.","summary":"A reopen goes up as the token's person whoever reopened it here","supersedes":"996fae6b913df2e7f6f682e1d39a61df95c7a8109f193b88dec89bad33c52908","tags":["review","security","status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.045063Z","id":"eaa57b0ce444bba8539b353190a5997e7de921ba85646a4342ff5aad246506d3","body":{"detail":"Failure: a home at migration 25 where a person's agent asked a question (a dev home run on this branch) keeps that question's item with recipient NULL after 26, so it sits in the owner's inbox and crates/clax-server/src/inbox.rs render reads its question unscoped (st.question), showing the person's question and answers to the owner, while the person never gets the item. Main's homes hold no person sessions, so they are unaffected. Accepted: migrations 24-26 are unmerged (spec M27), so only a dev home run on this branch can hold such items; questions themselves get their person from their session (questions.person is filled in by the migration).","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":739},"end":{"line":742},"content_hash":"4611fbab17797ab78415d9f71e991c5b174e8ca88f75ff87d6685c7d8474fc79"},"summary":"Migration 26 leaves every existing inbox item the owner's, including question and finished items a connected person's agent made at schema 24-25","supersedes":"5367fcc4689814242a680d9584e3d3bf9fc8dbd0f19447b827af1efaa70fb5d1","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.057956Z","id":"fa9ef7ec6a212075b784f288465206f9f8ba4fe4518a689e9792b17d012492d1","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":774},"end":{"line":776},"content_hash":"7b8c2cfc4b3987a8e331333cde1cdfbfbebd527f736765bcd9ae5f2176add692"},"summary":"Migration 27 (hosted sign-in) takes the next number after multi-person's 26; it renumbers if another branch lands first","supersedes":"89caff5089f0864057eb1a101a833112aac5c33d084cc313153b2578a65ece6a","tags":["hosted","merge","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.070633Z","id":"44826f125356d3e14e2b3224adcacfd4256c928d7f02134fb6c1ea7348264d0f","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":808},"end":{"line":930},"content_hash":"81d28a5a5d7d5d7c0afb566585eaf6cacea20053681ea5ebaef6e2b181507201"},"summary":"Migration 30 (publishing to a public Clax) follows akesling/clax-artifacts' 29 (sessions.client_name); it renumbers if another branch lands a 30 first. It also rebuilds inbox_items to add the `push` kind, as migration 26 left the table.","supersedes":"73a4817f62ff8f182f1e479807ffe5b3c0a2e4b15e76e8ac112f25f784c0a63a","tags":["migrations","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.083023Z","id":"924ede604cd1b21387e7f35a07e40463c97d30e734f704b9349c1b8f23826da7","body":{"detail":"Small rows, but they outlive the artifact and the grant. Dropping keys of revoked grants or older than some months would bound it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":888},"end":{"line":895},"content_hash":"3809d3eb40206bf1050d7706a17caa1d82c06599c44bd8c816fb14753e919899"},"summary":"publish_keys is never pruned: one row per version an agent token published with a key","supersedes":"301ee474309f153f63d3fded73bf060881730caadf7f644779fef8c43da3bc34","tags":["deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.095311Z","id":"388db751f418cfadff4e779d82b93299d47f7c05830ecb61b7b05d24ab9426a2","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":931},"end":{"line":948},"content_hash":"35ab1c3601e03d88addb1eff7ff7a3d1cbe46a10641e5c15a33cf6c41d818878"},"summary":"Migration 31 (GitHub identities) follows akesling/clax-artifacts' 30 (publishing to a public Clax); it renumbers if another branch lands a 31 first","supersedes":"f6b70331a5488de143e69751e04d123dbe8cabfa5bccedef065108a602f10b06","tags":["migrations","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.107354Z","id":"bb077166d10bc3811e6e95115fbcf180c3601d9653f97b251ed1bd6bcae4a6a3","body":{"detail":"thread_id is the PRIMARY KEY; scan_linked queues a fresh local thread only when no linked_threads row names it (crates/clax-core/src/store/linked.rs scan_linked), so the first remote scanned takes it and the other never gets it, nor its replies. Threads mirrored from either remote are separate local threads.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1001},"end":{"line":1014},"content_hash":"422e16fad9ac387965892c1a684d9f7f45d108c71b2cd3fbe0fa9890e34ef65e"},"summary":"linked_threads is keyed by the local thread alone, so an artifact linked to two remotes sends its local threads to only one of them","supersedes":"8194fd2ad48a9483b2ee82fdf3775c9785cb3ed8dcb90ba9f0eb82fe584f6b43","tags":["review","linked-threads","revisit:an artifact is pushed to a second remote","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.119198Z","id":"7dd6216809f573127439c941b3d322c44109cb8e1be2e390bdfade054aa33d3b","body":{"detail":"A hosted daemon keeps every key a linked local daemon's up-sends named (crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs comment_key), as publish_keys keeps every publish's. Rows are small, but nothing removes them, not even when the thread or grant is deleted.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1052},"end":{"line":1059},"content_hash":"4ba09b7472a4ca6e5001974915649601eee612783ece3677d8a9dc4398698508"},"suggested_fix":"Delete a grant's keys with the grant and a thread's with the thread, or prune keys older than the outbox could resend (a day).","summary":"comment_keys is never pruned: one row per thread or comment an agent token wrote with an Idempotency-Key","supersedes":"73044f1d375391dc59e5a787126cb70d57cc417b74442142c0c15790099e2c82","tags":["review","status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.131113Z","id":"e614fbdc769ca508f6ed36a404697e22dbdbe83e501e063ca548856556c9a152","body":{"kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1095},"end":{"line":1101},"content_hash":"40e0ef842deae344eeb6cb9ab562cb44f1e01fd90bba9720a79e05d2a441f941"},"summary":"question_keys is never pruned: one row per question an agent token asked with an Idempotency-Key","supersedes":"9359e05259d026fe9bf2746633dce84ad47780888565af9b66a61fe29b49bf22","tags":["linked-threads","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.142955Z","id":"102e3b6ab506e2afed4c6ba1a5d647ebabf086a44181e793e234857f2b4f999b","body":{"detail":"Measured on this machine (load average about 45): the clax-core lib tests take 12.4 s with --skip the_store_tests_pass_on_one_connection and 20.8 s with it, since the child runs 455 tests after the parent's. The threshold `passed > 300` passes with 455; a module dropped from the filter (or from test_util::store) loses its coverage on one connection without failing it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":757},"end":{"line":783},"content_hash":"b3bfd31319c95da4542d5ac7bd7f9fa165b3082f4e9534f5f055a9a24bdcbbee"},"suggested_fix":"Compare `passed` against the count the same filter lists (`--list`) less the ignored ones, or pin the module set.","summary":"The one-connection rerun adds about 8 s to the clax-core unit suite, and its >300 threshold only catches an empty filter","supersedes":"662c3db594b21a7060f0afddc51aaf69ec84a89ba9bf35f8844f6667cdf936f3","tags":["wasm","gate-speed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.154868Z","id":"04ea488108b300d4a6aca940d7abbd32b1de4aff58e79b6e0de3504afab9dc7c","body":{"detail":"For flow invite the grant's events carry grant_id and person but not invite_id, so the journal cannot join invite.create to the grant made from it except by person and time; invites.grant_id holds the link only while the row lives.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1129},"end":{"line":1143},"content_hash":"a055d17fb6d13921d9565129c8f0b702f534ab8d657151596b97465c24004831"},"suggested_fix":"Add invite_id to grant.request (flow invite) and to audit spec section 6.13 and multi-person spec section 20.2.","summary":"An invite-flow grant.request and grant.approve do not name the invite they redeemed","supersedes":"b5059e16624c0d267922097dc173ae96980c5a0a1adaa9e508d7accc51259757","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.166796Z","id":"b5061b84e7285328c9031a1c7e88c8a8eb46088d550ddab7e4b56ecec4ff722d","body":{"detail":"approve_owner_on_connect is the single approval made without a browser (spec section 21 item 3, M15). It is bounded to the connect: once per grant, within OWNER_ANSWER_SECS (10 minutes) of the tokens' issue, never once the person has made or revoked any approval of the owner (409 owner_answered, so a revocation in People stands; 409 answer_closed after the window), replays refused by accept_t first. Only the continuation token says it, never the access token agents sign with (crates/clax-server/tests/api_grants.rs a_connected_machine_approves_the_owner_through_its_continuation), and clax connect refuses on an agent channel (crates/clax-cli/tests/connect.rs connect_refuses_on_an_agent_channel). What remains: a process of the person's that reads remote.json within those ten minutes, before clax connect answers, could answer yes for them; the person can revoke it in People, and that revocation is final. Tests: store::people::tests::connecting_records_the_persons_approval_of_the_owner_once, the_answer_about_the_owner_never_overrides_the_person.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1518},"end":{"line":1610},"content_hash":"d5ef04715b7251bf982fd51818c94f17a2b0b3b2dd3450f46854211db24ca24d"},"summary":"The person's approval of the owner is recorded without a browser once, at connect: an agent present then could answer for the person","supersedes":"fbaca2aabd674f7dca2ec3c27dcb211fc7db64bbd0f2ef76e12275c3f3c67474","tags":["security","spec:6.3","spec:21","M15","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.178589Z","id":"809ea47e5edcb330e91a49fd30071ba89f0ff578cd38c7877f2ec99416ad8884","body":{"detail":"It is an outbound credential the daemon presents to the public Clax on every push, so it cannot be hashed like the inbound tokens the store verifies. It never appears in a view (Remote has no token field; tests/api_remotes.rs checks no listing carries cxa_), an event or an audit record. When a sign-in connects, the daemon makes the home 0700 and the database's files 0600 (crates/clax-server/src/routes/remotes.rs owner_only; checked in api_remotes's connect). A home copied elsewhere carries it: clax remote remove revokes it there, or the public People page does. Moving it to the OS keychain would protect a copied home but needs code the Durable Object build must not compile.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":323},"end":{"line":335},"content_hash":"fd9f0bd8892117130346d36e0afcd15890f15c5a754e582aba89c15a40ae038f"},"summary":"A remote's agent token is kept as it is in the home's database (remotes.token), not hashed","supersedes":"ac2c115c8d3fa17746e2167224ec1d8464182a95cc245c4706eb3a633772d326","tags":["security","revisit:a home is synced or backed up off the machine","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.190557Z","id":"2c203ab379c5e32003767d1a4be205bb125ee9cc63c612e2368f29cc3f947a84","body":{"detail":"Registration derives a name from the repository and branch (spec section 11) without an event; session.start's body is harness, harness_session_id, cwd, transcript_path and pid. The first agent.name then reports previous: <derived name> with no earlier event naming it, and an @name in a comment cannot be tied to its session from the journal alone.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":214},"end":{"line":220},"content_hash":"2531645c1bbef5581474f3318cd70a2a599ab739af3be8223fbe8da994159a5b"},"suggested_fix":"Add name (classed as a name for redaction) to session.start and session.join bodies, and say so in audit spec section 6.8.","summary":"A session's derived name is never recorded, so agent.name's previous names a value the journal never held","supersedes":"d9e10887cdadd2188c1a0e14e22fa5637be5844ee1aa068fb99877df4e0aadef","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.202824Z","id":"2f7ad0c31d5ad2bbe41600de63962e39f43dc20b233c2313ca38b32a75eed0bc","body":{"detail":"routes/sessions.rs register calls end_bearer_sessions_beyond(gid, BEARER_SESSION_CAP - 1) and then register_session_restoring in separate transactions; concurrent initializes of one token can each count the same live set. The next registration trims it back. Accepted as a bound on build-up, not an exact limit.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1319},"end":{"line":1348},"content_hash":"8ef33f44d4f1cafe046fb180228494b8e47afb2f14aca6b7df5ba45bf9f7a4bc"},"summary":"Two agent-token registrations at once can each leave room for themselves, so a token briefly holds more than BEARER_SESSION_CAP live sessions","supersedes":"bdba21c35e648a55e17ed451f6538152b7656a55a8117129b54a4992b5f5c9af","tags":["hosted","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.215129Z","id":"8d99d26fa8b625f0d5c3e6d761d415e91e5729ed606abf9203b4012bcb4d01b3","body":{"detail":"release_owned_in (crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs) selects threads WHERE target_session_id = ?1, and Store::roster groups threads by target_session_id; crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs indexes neither. Both are full scans of threads: off the request hot paths (ends, the reaper, GET /api/agents) and cheap at today's sizes, but linear in all threads ever made.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1730},"end":{"line":1746},"content_hash":"ed1cb058eed0b38a9d4e07ae6c733539b4ca4c1c6388d6f7a4614ccf4b5c1af2"},"suggested_fix":"Add CREATE INDEX threads_by_target ON threads(target_session_id) WHERE target_session_id IS NOT NULL in the next migration.","summary":"Every session end and every roster read scans threads for target_session_id, which has no index","supersedes":"6166fd3e2db5709106a3bc65071f99db02c217dfb40a59adc6ca0256ae12af21","tags":["perf","revisit:the next migration on this branch","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/shares.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.227439Z","id":"87ab348fb448e0d54693db458f622fb8252da856b3e1524bc3787901d5b361c9","body":{"detail":"share_artifact resolves a login through github_identities.login, which is refreshed only at each sign-in (crates/clax-core/src/store/github.rs link). If account A signed in as 'octo', later renamed on GitHub and never signed in here again, and someone else now holds 'octo' on GitHub, a share to '@octo' binds to A's person, not to whoever owns the login today. A login no one here has signed in with waits and binds at its first sign-in, which is safe: from then on the share follows the person, not the login (tested in shares.rs a_login_share_waits_for_its_first_sign_in_then_follows_the_person).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":331},"end":{"line":346},"content_hash":"0f48399d24676bee458098b796956398d96ef690dc90960df446288dc6c15847"},"suggested_fix":"Look the login up on GitHub's API (GET /users/<login>) when sharing, and bind by numeric ID.","summary":"A share by GitHub login binds at once to whichever account last signed in with that login here, which may be stale after a rename","supersedes":"da6660c8e4d8ce6971cbbb0ec46d124ad6b8541cf86441d5c4798c769c1bf3a6","tags":["security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/shares.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.239730Z","id":"95291e43db5fca6260dff6fbeca8e715fa47469be7eaf6b834b21662f630fb5b","body":{"detail":"share_artifact's login lookup (github_identities joined to viewers) checks only that the row is not the owner's; it does not read github_identities.blocked_at or viewers.person_revoked_at. ShareTo::Person refuses a revoked person (unknown_person), so the two paths disagree. No access follows (a blocked account cannot sign in and a revoked person's grants end), but the sharer sees the share as granted to a named person rather than refused.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":333},"end":{"line":346},"content_hash":"32639782b0a4356b493eedf2bea40b3ee1b0c257d7eecf9ed56009cab56ffc0f"},"suggested_fix":"Refuse such a login as ShareTo::Person refuses a revoked person, or show the share as blocked.","summary":"A share by login binds to an account whose GitHub identity is blocked or whose person is revoked, and the dialog lists it as an ordinary person","supersedes":"bdf27a495da332ac06aaed9e8107c95921ffc6fa65f24fdeae2f81e804a0aa85","tags":["sharing","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.252272Z","id":"f05ee8bd2b63563b462ae0a510c4c5912509d3b491c016a91416f26fac5867ff","body":{"detail":"Before 274f3832 the clip was written inside the thread transaction after the liveness, version and anchor checks. create_thread_inner now takes the content lock, checks liveness and puts the clip first; invalid_anchor, unknown_version and route checks fail later in the transaction and the clip is removed at threads.rs:926. A failed removal is only logged, leaving an unreferenced clip under clips/ (FsContent) or the clip-<thread> asset key. The content lock also makes a clipped thread wait for a publish of the same artifact in progress. Checking the version and anchor in a read before the put would keep refusals free of content I/O.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":841},"end":{"line":853},"content_hash":"da9c324b36bc56145b156ff2a9e326de501b4210777bf1a14697ddd9bfe8b870"},"summary":"A clipped thread now writes its clip before the version and anchor are checked, so every refused clipped request writes and deletes a clip","supersedes":"41096f57f311a889782d90ef468545c5d7eedf754cdd0cfe84ea00fdb57758a1","tags":["content-store","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.264647Z","id":"8d5ba8ae01133936c7f569fd0fa64b960965112aa28096760c2f9e22d756d56f","body":{"detail":"At 8446429: upsert_viewer(lan, 'Аlex') with no owner name succeeds; set_owner_name('Alex') then succeeds too, and both names stand. An agent registering from repository web is named 'web' beside a LAN viewer 'wеb'. New people are covered (check_person_name refuses a look-alike held by an uninvited viewer). The owner usually names themselves late, on a first comment, so pre-squatting is the likely order.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":122},"end":{"line":144},"content_hash":"1de938dd9fb1b372a1c0a4ff8a6d6621a8555d5847b284aed129ce694034651a"},"suggested_fix":"Mark it where names are shown: an unconnected viewer whose name looks like a protected name is flagged in the shell and in agent author lines (with spec section 9.6's '(not connected)', Task 17), rather than refusing the owner their own name.","summary":"The look-alike check runs only when the later name is set: a LAN viewer who took 'Аlex' before the owner named themselves 'Alex', or 'wеb' before an agent web went live, keeps it","supersedes":"f2d8e56e2cd87ead18a180f4cbdeeeca7b0f115248d5b8aab7918b5e38b27f27","tags":["review","spec:9.6","revisit:task-17","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:42:16.558072Z","id":"f1ef9b15eeadbde82d59feecdeb37c13878341f07c09bcaa5b952297cd9e0cd9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","summary":"Moved to crates/clax-store/src/approvals.rs:1126:1135 as b23d2792 in git:9f99ad87","supersedes":"5df9c89339dbe142495d9233397a03ae885eae865fe04f1e6a3033baa819eb87","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
