{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/github.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:49:31.122477Z","id":"9a3fbff2c594c3aca96b184934382fad1e083d1fc0f1e4dbe2d0d6f39d507b3b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:cf71672d069b759a82005c15e8f27221738eef9e","summary":"Fixed in cf71672d: member_rights (crates/clax-store/src/github.rs:93-106) grants clax-ask's ASK_ACTIONS, so a member's agents ask their own person; api_hosted::an_agent_tokens_ask_reaches_its_person_alone_and_returns_their_answer runs on members' default rights and passes (bazelisk test //crates/...: 31 of 31 targets pass)","supersedes":"a0ccecca72086ca75c0f165f6bd73262a1c43ce259879974de9c5eea7b3ea1e2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:58:53.695918Z","id":"d359fbc3080ed0ffdd9d597ead37fae59d6b4b5cefc31aaf07a7e872582029e0","body":{"detail":"The app harness takes its comments on the wait tier (line 323). Tier::Wait is in_band (crates/clax-core/src/feedback.rs:43-46), so Store::take_feedback stamps acknowledged_at when it hands a row over, and Tier::resends excludes it, and TAKE_FEEDBACK only resends rows whose delivery_tier is stop_hook, prompt_hook, queue or inject. A comment the app's worker has taken is therefore never delivered again: if the daemon or app dies while the agent is applying the change, the thread stays open with its row acknowledged and nothing resends it. docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-12-flutter-app.md:32 (Review Focus 1, test worker_survives_daemon_restart_mid_change in Task F9) expects the comment to be delivered again after a restart. Either the app worker recovers on its own (on start, list its open threads whose latest comment is acknowledged but has no agent reply, and run them), or the app takes a tier that acknowledges only on an explicit ack and is resend-eligible.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":321},"end":{"line":328},"content_hash":"0352d9547ff8002a8de0b8024335221ff28f38dc40730c0730b336967befefb5"},"summary":"An app session's feedback is acknowledged at hand-over and never resent","tags":["status:needs-decision","flutter-app","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:02:35.346003Z","id":"74211b606185d9891c563b61ae8e766f10c9f8b1deb47f17ac9027d02bbc55a3","body":{"detail":"GET /api/threads (crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs:134-180) returns every open thread with status, sent_to_agent, comments[] (author_kind, via_harness, created_at) and feedback_state (crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs:410). A thread whose latest owner comment has no agent reply is either still pending (feedback_state.state \"sent\": the next wait poll delivers it) or taken and lost (\"acknowledged\", tier \"wait\"). A recovery that re-runs every unanswered sent thread also re-runs the pending ones, which the poll then delivers again. Selecting sent_to_agent && state == \"acknowledged\" && no agent comment after the last viewer comment avoids that.","kind":"comment","references":"d359fbc3080ed0ffdd9d597ead37fae59d6b4b5cefc31aaf07a7e872582029e0","span":{"start":{"line":321},"end":{"line":328},"content_hash":"0352d9547ff8002a8de0b8024335221ff28f38dc40730c0730b336967befefb5"},"summary":"A client-side recovery has what it needs from GET /api/threads; it must select by feedback_state to avoid running a change twice","tags":["review","flutter-app","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:08:36.940381Z","id":"36b064aa8c99973e045e61850ba49d55669a8ad6b38ba5f84976da693791531d","body":{"detail":"The store keeps a full directory per version (version_file_path, crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs:91), with no content-addressed blob store, so restore_version copies each file of version n as publish copies carried files. Bytes, content types, per-file hashes and content_sha256 equal version n's (tests/api_restore.rs restore_republishes_the_old_files_as_a_new_version), but each restore adds n's full size on disk. The spec's §4 row 'Version restore' (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md:425) says 'reusing the stored blobs'; that wording does not match this storage.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":784},"end":{"line":827},"content_hash":"99b97851785d4f8cec1984f12fb3432d23c91f25b32108eafcf2cbd49c45a381"},"summary":"A restore copies version n's files into a new version directory; nothing is shared","tags":["storage","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:11:13.307784Z","id":"ce1059f409027e886ee6de4fa2c2f327c5b651489bcd3c6b8f8daf8ee4abe312","body":{"detail":"restore_version (crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs:784) reaches write_version_from with every path of version n in `prev`, so carried_paths (line 899) holds all of them and version_record (line 1011) writes them under `carried`. docs/contract.md:4052 documents `carried[paths]` for version.publish, and for every other write it means files kept unchanged from the previous version (index.html is never in it). For a restore the files come from version n and may differ from the previous version, so an audit reader diffing by `carried` sees no change where the page was rolled back. The only trace of the source is the free-text label/note (`Restored v<n>`). Either leave `carried` empty (or list only the paths whose hash equals the previous version's) and add a `restored_from: n` field, or document the restore case in docs/contract.md.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1011},"end":{"line":1011},"content_hash":"6f0a104ecd4832e0edb98fa196f9f6e94b047c6753f4018a6bc86356267a9455"},"summary":"A restore's version.publish audit record lists every file, index.html included, as carried, and names no source version","tags":["audit","review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:17:24.147654Z","id":"8fb67de154b2d90d1f33776bce8b00480dadb1fd47d60eeaa12569479caa1efc","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:6598f558","summary":"restore_version now passes Carry::Restore{from, unchanged}: version.publish carries restored_from: n and carried lists only non-index files whose sha256 equals the previous version's; publishes keep Carry::Forward. cargo nextest run -p clax-core -E 'test(/a_restore_records_its_source|a_publish_records_no_source_version/)' passes; contract row noted for docs/contract.md:4052.","supersedes":"ce1059f409027e886ee6de4fa2c2f327c5b651489bcd3c6b8f8daf8ee4abe312","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
